NesInternalRam:0000:scratch_ptr_lo:General-purpose ZP scratch pointer LO (project-wide default; 13 of 16 banks touch this). In the VM = computed-address + indirect-call target (was ptr0). Kept generic deliberately -- NOT VM-exclusive.
NesInternalRam:0001:scratch_ptr_hi:General-purpose ZP scratch pointer HI (was ptr0).
NesInternalRam:0002:vm_sp_lo:VM operand-stack pointer LO (was ptr1). Reset-inits to $FF -> $05FF stack base; VM frame alloc does vm_sp -= 9; syscall_dispatch reads params via (vm_sp),Y. CAVEAT: a few kernel syscalls (e.g. sram checksum $C5AA) transiently borrow $02/$03 as a scratch pointer.
NesInternalRam:0003:vm_sp_hi:VM operand-stack pointer HI (was ptr1); reset-init to $05.
NesInternalRam:0004:vm_fp_lo:VM frame-base pointer LO (was ptr2). Frame-local address = vm_fp + signed offset (the local/array access base; see vm_addr_ptr2_plus_word/sbyte).
NesInternalRam:0005:vm_fp_hi:VM frame-base pointer HI (was ptr2).
NesInternalRam:0006:vm_ip_lo:VM bytecode instruction-pointer LO (was ptr3). The dispatch loop does lda (vm_ip),Y / inc vm_ip to fetch opcodes + inline operands. Second-busiest indirect after scratch_ptr.
NesInternalRam:0007:vm_ip_hi:VM bytecode instruction-pointer HI (was ptr3).
NesInternalRam:001C:ppu_queue_a_lo:Pointer LO into $0020 (PPU upload queue A?); reset-init = $20
NesInternalRam:001D:ppu_queue_a_hi:Pointer HI; reset-init = $00 (forms $0020)
NesInternalRam:001E:ppu_queue_b_lo:Pointer LO into $0030 (queue B?); reset-init = $30
NesInternalRam:001F:ppu_queue_b_hi:Pointer HI; reset-init = $00 (forms $0030)
NesInternalRam:0050:brk_dispatch_id:Task ID for next BRK; IRQ handler reads this and indirect-JMPs through $C173+id*3
NesInternalRam:0066:brk_scratch_lo:Cleared on every BRK dispatch entry
NesInternalRam:0067:brk_scratch_hi:Cleared on every BRK dispatch entry
NesInternalRam:0068:brk_jmp_target_lo:IRQ-computed indirect JMP target LO; reused later as general data-pointer LO (byte-meaning-by-context)
NesInternalRam:0069:brk_jmp_target_hi:IRQ-computed indirect JMP target HI; reused as data-pointer HI
NesInternalRam:006E:p1_buttons:P1 held buttons (ABSS UDLR, MSB-first); written by controller_poll ($C628) every NMI
NesInternalRam:006F:p2_buttons:P2 held buttons (same format)
NesInternalRam:0071:ppuctrl_shadow:PPUCTRL ($2000) shadow; the codebase never reads $2000 directly. Managed by $C6A6 ($C54F/nmi_off, $C68A/nmi_on).
NesInternalRam:0072:ppumask_shadow:PPUMASK ($2001) shadow; managed by $C570 ($C567/rendering_on, $C69D/rendering_off).
NesInternalRam:0073:prg_bank_shadow:Current PRG bank in the MMC1 $8000-$BFFF window. set_prg_bank ($C577) compares A against it (skips the switch if already current), records the new bank here, then serial-writes A to $FFF0. The banked syscalls (memcpy_banked / call_bank / ppu_copy_rect / ppu_upload_block) read it to save/restore the bank around a switch. Reset-init = 0 (boot selects bank 0).
NesInternalRam:0075:mul_acc_lo:16-bit accumulator LO for mul_xy_by_3 ($C6AD): result = Y added X times (= X*Y); used to scale a dispatch ID by the table stride (e.g. the IRQ syscall id*3).
NesInternalRam:0076:mul_acc_hi:16-bit accumulator HI for mul_xy_by_3.
NesInternalRam:0074:palette_dirty:Non-zero = palette upload pending; $C6D4 uploads $0700-$071F to PPU $3F00-$3F1F then clears this
NesInternalRam:0079:music_voice_idx:Outer-loop voice index (0-4) during music driver scan
NesInternalRam:007A:music_ptr_lo:Pointer LO into current voice record at $0734+N*9 ($7A/$7B)
NesInternalRam:007B:music_ptr_hi:Pointer HI into current voice record
NesInternalRam:0080:skip_vblank_wait:Non-zero = $C537 (wait-for-VBlank) returns immediately without spinning
NesInternalRam:0081:nmi_busy:Semaphore: foreground sets to 1, spin-waits for NMI to clear it. The 'wait for VBlank' handshake.
NesInternalRam:0083:clock_a_hi:16-bit wall-clock A high byte; NMI adds +2 every frame (gated by $89); reset = $04 (init $04D2 = 1234)
NesInternalRam:0084:clock_a_lo:Wall-clock A low byte; reset = $D2
NesInternalRam:0085:clock_b_hi:16-bit wall-clock B high byte; reset = $04
NesInternalRam:0086:clock_b_lo:Wall-clock B low byte; reset = $D2
NesInternalRam:0089:skip_wallclock:Non-zero = NMI does OAM/audio/input but skips the wall-clock tick
NesInternalRam:00B0:nmi_skip_all:Non-zero = NMI bails after OAM DMA (skips controller/palette/audio/clock)
NesInternalRam:0720:audio_mute_triangle:Non-zero = triangle channel writes suppressed (for sound-effect ducking)
NesInternalRam:0721:audio_active_v0:Voice 0 active flag (always $01 during song playback)
NesInternalRam:0722:audio_active_v1:Voice 1 active flag
NesInternalRam:0723:audio_active_v2:Voice 2 active flag
NesInternalRam:0724:audio_active_v3:Voice 3 active flag
NesInternalRam:0725:v0_config:Voice 0 config (3 bytes: tempo_div, song_ptr_lo, song_ptr_hi); written by audio_load_voice ($C3AD)
NesInternalRam:0728:v1_config:Voice 1 config (3 bytes)
NesInternalRam:072B:v2_config:Voice 2 config (3 bytes)
NesInternalRam:072E:v3_config:Voice 3 config (3 bytes)
NesInternalRam:0731:v4_config:Voice 4 config (3 bytes)
NesInternalRam:0734:v0_trigger:Voice 0 byte 0: 1-4 = play on channel; 5-8 = just played (dormant); 0 = idle
NesInternalRam:073D:v1_trigger:Voice 1 byte 0 (same encoding)
NesInternalRam:0746:v2_trigger:Voice 2 byte 0
NesInternalRam:074F:v3_trigger:Voice 3 byte 0
NesInternalRam:0758:v4_trigger:Voice 4 byte 0
NesSaveRam:0003:fief_history_table:Per-fief HIGH-WATER MARK table — 17 entries x 8 bytes each (136 bytes total at $6003-$608A). Tracks historical maxes of 4 economic stats so income harvest uses peaks, not current. FULLY DECODED 2026-05-25 from sub $A0A9 in bank 0. Per-slot layout (idx*8 from base $6003): +0=output_max, +2=dams_max, +4=loyalty_max, +6=wealth_max. Each updated via 'if current >= history: history = current' pattern. STRATEGIC IMPLICATION: stats drained by war/Train/tax don't hurt income — the peak is remembered permanently. 'Build everything to max once' is mathematically optimal because the high-water mark drives gold/rice harvest.
NesSaveRam:0CF7:province_ai_state:Per-province GRANT-POLICY byte (0-5, 0xFF=excluded). 0=Home 1=Industrial 2=Military 3=Balanced 4=Farming 5=Direct. The per-fief AI driver ai_per_fief_command_driver ($B89B) switches on it (cases 0-5) to pick that fief's command handler. **[CENSUS-CONFIRMED 2026-06-03, probe-ai-policy-distribution.py] This is a PLAYER affordance, not an AI choice — the AI never picks a style.** Every normal save reads {Home:49, Direct:1}: all 49 AI fiefs sit at 0 (Home) and only the human's own fief is 5 (Direct). States 1-4 appear ONLY in saves where the PLAYER has conquered+granted (they scale with extra Direct fiefs — e.g. VICTORY {0:33,3:10,5:7}, blockade-complete {0:37,2:1,3:5,5:7}). new-game seeds ALL fiefs 0 ($89A3 $89F9); char-creation stamps the player fief 5 ($8694); conquered AI fiefs stay 0. So state 0 = the AI's universal behavior: 0->ai_econ_action_state0->ai_econ_command_dispatch, the RNG-weighted Balanced loop run on EVERY AI fief every turn (per-fief variety comes from resource surplus + RNG + daimyo stats, NOT from policy). Eligibility/ownership plumbing: count_eligible_targets ($8172) requires !=0xFF, province_state_is_FF ($D999) tests ==0xFF; set on ownership change by sub_98A3 ($6CF7[fief]=arg3); player Grant writes via driver_grant ($AF66). [[project_nobunaga_ai_command_pass]]
NesSaveRam:0D2D:fief_tax_rate:Per-fief TAX RATE byte (0-100), one per province (flat array indexed by fief, NOT in the 26-byte record). CONFIRMED 2026-06-02 (main-turn-loop/planner walk): driver_tax ($99A6) takes &$6D2D[fief], displays it as 'Tax is %d, enter new tax' ($99C2), and writes back number_input(1..100) ($9A3D); the old-new delta drives the loyalty/wealth penalty via effect_tax. Save-dump range 20-64, consistent. USED AS: (a) the income multiplier in the harvest sweep -- gold/rice = pct_op(tax, wealth) + pct_op(tax, pct_op(40, town)) (bank0 $A1E1/$A20C/$A25C), i.e. income is literally tax% of the economic base (this is the harvest memory's 'od_pct'); (b) an event-probability term square_over_2025(100-tax) (bank0 $9DCD) -- this particular roll rises at LOW tax, so it is NOT the high-tax riot; (c) the per-period gate at $A32A: if (tax < 90-skill) province[+12] *= 0.9 (a 0.9x decay of the +12 field -- +12 is loyalty per the high-water map, larger-range; the decay DIRECTION reads counterintuitive (fires at normal/low tax) so recheck the condition vs raw bytecode before doctrine). OPEN: reconcile the +12 loyalty range + the $A32A decay direction (Inbox).
NesSaveRam:0D5F:current_season:Season-of-year counter (0-3). RUNTIME: ai_strategic_turn_planner ($A47F) does season=(season+1)&3 each period; current_game_year increments only when it wraps to 0 ($A48B/$A48E) -> 4 seasons = 1 year. per_period_fief_daimyo_update_driver ($A36F) switch(season): 1=init_province_highwater_from_records, 2=harvest_income_sweep_all_fiefs (the FALL harvest), 3=normalize_relations_matrix_lower; per_turn_age + natural-death run every season. Planner event-select gates on season==1 ($A4CB). BOOT: byte 0 of the 4-byte config block at $6D5F-$6D65 (init '01 01 02 32'); neighbor $6D63=const_two (Grow's sqrt subtrahend). Renamed from config_block 2026-06-02 (main-turn-loop walk).
NesSaveRam:0D63:const_two:NOT a constant -- it is the SKILL LEVEL / difficulty knob (1-5), default 2. SET at new-game by init_new_game_state ($8AD6: const_two = number_input(1..5) after 'Please select skill level.'). It is a GLOBAL difficulty multiplier read in ~35 sites across ALL 4 banks. The headline: the 5 development commands all use it as the (6-const_two) numerator term -- Grow gain = 2*floor(amount*(6-const_two)/sqrt(output+amount)) (Build/develop-loyalty/wealth/morale identical shape). EMULATOR-CONFIRMED (probe-skill-impact.py): on one fief, amount 100 -> gain 76/60/46/30/14 for skill 1/2/3/4/5 = a 5.4x swing. So HIGHER skill = LESS development = harder (the long-standing '*5' in the Grow formula was just skill-1's 6-1=5; all earlier cracked formulas are the skill-2 default case). Beyond development it also scales: starting stat boosts (apply_scenario_starting_stat_boosts, const_two*5/*10), AI trade/decision gates ($B8CC 55-const_two*5, $B552 const_two+3), event/uprising magnitude (rng_mod_30=(const_two+1)*10, $A641), and combat casualties/damage (bank2 $9EC1 rng_mod(6-const_two), $9FEE field-=const_two, bank15). DISCOVERED 2026-06-02 (init_new_game_state walk + footprint search). Name kept (high doc blast-radius); rename to skill_level/game_difficulty captured as an Inbox ticket. Byte 4 of the config block at $6D5F (init '01 01 02 32' -> the '02' is skill 2).
NesSaveRam:0F1B:daimyo_turn_order:Per-season turn-order array (one byte per acting fief, sized to scenario_fief_count -> up to 50 bytes). Re-randomized each season by shuffle_fief_turn_order_array ($A742): scenario_fief_count random transpositions via swap_byte ($A757/$A763). Consumed by ai_per_fief_command_driver ($B918): selected_province_idx = daimyo_turn_order[ai_per_fief_loop_index] picks who acts next within the season. Seeded at new-game init ($89F3). RELOCATED from $6F0B 2026-06-02 (main-turn-loop walk) -- $6F0B has ZERO references in any bank; the real array base used by both the shuffle and the command-driver reader is $6F1B. [[project_nobunaga_turn_order_randomization]]
NesSaveRam:0F5F:selected_province_idx:Word holding the currently-selected province index (0-16 for 17-fief scenario, 0-49 for 50-fief). The 'A4 5F 6F 8B 1A B5 8C 01 70 BB' province-access idiom (chapter 9 §4) reads this, multiplies by 26 (record size), and adds $7001 (table base) to get the record pointer. Appears 81+ times across banks 0/1/2/15. Idx=50 ($7515) is the zealot/uprising slot (header=9999 marks special).
NesSaveRam:0F63:battle_defending_province:Word: the province whose tactical map is loaded for the current battle (the defender's fief). Read by map_populate ($8903, bank 2) to index province_to_mapid_table ($F70E) -> map_id -> tactical_map_cell_pool ($A57E + map_id*55, bank 4). Distinct from selected_province_idx ($6F5F). Seeding this + scenario_fief_count is sufficient to drive the ROM->SRAM map populate (render-rom-to-map.py). Session 2026-05-30.
NesSaveRam:0D67:rest_turns_remaining:Per-daimyo turn-skip counter (Rest command). PINNED 2026-05-30 by driver_rest ($ADB3, Command 17): sets $6D67[d77e()] = number_input(1..10) — 'rest for N turns' (health/age recovery, ch11). The turn loop then: sub_B79B, if $6D67[daimyo]!=0, decrements one and skips the daimyo's command-pick (resting = no action this turn); the war-target planner ($A578) skips flagging a resting daimyo as prey; several other action drivers gate on it too ($8CB2/$902B/$9B52/$9C09/$9057/$B943). I.e. a resting daimyo is inert and untouchable-as-target until the counter drains.
NesSaveRam:0D9D:scenario_fief_count:Word: the active scenario's fief count — 17 or 50. The 17-vs-50 selector the battle map-populate path branches on (sub_DC88: UCMPGT 50). With battle_defending_province ($6F63), the only SRAM input map_populate ($8903) needs. Session 2026-05-30.
NesSaveRam:0DD4:daimyo_weakness_flag:Per-daimyo 0/1 WEAKNESS/CONDITION mark (NOT a pure war-target flag — that was an over-read, see below). WRITER (AI planning pass, bank 0 $A4AB-$A5AF): cleared to 0, then $6DD4[D] |= (rng_mod(400) < (100 - daimyo_health)) for health<=99 daimyo (gates: skip if health>99 at $A56A, or rest_turns_remaining[$6D67][D]!=0 at $A578). So P(marked) = (100-health)/400 per pass — empirically SHAPE-confirmed 2026-05-30 (flagged mean health 66.6 vs 81.9). READ BY TWO SYSTEMS: (a) war-targeting — fief_owner_weakness ($D972, 'called only by War', 8 read sites incl. per-fief AI driver $B8A0) treats a marked daimyo as preferred/weak prey; (b) natural-death/health — sub_9154 ($9187) reads it in the death-roll result. RECONCILES the 2026-05-28 5-dump finding that called $6DD4 a chronic-illness/condition flag: it's a per-TURN low-health-weighted mark, but sustained-low-health daimyo (e.g. Saito) get re-marked every turn, so it LOOKS chronic across yearly dumps. **CAUTION (empirical, 2026-05-30): NOT a hard war-immunity gate** — a health>99 daimyo (never marked) was still invaded, so the mark is a PREFERENCE/vulnerability signal that biases AI targeting, not the sole war trigger. Index per-daimyo (writer loops D=0..fief_count, indexes daimyo_table_17[D] via sub_D7CD AND $6DD4[D] by same D; fief-indexed uses ride the scenario identity). Daimyo record +1 = health CONFIRMED via 50Diamyo cross-check (31/38 = start+5). Exact war role pending SRAM-dump confirmation.
NesSaveRam:0E15:fief_to_daimyo_map:17-byte array, position i = current owner-daimyo idx for fief i+1 (1-based). Found 2026-05-25 via SRAM cross-reference. Initial state: identity (fief i+1 owned by daimyo i). After conquests, values change — e.g. when Tokugawa took Owari, position 16 changed from 16 (Oda) to 7 (Tokugawa). Daimyos whose value doesn't appear anywhere have lost their home; they remain in daimyo_table_17 as 'wandering' (status=$01 in chapter 7 terms, vs $00 for fief-holding lords).
NesSaveRam:1515:zealot_uprising_slot:Province-record-format slot (26 bytes, idx=50) for the zealot/Ikko-Ikki uprising force when it spawns. Uses standard 26-byte province record layout so it slots into combat engine without special-casing. Distinguishing markers: header=9999 (special), extreme loyalty/morale (1300/1516 observed), tiny skill/arms (4/4). Cleared after combat resolution. Spawn check likely lives in bank-0 season-turnover code.
NesSaveRam:1001:province_table_live:AUTHORITATIVE live working province table (chapter 9 §4 reconciliation). 17 records x 26 bytes for the 17-fief scenario. Confirmed field layout (offsets, all 16-bit LE since loadA_ind_word reads low-byte-first): +0=gold, +2=debt, +4=town, +6=rice, +8=output, +10=dams, +12=loyalty, +14=wealth, +16=men, +18=morale, +20=skill, +22=arms, +24=header (base koku, the development ceiling). Record N is at $7001 + N*26.
NesSaveRam:152F:daimyo_table_17:17-fief scenario daimyo records — 17 records x 7 bytes. Each: +0 age, +1 Health, +2 Drive, +3 Luck, +4 Charisma, +5 IQ, +6 status/generated-flag. Index parallel to daimyo_name_table at $77A8. Tokugawa is record 7 at $7560. **+6 (status) = the ORIGINAL-vs-GENERATED flag** (0 = original scenario daimyo, 1 = generated/replacement): set to 1 by assign_unique_daimyo_face_code ($DB97) on succession, and read by draw_daimyo_portrait ($E76F) to choose preset (dedicated) vs composite portrait. 50-fief records are the parallel daimyo_defaults table at bank-3 $9532; live SRAM records load from there at new-game.
NesSaveRam:1560:daimyo_rec_tokugawa:Player slot in 17-fief scenario. Record 7 of daimyo_table_17. Format: age + H + D + L + Ch + IQ + status (7 bytes).
NesSaveRam:17A8:daimyo_name_table:17-fief daimyo names — 17 names x 9 bytes (8 ASCII chars + null pad). Indices parallel to daimyo_table_17. Order in 17-fief scenario: Hatakeyama, Uesugi, Hojo, Honganji, Asakura, Anekoji, Imagawa, Tokugawa, Iera, Tsutsui, Asai, Rokkaku, Kitabatake, Ashikaga, Miyoshi, Takeda, Oda. WHEN A DAIMYO IS DISPLACED AND REGENERATED (via zealot conquest, etc.), this entry is overwritten — sometimes cleanly (e.g. 'Iera' -> 'Saito'), sometimes with partial syllable-overwrite producing garbled names like 'Sate\0ui' (from 'Tsutsui'). The name regenerator may use a clean-name table with a syllable-stitch fallback.
NesSaveRam:1C00:map_tile_data:Strategic-map background tile indices. ~558 bytes covering the 18x31 map grid.
NesSaveRam:1F00:ui_transient_state:Transient UI cache: frame counter at $7FE9, animation timers, menu position, status flags. Boot bytecode zeroes $7FE7/$7FC7/$7FD3/$7FD1 on game start (chapter 6). NOT preserved across power cycles — only canonical tables survive a save.
NesSaveRam:1FE9:frame_counter:Per-frame counter (60Hz tick). Drives animation timing, cursor blink, music transitions. Continuously incremented when game is unpaused, frozen when paused.
NesSaveRam:0FF6:combat_arena_x_min:[ORACLE-CONFIRMED 2026-06-02] The 4 words $6FF6/$6FF8/$6FFA/$6FFC are NOT damage magnitudes -- they are the tactical-arena BOUNDING RECTANGLE [x_min,y_min,x_max,y_max]. $6FF6 = x_min. Default rect (0,0,10,4) = the 11x5 tactical grid (rand%11 x rand%5). is_coord_in_combat_rect ($970A) tests x in [x_min,x_max] & y in [y_min,y_max]; player_interactive_unit_move_loop + rng_search_combat_rect_for_unit_cell bound movement to it. set_combat_arena_rect_by_approach ($9675) pulls x_min->7 on an EAST approach (attacker enters the east strip). Overturns [[project_nobunaga_combat_damage_formula_decoded]] (the '{1,2,4,7} damage table' were these rect coords). Proof: tools/probe-combat-arena.py.
NesSaveRam:0FF8:combat_arena_y_min:[ORACLE-CONFIRMED 2026-06-02] y_min of the tactical-arena rect (see $6FF6). Default 0; set to 2 on a SOUTH approach (attacker enters the south strip, y in [2,4]). NOTE: the decompiled C's set_combat_arena_rect_by_approach shows the S branch writing 'word_3' -- a VM store-annotation bug; the oracle proves S writes $6FF8 (y_min), N writes $6FFC (y_max). For the teardown.
NesSaveRam:0FFA:combat_arena_x_max:[ORACLE-CONFIRMED 2026-06-02] x_max of the tactical-arena rect (see $6FF6). Default 10; set to 3 on a WEST approach (attacker enters the west strip, x in [0,3]).
NesSaveRam:0FFC:combat_arena_y_max:[ORACLE-CONFIRMED 2026-06-02] y_max of the tactical-arena rect (see $6FF6). Default 4; set to 2 on a NORTH approach (attacker enters the north strip, y in [0,2]). See the store-annotation-bug note on $6FF8.
NesSaveRam:1FEB:sram_save_checksum:[DATA-WALK CONFIRMED] Stored 16-bit running-sum checksum of the SRAM save body ($6001-$7FFF). write_sram_save_checksum_and_signature ($A3AA) accumulates the syscall-22 checksum and STORES it here; verify_sram_save_integrity ($821E) recomputes + compares against it on load (match -> ret 1). Sits just below the signature string at $7FED.
NesSaveRam:0F4F:deduped_owner_list:[DATA-WALK CONFIRMED] FF-terminated list of UNIQUE owning-daimyo ids. dedup_owners_to_6f4f ($8DE1) reads an FF-terminated fief list, maps each fief->owner (fief_to_daimyo_map via fief_owner), dedups, and writes the unique set here, returning the count. The 'distinct daimyo involved' working set (e.g. who's party to a multi-fief event).
NesSaveRam:0D9F:current_game_year:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM HIGH] 16-bit current game YEAR (base 1560=$0618). calc_year_scaled_random_value ($9214) scales RNG by (year-1560)/2; aging skips the first year (year!=$0618); AI spend caps = (year-1559)*N. Incremented in place by ai_strategic_turn_planner ($A48E LOADL_abs / INC / $A492 STORE_abs) on the season-counter wrap. Neighbors config_block($6D5F)/const_two($6D63).
NesSaveRam:0E0D:gold_rice_exchange_rate:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM HIGH] Current gold<->rice exchange RATE (element 1, stride 2, of the period-rate table at $6E0B). Random-walk updated (prev + rng_mod(11) - 5, clamped >=10) by roll_period_rate_table_6e0b ($924A); read by gold->rice convert ($B338, math32 muladddiv), buy/sell-rice handlers ($A068/$A003), and the 5-stat view ($8094).
NesSaveRam:0F81:war_attacker_men:[DATA-WALK AMEND HIGH] Attacker MEN count in war/siege (province record field +16 = men). driver_war ($997C): defender_men -= war_attacker_men; apply_conquest_outcome ($E0EA): men = attacker($6F81) + defender($6F87); strength compare $6F81 vs $6F87 ($8F0F). The 'How many men' prompt writes it ($9913). Part of the attacker triple $6F7D/$6F7F/$6F81 = +0 gold / +6 rice / +16 men.
NesSaveRam:0F4D:audio_wait_gate:[DATA-WALK AMEND HIGH] Boolean gate for audio_control (syscall $0A) busy-wait loops — gated spins at $80B8/$8166 (bank0), $8BB1 (bank1 helper_8B8F), $B08D (bank1 subhandler_B066), $947A (bank2 announce_battle_outcome) all wait on the audio syscall while set. Written =1 at init_new_game_state ($89A9) and verify_sram_save_integrity ($8358); save/restore slot in reassign_daimyo24_fiefs.
NesSaveRam:1BE8:cur_combat_side:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM HIGH] Combat SIDE index (0=attacker / 1=defender). get_battle_side_province ($838F) maps it to one of the two battle provinces; resolve_attack_apply_casualties ($9E73) uses it AND (side^1) for both combatants (the ^1 flip appears 17x, applied to THIS, never to $7BE4); per-unit flags index *(side + $6F65). Read across ~40 bank-2 combat subs as the side discriminator.
NesSaveRam:1BE4:cur_combat_unit_slot:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM HIGH] Current combat unit-SLOT index (0..4). The *5-stride outer index in the unit-field address arg*5+arg+$6FD0 ($8290); loop bound `slot>=5` recurs at $98FA/$9A14/$9B01/$AC77/$AD33; 1-based display (slot+1) at $93A9. Companion of cur_combat_side ($7BE8) — the ^1 side-flip is applied to $7BE8 only, cleanly separating slot vs side.
NesSaveRam:1BEA:battle_side_strength_mod:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Per-side word pair (side 0=attacker @ $7BEA, 1=defender @ $7BEC) = the weighted stat-advantage score. WRITTEN by ai_sum_battle_strength ($8E5C): each of 8 daimyo+province stats the side wins adds that stat's battle_strength_stat_weights entry here. READ by ai_score_strength_term_40pct ($8E40): base + pct(pct(base,40), this[side]).
NesSaveRam:16A9:province_unit_type_pct:[MED 2026-06-10] Per-province unit-type composition: 5 bytes per province (stride 5, base $76A9), each a percentage of the army allotted to one of the 5 unit types. Read by distribute_men_into_unit_strengths ($91D5) to split total men into per-unit strengths. Writer not yet ground.
NesSaveRam:0DA1:ai_turn_flags:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM MED] AI-turn/war/conquest BITFIELD (per-bit RMW, never a count/index). bit0: trade ($B8AD &~1 / $B8C8 |rng, read $8A48 &1). bit5: |32 ($A6CC), tested by msg-selectors ($8BA8/$DE83) + apply_conquest_outcome ($E0AC). bit7: |128 abort-gate ($D96E/$B901), tested in vm_bootstrap ($A7A5) + ai_strategic_turn_planner ($A4BE). bits4&6 cleared (&~112) at $9988/$E1CE. 40 refs/15 subs.
NesSaveRam:0DA2:fief_is_daimyo_capital:[DATA-WALK CENSUS-CONFIRMED 2026-06-03, probe-ai-policy-distribution.py] Per-fief 0/1 flag = is this fief its owner's CAPITAL / home seat. ORACLE: across every real SRAM save the count of set flags == the count of distinct owning daimyo, and no two set fiefs share an owner — a clean bijection (exactly one capital per living daimyo). At game start each daimyo owns 1 fief = its capital (all set); the count shrinks as daimyo are eliminated. Uses: (a) transfers on conquest (cleared on the attacker's fief / set on the captured fief in apply_conquest_outcome — the seat relocates) — AND on a player MOVE answering 'lead them personally' out of the capital (driver_move $9782 clears src / sets dest, + ai_state[dest]=5 Direct): the player can VOLUNTARILY relocate the seat to dodge assassination ($A349) [ledger #19, 2026-06-12]; (b) DEFENSIVE bonus in ai_sum_battle_strength ($8E5D) as (fief_is_daimyo_capital[def]+2)*weight (defending the lord's castle); (c) the living-daimyo tally count_6da2_set ($D628, counts capital-or-ownerless fiefs) feeds the game-over victory/defeat branch; (d) gates command-entry branches in issue_province_command ($B7BB) + ai_econ_command_dispatch. Written via set_fief_ownership_record ($98A3: $6DA2[fief]=arg2). Resolves the long-standing '$6DA2 = unknown per-fief flag, needs a data-walk' ROADMAP thread. [[project_nobunaga_ai_command_pass]]
NesSaveRam:0FFE:tactical_battle_phase:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM MED] Tactical-battle PHASE enum {0,1,2}. switch(phase) in draw_tactical_cursor_region ($95CB); is_cell_valid_for_phase ($960E) gates cell validity on ==1/==2; map_render_driver branches if !=2; tactical cell-coord offset = phase*3 ($83A2). Read-only in bank 2 (set by the native battle-setup path).
NesSaveRam:1FCD:ui_window_col:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM MED] UI column / X coordinate. redraw_window ($CEC4) uses it as the line-wrap/column boundary (>31, ==32 for the 32-col nametable) and blits at column (col-1). Paired {col=$7FCD, row=$7FCF} loaded together in select_province_by_cursor ($D59D), province_select_prompt ($804C), poll_input ($D14E), find_record_9e3c ($E554).
NesSaveRam:1FCF:ui_cursor_row:[DATA-WALK AMEND MED] UI cursor/draw ROW coordinate, the row-axis partner of ui_window_col ($7FCD). find_record_9e3c ($E554) computes addr = base + (row-4)*28 + col; 0x00FF sentinel. ('menu count' refuted: ui_get_menu_count_7fcf's bounds-check at $CDC2 is dead code.)
NesSaveRam:1FD3:ui_input_mode:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM MED] Input-mode selector. poll_input ($D158) does switch(mode){case 0..4} dispatching distinct input/selection branches. Written 0 before the input-poll loops ($809A/$81BC), in the boot-zero block ($89C2, with $7FC7/$7FD1), and =1 on the AI UI path ($A45B). $7FCx-$7FDx UI-transient block. Exact per-case semantics only partly mapped.
NesSaveRam:0F79:ai_turn_loop_redispatch_flag:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM MED] Boolean turn-loop control flag (war/AI). vm_bootstrap ($A778) re-dispatches while set (JUMPT $A7FD) / proceeds when clear; ai_per_fief_command_driver ($B89B) skips the normal per-fief advance when set ($B98D) and early-breaks the scan ($B9A7). (2 of 4 reader subs act on it; the others are dead prologue-artifact reads. The set-to-1 path isn't in this material — all observed stores write 0.)
NesSaveRam:0F57:battle_winner_province_sel:[DATA-WALK AMEND MED] Battle/conquest province-index word — the WINNER/survivor-side selector. reassign_fiefs_to_conqueror ($DEC6): `if($6F57 == defender $6F63) winner=$6F5F else winner=$6F63`, driving the owner lookup (fief_to_daimyo_map) + fief reassignment ($E061/$AE43). NOT the attacker (that's $6F5F, per get_battle_side_province). Exact winner-vs-working-slot role unpinned -> kept generic. Province-index cluster $6F57/$6F5B/$6F5F/$6F63 (stride 2).
NesSaveRam:0F5B:active_province_idx_copy:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM MED] Held-stable province/fief index — a scratch copy of selected_province_idx ($6F5F) kept across the unpack/marry/view chain. daimyo_creation_stat_roll_screen ($87F0) stores $6F5F->$6F5B; used as a table index in the base-5 record unpack ($8086: (idx<<1)+$6EB1); marry path bounds-checks <53. Cluster $6F57/$6F5B/$6F5F/$6F63 (stride 2).
NesSaveRam:0EB1:daimyo_face_code_table:[HIGH 2026-06-01] Packed base-5 PORTRAIT face-code word per daimyo (SRAM word table, idx*2). Assigned uniquely at creation by assign_unique_daimyo_face_code ($DB97, dup-rejected); split into base-5 feature digits by compose_upload_daimyo_portrait ($8086) to select the bank-8 portrait_feature*_tiles -> the composite face. Indexed-mode only (data-xref blind).
NesSaveRam:0F5D:selected_record_idx_9e3c:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM MED] Index into the 34-byte-stride record table at $9E3C (0xFF = none). fief_select_input_loop ($ADF6) computes idx*34+$9E3C and a parallel idx*448+$8D5A; find_record_9e3c ($E554) gates idx<=8 (9 rows); get_6f5d_or_ff ($CCF9) handles the FF sentinel. Exact entity unpinned -> kept generic.
NesSaveRam:0F65:war_side_state_flag:[DATA-WALK AMEND MED] Per-side bit-7 war/siege state flag (byte, 0 or $80; accessor test_6f65_bit7 $D9E5). In resolve_siege_assault ($8E7D) it is the attacker strength coefficient ((bit7!=0)+2), mirroring the defender's province+$6DA2 byte on the next line. driver_war ($9956) sets $80 when the province's $6DA2 state byte is set; apply_conquest_outcome ($E1B1) writes bit7 into the conquered province's $6DA2 array. (CORRECTION 2026-06-10: is_unit_present $8F79 bytecode @ $8F84 DOES index $6F65 — LOADL 12, +$6F65, BYTE_DEREF, >>arg2, &1 — testing bits 0-4 as per-side unit-slot PRESENCE. So $6F65[side] is a PACKED byte: bits 0-4 = unit presence, bit 7 = war/siege state. The earlier 'indexes $6DA2/$6F5F' claim is REFUTED; whether bit-7 war-state truly lives at $6F65 vs sibling $6F66 to re-confirm when resolve_siege_assault $8E7D is ground.)
NesSaveRam:0F7D:war_attacker_gold:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM HIGH] Attacker GOLD in war/siege — head of the attacker triple $6F7D/$6F7F/$6F81 (+0 gold/+6 rice/+16 men). driver_war ($9967) deducts it from the target province's field +0; apply_conquest_outcome ($E0D3) sets conquered gold = attacker($6F7D)+defender($6F83). Sibling of war_attacker_rice/war_attacker_men.
NesSaveRam:0F7F:war_attacker_rice:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM HIGH] Attacker RICE (+6) — middle of the attacker triple. driver_war ($9931) sets it via number_input capped at the province rice field, then deducts ($9971); apply_conquest rice = $6F7F+$6F85 ($E0DE).
NesSaveRam:0F83:war_defender_gold:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM HIGH] Defender GOLD snapshot (+0) — head of the defender triple $6F83/$6F85/$6F87, mirror of the attacker triple. Snapshotted from the defending province in battle_init_clear_defending_province_fields ($92EF) + ai_commit_attack_deduct_resources ($9165); conquest gold = $6F7D+$6F83 ($E0D3).
NesSaveRam:0F85:war_defender_rice:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM HIGH] Defender RICE (+6) — middle of the defender triple. Snapshots the defending province's rice field ($92CA/$9046); conquest rice = $6F7F+$6F85 ($E0DE). (+6=rice cross-checked via harvest_income_sweep $A2C0.)
NesSaveRam:0F87:war_defender_men:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM HIGH] Defender MEN (+16) — defender mirror of war_attacker_men ($6F81). ai_attacker_outstrengths_defender ($8F10) compares $6F81 vs $6F87; conquest men = $6F81+$6F87 ($E0EA); battle_init zeroes the slot ($9337); also feeds transfer_force_triplet ($DF96).
NesSaveRam:0F7B:ai_planner_event_handler_select:[DATA-WALK AMEND MED] Enumerated 0-3 selector in ai_strategic_turn_planner ($A455, planner-local) picking WHICH random-event/disaster handler runs this turn: 1->decay_fief_wealth_output_disaster1 ($9CB3), 2->ravage_output_mark_weakness ($9D00), 3->ai_event_build_two_batches_dispatch ($9ED9); CALL-ptr dispatched ($A549). (Not a 'strategy mode' — the handler tables are decoded.)
NesSaveRam:0E09:ai_player_count:[DATA-WALK AMEND MED] AI-player count = 8 - newgame_player_count ($6D61, the 1..8 'How many players' input), write-once in init_new_game_state ($8B4B-$8B50; renders correctly as `8 - newgame_player_count` since 2026-06-01 — was the $40-$4F qimm-clear decompiler bug, not a SUB fold). Used as a loop bound (ravage sweep $9C22 runs 8-$6E09 = human-player count times) and an <8 gate (get_6e09 $D982). Sharpened from 'setup_count_complement' once $6D61 was pinned (batch 4).
NesSaveRam:0E0B:loan_rate:[DATA-WALK AMEND HIGH] First entry of the period-rolled MARKET rate table $6E0B/$6E0D/$6E0F/$6E11/$6E13 (roll_period_rate_table_6e0b $924A; $6E0B = rng_mod(10)+1 = 1-10). The LOAN rate: subhandler_9F04 ($9F45) sizes the borrowable principal as min(cw, cw*($6E0B+10)/(town-debt)) before the 'borrow' prompt; shown as 'Rate' in the Market view ($80B0). Sizes the loan, not interest (repay $9FAF never reads it).
NesSaveRam:0E0F:arms_buy_price_rate:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM HIGH] +4 entry of the Market rate table (= year_scaled_random/2, $9281). The ARMS price: the Market view formats it as 'Arms %2d.%1d' ($80E4); buy path effect_buy_arms ($A13A) + AI ai_state2_recruit_arm_train ($B5A5/$B5CA) deduct gold and grow the arms field (+22). Sibling of gold_rice_exchange_rate.
NesSaveRam:0E11:gold_men_hire_rate:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM HIGH] Market rate table entry (= pct_op(year_base,70), $928E). Gold cost per MAN: effect_hire_men ($A553) gold -= math32_muladddiv(men, $6E11); AI recruit ($B534) affordability via helper_8357. Men-side sibling of arms_buy_price_rate ($6E0F).
NesSaveRam:0E13:hire_gold_rate:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM MED] Year-scaled Market rate (rolls UP over the campaign: (rng_mod(101)+(current_game_year-1560)*10+4)/4, $92A5) pricing the Hire command's gold cost: effect_hire_pay_gold ($A2B5) subtracts math32_muladddiv(units,$6E13) from province gold; effect_ninja_sabotage ($A2E6, formerly 'effect_hire') gates affordability. 5th of the $6E0B table.
NesSaveRam:1BE0:ui_input_prompt_active_flag:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM HIGH] Boolean 'interactive input prompt active' gate — set 1 before / cleared 0 after every interactive-input call: prompt_select_player_daimyo ($86AD/$8745), driver_send around number_input ($9AB9/$9B0D), driver_view around select_province_by_cursor ($A72C/$A738). Consumed by the native input layer (~$D43C 'if==1 return -1'; reader is in raw-hex region so data-xref missed it).
NesSaveRam:1BE6:latched_selected_record_idx:[DATA-WALK AMEND MED] Latched copy of selected_record_idx_9e3c ($6F5D): get_6f5d_or_ff ($CD16) + repaint_screen ($CD90) do `if(sel!=0xFF){ $7BE6=sel; sel=255; }` — latch the menu selection on close, then clear the source. Read by battle_setup_select_province_phase ($AF98). Exact entity tracks $6F5D (unpinned).
NesSaveRam:1FC7:ui_pending_flag_7fc7:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM LOW] Consume-and-clear UI flag (1R/5W): the sole read ($CD4F in repaint_screen) gates a branch then clears it ($CD7B); set =1 in a develop path ($8B57); zeroed at boot/init ($835C/$89BE) in the ui_transient_state block. Specific pending-action unproven -> generic ui_ name.
NesSaveRam:1FD1:ui_msg_col_shift_flag:[POLARITY AMENDED + AXIS OPEN 2026-06-10] UI flag selecting the message-window shift coord (20 vs 22). open_message_window ($CC89) + message_display ($D338) branch on it. CORRECTIONS to the prior note: (1) POLARITY was inverted -- code is `flag ? 20 : 22`, i.e. !=0 -> 20, ==0 -> 22 (prior note said the opposite). (2) AXIS contested: in open_message_window the 20/22 lands in set_cursor's ROW arg (ui_cursor_row), reading as a vertical/ROW shift, NOT a column -- so the 'col_shift' name is suspect. Left un-renamed pending a read of message_display ($D338) to confirm the axis across both consumers. Written 0 at save-verify + init. Sibling of $7FCD/$7FCF/$7FD3.
NesSaveRam:1FDF:ui_input_sel_latch_7fdf:[DATA-WALK AMEND MED] Input/selection latch (holds buttons&1, a 1-bit toggle). 6 writers store 0xFF sentinel paired with ui_input_mode=0 on menu/screen init; poll_input ($D179) does change-detect `if((buttons&1)!=$7FDF){...; $7FDF=...}` then redraws. Reader lives in the un-disassembled $D159-$D286 switch body, so data-xref's 0R is a disasm artifact, not write-only.
NesSaveRam:0D61:newgame_player_count:[DATA-WALK AMEND HIGH] Number of HUMAN players (1..8). init_new_game_state: 'How many players' string ($B9CD) -> number_input ($8A2C); drives the 1..count player-setup menu loop. ai_player_count ($6E09) = 8 - this. 3 refs, all in init_new_game_state.
NesSaveRam:0E7D:ui_confirm_flag_6e7d:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM MED; AMEND 2026-06-12] The user-facing 'watch other daimyo's battles' setting (Other menu -> Battle, setting_watch_battles $B12B writes it). Read in the combat path (ai_commit_attack_deduct_resources $913D / $9130, `ui_confirm_flag_6e7d || ai_state==5`) to decide whether an AI-vs-AI battle is shown vs auto-resolved off-screen. Also reused as a transient A/B-confirm flag elsewhere (prompt_select_scenario_size $867B). NOT the 17/50 scenario value (that goes to scenario_fief_count). [ledger #22]
NesSaveRam:1BF5:tactical_cursor_cell_7bf5:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM MED] Tactical cursor cell coordinate — first of the pair set by set_combat_state_pair_7bf5_7bf7 ($8270: arg1->$7BF5, arg2->$7BF7). draw_tactical_cursor_region ($840B) reads both, validates via is_cell_valid_for_phase, and seeds calc_tactical_cell_coords. Paired with $7BF7.
NesSaveRam:1BF7:tactical_cursor_row_7bf7:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM HIGH] Row origin/counter of the cursor region on the 4-wide tactical grid; paired with column origin $7BF5. Set by set_combat_state_pair_7bf5_7bf7 ($8270), advanced +1 per row-wrap ((col+1)&3==2) in draw_tactical_cursor_region ($840B); 4x4 region.
NesSaveRam:1BAB:scenario50_event_current_fief_idx:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM HIGH] Byte fief index (0..49) carried between the two 50-fief scenario-event subs: written each iteration of scenario50_fief30_event_eligible's ($96B0) 255-terminated fief scan, read by reassign_daimyo24_fiefs_to_owner50 ($9621) as the selected_province_idx cursor. 50-fief scenario only (gated on $6D9D==50).
NesSaveRam:0F68:battle_staging_entry_flag_array:[DATA-WALK AMEND MED] Paired 0/1-flag column of the stride-2 battle-staging entry array (ids at $6F67); writer $8E99 sets it 0 ($8FD3) or 1 ($9614) via LOADR_imm2 (data-xref blind). vm_bootstrap reads element[0] as a scalar boolean: ==1 -> confirm-prompt $BF40; !=0 -> 0/1 arg to $A5E6.
NesSaveRam:0E33:post_elim_owner_sentinel_id:[DATA-WALK AMEND MED] 1-byte sentinel-ID holder, write-only (2W/0R): set to 51 by reassign_owner50_fiefs_to_daimyo24 ($99AB, daimyo-24 elimination branch before the $7FD5 owner-array rewrite) and to 50 by battle_setup_select_province_phase ($AF3B). Consumer cross-bank/unresolved; differing write values (50/51) keep it a provenance name.
NesSaveRam:0E4A:daimyo_pool_sp_6e4a:[DATA-WALK AMEND MED] Top-of-stack index for an adjacent LIFO at $6E4B; sole accessor list_op_6e4a ($DC0E) does inc/dec-then-access. Pops feed install_new_daimyo (fief_to_daimyo_map base $6E15) = a daimyo-ID pool. SP/count role solid; pool semantics MED.
NesSaveRam:0E48:ai_turn_planner_resume_flag:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM MED] Boolean latch (writes 0/1, reads tested ==1). ai_strategic_turn_planner ($A461) consumes-on-read + skips time-advance; vm_bootstrap ($A78C) gates battle-resume; bank-2 ($AA1A/$AF6A) bypass the interactive province pick. A 'resume mid-turn' gate.
NesSaveRam:0F61:sram_save_pending_flag:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM MED] Save-pending boolean in the SRAM-save cluster: cleared 0 after checksum verify ($82EB), after committing the checksum ($A440), and after the Y/N save-confirm ($B11C, before 'Game will save at end of season'). Read as a gate by ai_strategic_turn_planner ($A476) + the checksum syscall path ($A3AF).
NesSaveRam:0F66:battle_defender_status_flag_6f66:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM HIGH] Bit7-packed copy of the defending province's $6DA2 status byte: resolve_siege_assault ($8E57) + battle_init_clear ($92E1) set it = byte[$6DA2+def]<<7; cleared on resolution ($8F8E). Matches the bit7 test on war_side_state_flag ($6F65 @ $8E7D). Write-side snapshot (no readers found).
NesSaveRam:0F67:battle_defender_province_staging:[DATA-WALK AMEND MED] Sentinel-reset byte: set =0xFF at per_period_fief_daimyo_update_driver ($A369) + vm_bootstrap ($A796); read at $A7BA, copied to battle_defending_province ($6F63) and used as a !=0xFF gate ($A7C4). Seeds the defender province in bootstrap. (No enqueue site -> not a real 'pending' queue.)
NesSaveRam:0001:ai_per_fief_loop_index:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM MED] Per-fief command-pass index in ai_per_fief_command_driver ($B89B): read@$B8A4, incremented ($B996 = +1), reset 0 on exit ($B9AE); loop bound = scenario_fief_count ($6D9D), gated by ai_turn_loop_redispatch_flag ($6F79). Standalone word.
NesSaveRam:0D65:delay_loop_count:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM HIGH] Busy-wait delay length. delay_loop ($D73E) spins (outer = arg, inner 240); standard_delay ($D75E) PUSH_abs $6D65 -> CALL delay_loop. Written =50 at boot/init ($8352/$89B8); subhandler_B0D2 sets it = (number_input^2 << 1) = user-adjustable (a 'speed/message-delay' setting). $6D5F config_block neighborhood.
NesSaveRam:1BFB:combat_unit_window_mode_flag:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM MED] Combat unit-window mode flag (word, no index). Tested ==2 (draw_unit_stat_field $8B92, combat_unit_window_refresh early-return) and ==1 (dispatch loop $AC9C); reset 0 at init ($8DB5) + teardowns. Co-cleared with $7BF9 in repaint_screen.
NesSaveRam:1BF9:ui_state_flag_7bf9:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM MED] UI state boolean. All writes =0 (clear_rect_lower_right $CCBA, view_render_five_stats, repaint_screen $CD20 — co-cleared with $7FC7/$7FC9/$7FDF/$7BFB); read as a boolean branch in ai_per_fief_command_driver ($B930). SET meaning unproven -> generic ui_state name.
NesSaveRam:1BF3:combat_casualty_skip_flag_7bf3:[DATA-WALK AMEND HIGH] Gate that SUPPRESSES the casualty-apply branch: resolve_attack_apply_casualties ($9EDD) `if($7BF3) goto` skips the casualty decrement; cleared 0 in the apply path ($9FC8) and at the combat-turn loop top ($ADDC). Boolean (only ever assigned 0, branch-tested).
NesSaveRam:1BE2:fief_menu_info_mode_flag:[DATA-WALK CONFIRM MED] fief_info_display ($8724) writes it = arg, then branches: 0 = 12-row loop / nonzero = 21-row loop (which stat panel to draw); command_menu_select_loop reads it as a bool ($B6CB/$B711/$B737) and ==1 gates a cursor row. Standalone scalar.
NesSaveRam:1FC5:ui_msg_oneshot_flag_7fc5:[DATA-WALK AMEND HIGH] One-shot UI message flag: SET=1 in ai_run_all_units_combat_actions ($AC49); test-and-clear consumer in message_display ($D32B read -> $D335 clear); also cleared at title init ($88B2). (Decompiler renders the =1 set as =0 — the $40/$41 qimm-load gap; ROM byte $41 is authority.)
NesSaveRam:1FC9:ui_pending_flag_7fc9:[DATA-WALK AMEND MED] UI palette-pending/dirty flag. PRODUCER effect_view_a ($845B) sets =1 after ppu_render_rect; CONSUMER repaint_screen ($CD20) tests, runs 3 palette_write calls, then clears 0 ($CD4C). Sibling of ui_pending_flag_7fc7 (identical producer/consumer shape). (bank_01.c:321 mislabels the set as =0; ROM byte $41 is authority.)
NesSaveRam:1FCB:cutscene_id:[HIGH 2026-06-10] Cutscene/event id. trigger_cutscene ($E80C) writes arg1 here; bank-14 run_cutscene ($80AD) reads it as the index into cutscene_table ($AF80, stride 5).
NesSaveRam:1FE5:sound_request_id:[HIGH 2026-06-10] Requested sound/music id consumed by bank-10 play_audio_by_id ($8003): >64 no-op, <27 song (3 voices), 27-63 single SFX voice. Indexes the $8617 voice-config table.
NesSaveRam:1FDD:selected_province_idx_latch_7fdd:[DATA-WALK AMEND MED] Latched copy of selected_province_idx ($6F5F): written by prompt_select_player_daimyo ($8755) + issue_province_command ($B7A3); read in render_section_for_selected_province ($E6A2/$E6AB) as a province index into a per-fief table (+$FED8 17-fief / +$FEA6 50-fief). Analogous to the $6F5B/$7BE6 latches.
NesSaveRam:1FE7:ui_timer_gate_flag_7fe7:[DATA-WALK AMEND MED] Boot-zeroed ui_transient flag gating poll_input's timeout path: poll_input ($D1B2) `if($7FE7==2) goto` bypasses the frame_counter countdown + timeout switch and reads the controller directly. Written 0 at init + read_frame_timer ($D2AC). Only 0/2 observed -> 'gate' not 'mode'.
NesInternalRam:0600:oam_shadow:256-byte shadow OAM ($0600-$06FF), 64 sprites x 4 bytes. NMI DMAs it to PPU OAM via OAMDMA ($4014) page $06. Reset fills every sprite's Y (byte 0) and X (byte 3) with $F8 so unused sprites stay off-screen.
NesInternalRam:0090:palette_alt:32-byte alt palette buffer ($0090-$00AF). Used by palette_swap ($C36C, task $12) to atomically swap with palette_shadow for fade/transition effects. Reset-fill $3E (paired with palette_shadow).
NesInternalRam:0700:palette_shadow:32-byte palette shadow ($0700-$071F); foreground writes here + sets palette_dirty; $C6D4 uploads to PPU $3F00 next NMI. Reset-fill $3E (medium grey).
NesSaveRam:0F89:fief_index_list:[DATA PHASE 2026-10-27] Byte list of fief indices, passed by address: find_first_enemy_owned_fief, avg_daimyo_charisma_over_fief_list, mark_fief_list_entry_removed, select_provinces_and_assign_ai_state (25 refs, 15 subs). Kind only; its length and terminator are naming work.
NesSaveRam:0193:relations_matrix:[DATA PHASE 2026-10-27] Daimyo relations matrix base: read through relations_matrix_cell_addr / relations_matrix_get, written by set_pact_relation, used by effect_war_a. (400 = 50 x 8 past fief_history_table is a coincidence.)
NesSaveRam:1BAD:province_candidate_list:[DATA PHASE 2026-10-27] Byte list of provinces built by collect_high_loyalty_provinces_to_candidate_list, consumed by announce_seasonal_event, revolt_spread_sweep_flip_fief_ownership, decay_fief_list_wealth_and_output_disaster1.
NesSaveRam:1BEE:battle_unit_byte_table:[DATA PHASE 2026-10-27] Byte table indexed by side or unit: incremented in resolve_attack_apply_mutual_casualties, zeroed per entry in run_both_sides_combat_turn, tested > 0 in find_flagged_present_unit_type, read by ai_eval_battle_strength_total. Follows battle_side_strength_mod ($7BEA, a word pair). Role to be named in the naming phase.
NesSaveRam:1FD5:player_daimyo:[DATA PHASE 2026-10-27] Byte per human player: the daimyo that player controls. init_new_game_state sets each to -1 (255); poll_input compares player_daimyo[player] with fief_owner(..) where it prints 'Control %d' (player + 1); reassign_owner50_fiefs_to_daimyo24 rewrites 24 -> 51.
NesSaveRam:1B79:fief_revolt_type:[DATA PHASE 2026-10-27] Byte per fief: the revolt type. Values 6 and 7 select the message in select_rebellion_message (bank 0) and revolt_type_message (bank 15).
NesSaveRam:1FE1:input_mode3_latch:[DATA PHASE 2026-10-27] poll_input mode 3's latch: stores buttons & 1 ($D23A), read at $D1EE; battle_init_defender resets it to 255. The mode-3 twin of ui_input_sel_latch_7fdf two bytes below.
NesSaveRam:0E7F:list_remove_matching_list:[DATA PHASE 2026-10-27] Byte table indexed by fief: list_remove_matching takes it as its list, revolt_spread_sweep_flip_fief_ownership writes entries, ai_try_war_attack reads [selected_province_idx]. Provenance name; the role is naming work.
NesSaveRam:0FE5:unit_count_digit_tiles:[DATA PHASE 2026-10-27] 9-byte entries (side * 9): draw_unit_count_digits writes tile 178 or 179 and the digits, then ppu_copy_rect_wrap draws the entry.
NesSaveRam:1FED:sram_save_signature:[DATA PHASE 2026-10-27] The save's signature string: verify_sram_save_integrity strcmp's it with 'KOEI'; write_sram_save_checksum_and_signature strcpy's 'KOEI'; on failure the 'data can't be used' text. Follows sram_save_checksum.
NesSaveRam:1985:province_name_table:[HIGH 2026-10-28] SRAM table of 10-byte, zero-padded province names, indexed by province: redraw_window((idx * 10) + 0x7985) at $87C1 / $D9E4 draws one. Read from the SRAM dumps (traces/VICTORY-final-sram.dmp, aftertax.dmp, b2-beforecombat.dmp): 'Noto', 'Echigo', 'Musashi', 'Kaga', ... Missed by the data lane's hot list (2 refs, threshold 3).
NesPrgRom:3C004:relation_sram_base:[SRAM-ADDR 2026-06-10] SRAM base of the relations region (syscall16_sram_wrap, relation_base_6f4f).
NesPrgRom:3C300:relation_sram_8300:[SRAM-ADDR 2026-06-10] SRAM relations region address (syscall16_sram_wrap, relation_base_6f4f).
NesPrgRom:3C45C:strategic_map_chr_tiles:[MAP] Strategic-map CHR (bank 4), uploaded to PT1 $15B0 by repaint_screen. Tilemap cell V>=91 -> CHR $845C+(V-91)*16; terrain block runs to $8D5C (tiles 91-234). Cells <=80 are the shared game font (fief-number labels). See render-strategic-map.py.
NesPrgRom:3CD5A:window_tile_gfx_8d5a_alias:[GFX-TILES 2026-06-10] Alias of window_tile_gfx_8d5a ($8D5A), read by find_record (ppu_copy_rect_wrap).
NesPrgRom:3CD5C:strategic_map_section_tilemaps:[MAP] 9 strategic-map section tilemaps (bank 4), 0x1C0=448 B each = 28x16 tiles, blitted to the nametable by render_map_section(section). 17-fief uses sections 0-1, 50-fief uses 0-8 (discrete pages, not a scroll). Cells <=80 = font glyphs, >=81 = terrain. See render-strategic-map.py.
NesPrgRom:3DD1C:strategic_map_section_attributes:[MAP] 9 strategic-map section attribute tables (bank 4), 0x20=32 B each (BG sub-palette per 16x16 quad), uploaded to nametable attrs $23C8 by render_map_section.
NesPrgRom:3DE3C:record_sram_9e3c_alias:[SRAM-ADDR 2026-06-10] Alias of record_sram_9e3c ($9E3C), read by find_record.
NesPrgRom:3E57E:map_cell_sram_a57e:[SRAM-ADDR 2026-06-10] SRAM map-cell pool address (syscall16_sram_wrap, read_map_cell).
NesPrgRom:3E604:portrait_gfx_a604:[GFX-TILES 2026-06-10] Portrait/record tile-upload source (ppu_upload_block_wrap in unpack_record_to_sram). Type confirmed from C usage; exact image = viewing-deferred.
NesPrgRom:3EBA4:portrait_gfx_eyes:[GFX-TILES 2026-06-10] Portrait eyes tile set (uploaded at part_eyes*96 by unpack_record_to_sram).
NesPrgRom:3ED84:portrait_gfx_ad84:[GFX-TILES 2026-06-10] Portrait tile-upload source (ppu_upload_block_wrap, unpack_record_to_sram).
NesPrgRom:3EE34:portrait_sram_ae34:[SRAM-ADDR 2026-06-10] SRAM work region for unpack_record_to_sram (syscall16_sram_wrap).
NesPrgRom:3EE70:portrait_sram_ae70:[SRAM-ADDR 2026-06-10] SRAM work region for unpack_record_to_sram.
NesPrgRom:3EE8E:portrait_sram_ae8e:[SRAM-ADDR 2026-06-10] SRAM work region for unpack_record_to_sram.
NesPrgRom:3EEAC:portrait_sram_aeac:[SRAM-ADDR 2026-06-10] SRAM work region for unpack_record_to_sram.
NesPrgRom:3F144:jumptab_b144:[ROM-DATA] pointer/dispatch table; read by draw_daimyo_portrait via imm-word ptr; bytes: e9 e9 e9 e9 e9 e9 e9 e9 e9 e9 e9 e9
NesPrgRom:3F67A:strategic_map_bg_palette:[MAP] Strategic-map/UI BG palette table (read by repaint_screen), colors stored as words w/ 0 high byte: sub-pal0 $3E/$12/$29/$30 = backdrop/sea/land/coast, sub-pal1 $3E/$16/$38/$30 = volcanic red/yellow/white (mountain peaks).
NesPrgRom:3F77D:str_marriage_event_msgs:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] '...wants a %s','Demand gold','marriage pact','accept'
NesPrgRom:3F7CC:marry_palette:[GFX-PALETTE 2026-06-10] Marriage-scene palette words (palette_write_wrap, marry_helper).
NesPrgRom:3FEA6:province_to_map_section_50:[MAP] 50-fief scenario: province index -> strategic-map section (values 0-8, 50 entries). Indexed by selected_province_idx in driver_map/render_section_for_selected_province; the scenario_fief_count==50 branch selects this table (vs province_to_map_section_17 $FED8).
NesPrgRom:3FED8:province_to_map_section_17:[MAP] 17-fief scenario: province index -> strategic-map section (values 0/1, 17 entries). 50-fief uses province_to_map_section_50 $FEA6.
