NesPrgRom:3EF92:vm_op_unused_brk:[HIGH 2026-10-28] Handler of the 37 VM opcodes NA1's bytecode never uses ($80, $91-$9F, $CE, $EB-$FE: 0 of 23,802 instructions in banks 0/1/2/10/14/15). It is a BRK; irq_handler ($C139) sees the B flag and dispatches a syscall by whatever id is in brk_dispatch_id, then RTI lands at $EF94 (jmp dispatcher). A trap for an opcode that cannot occur, not a syscall API. Was 'vm_op_trigger_syscall_shared'; the discover gate's $EF92/$EF93 overlap conflict.
NesPrgRom:3EF93:vm_op_FF_unused_brk:[HIGH 2026-10-28] Handler of VM opcode $FF (never used: 0 of 23,802 instructions). It enters at $EF92's BRK signature byte, itself 00 = BRK, so its RTI would return to $EF95, inside the jmp at $EF94. Was 'vm_op_FF'.
NesPrgRom:3F020:vm_op_B2_pushA_B2:VM opcode $B2 handler (pushA_B2).
NesPrgRom:3CA03:call_bank10_entry:[MED] Tail-calls call_bank_wrap(10) = syscall_dispatch call_bank (id 7) on bank 10 (audio). Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CA12:deduct_byte_at:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Subtract-in-place on a byte pointer: *(byte*)arg1 = *(byte*)arg1 - (byte)arg2; return the new value (body @ $CA17). REFUTES the old [LOW] 'compares vs a const' note — there is no compare; the undecoded-op guess was wrong. Generic byte primitive, 7 sites. Was 'byte_helper_ca12'.
NesPrgRom:3CA31:word_sub_saturating:[MED] Saturating 16-bit subtract: r = *(word*)arg1 - arg2, floored to 0 on underflow, stored back. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CA65:is_digit:[HIGH] Returns true if arg1 in '0'..'9' (48..57). libc isdigit. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CA7E:strlen:[HIGH] Counts bytes from arg1 until NUL; returns length. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CA97:fill_bytes:[DEAD: no caller in any bank and 0 executions in 30.3 M traced steps (discover 2026-10-27)] [HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] memset: write byte arg3 into arg2 bytes starting at arg1 (`while(arg2){*arg1++=arg3; arg2--}`). REFUTES the old 'derived byte, not resolved' note -- the stored value is just (byte)arg3. Generic byte-fill primitive. Was 'fill_bytes_ca97'.
NesPrgRom:3CAB0:strcmp:[HIGH] Compares bytes at arg1/arg2 until mismatch or NUL; returns byte difference. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CAD9:strcpy:[HIGH] Copies bytes arg2->arg1 until NUL inclusive; returns original dest. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CAF0:memchr:[DEAD: no caller in any bank and 0 executions in 30.3 M traced steps (discover 2026-10-27)] [HIGH] Scans arg1 for a target byte over arg3 bytes; returns pointer on match else 0. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CB11:is_lower:[MED] Char range test from 'a' (97); lowercase classifier (gates to_upper). Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CB30:to_upper:[HIGH] If is_lower($CB11), subtract 32 -> uppercase ASCII. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CB4C:abs16:[HIGH CONFIRMED] Signed 16-bit absolute value: if (arg1 < 0) negate; return arg1. Decompiles to that shape; used by select_quadrant_damage_by_direction for |dx| vs |dy|. (was abs16.) Confirmed 2026-06-01.
NesPrgRom:3CB6F:max_word:[HIGH] Returns max(arg1,arg2). Mirror of min_word ($CB5E). Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CB80:swap_byte:[HIGH] Swaps the two bytes pointed to by arg1 and arg2. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CB94:swap_word:[HIGH] Swaps the two 16-bit words pointed to by arg1 and arg2 (via local temp). Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CBA4:chr_bank0_set_wrap:[HIGH] Thin wrapper: syscall_dispatch(...,21) = set_chr_bank0_reg (SOROM WRAM gate). Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CBB1:call_bank_wrap:[HIGH] Thin wrapper: syscall_dispatch(arg1,7) = call_bank (JSR bank arg1's $8000). Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CC42:ppu_fill_rect_wrap:[HIGH] Builds the param struct, calls syscall_dispatch(...,12) = ppu_fill_rect. The common menu/window blit wrapper. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CC54:ppu_copy_rect_wrap:[HIGH] Builds struct, calls syscall_dispatch(...,20) = ppu_copy_rect. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CCBA:clear_rect_lower_right:[DEAD: no caller in any bank and 0 executions in 30.3 M traced steps (discover 2026-10-27)] [HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] ppu_fill_rect_wrap(20,20,29,25,1) (blank the lower-right panel, cols 20-29 rows 20-25) + ui_state_flag_7bf9 = 0; return 0. REFUTES the old 'returns mem_7BF9' note -- it CLEARS the flag (and a rect), doesn't read it. Sibling of clear_rect_top_strip/left_*/right_panel. Was 'ui_get_7bf9'.
NesPrgRom:3CCD1:clear_rect_top_strip:[DEAD: no caller in any bank and 0 executions in 30.3 M traced steps (discover 2026-10-27)] [HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] BLANKS a rect with tile $01 (not a 'window draw'): ppu_fill_rect_wrap(2,3,29,3,1) = cols 2-29 of row 3, a full-width 1-row strip near the top. Old comment had the 5 args reversed AND miscategorized (wrong-category, cf. fief_owner/palette_swap). Renamed from clear_rect_top_strip (chapters may cite the old name).
NesPrgRom:3CCE1:reset_prompt_selection:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] ppu_fill_rect_wrap(2,26,29,26,1) (blank the bottom prompt strip, row 26) + ui_input_sel_latch_7fdf = 255; return 255. REFUTES the old 'returns the cursor selection' note -- it SETS $7FDF=255 (no-selection sentinel), not reads it. The 'cancel/reset the bottom prompt' primitive. Was 'ui_get_cursor_sel_7fdf'.
NesPrgRom:3CCF9:get_6f5d_or_ff:[DEAD: no caller in any bank and 0 executions in 30.3 M traced steps (discover 2026-10-27)] [LOW] Returns mem_6F5D unless it is the 0xFF sentinel. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CDAF:cursor_advance_row:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Advance the text cursor to the next menu row: ui_window_col=2; ui_cursor_row++; if (ui_cursor_row+1 > 27) wrap ui_cursor_row=3 (return 3 on wrap, else 0). REFUTES the old 'returns menu item count' note -- it WRITES the cursor, doesn't read a count. The line-feed used to lay menu rows down the screen. Was 'ui_get_menu_count_7fcf'.
NesPrgRom:3CDCA:char_classify:[MED] Char classification: range-tests vs 47/65/95 + switch -> class code (alnum/punct/control). Backs text layout. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CE81:char_advance_width:[MED] Per-character width/advance: special-cases newline (==10), uses char_classify + menu count. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CF50:fill_nametable_wrap:[MED] Wrapper: syscall_dispatch(1,0,5) = fill_nametable (nt 1, fill 0) -> clear screen. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CF5D:fill_attr_wrap:[MED] Wrapper: syscall_dispatch(0,0,8) = fill_attr_quadrant (quadrant 0, fill 0). Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CF6A:ppu_render_rect_wrap:[HIGH] Wrapper: builds struct, syscall_dispatch(...,13) = ppu_render_rect. 21 callers. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CF7C:ppu_upload_block_wrap:[HIGH] Wrapper: syscall_dispatch(...,1) = ppu_upload_block (PRG->PPU bulk). 30 callers. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CF8B:palette_write_wrap:[HIGH] Wrapper: syscall_dispatch(...,4) = palette_write. 33 callers (hottest in cluster). Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CF98:num_to_ascii:[HIGH] Recursive integer->ASCII-digit conversion (divide by 10, emit digit via arg1 ptr). itoa. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CFD4:atoi_decimal:[HIGH] ASCII decimal -> integer: local = local*10 + (byte-48) while digit; advances arg1. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CFFC:format_string:[HIGH] printf-style: scans for '%', switches on C/D/S, space-pads to width, calls num_to_ascii/atoi/strlen/to_upper. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3D14E:poll_input:[HIGH] Controller-poll state machine (switch on mem_7FD3), indexes the input/selection table at $7FD5, returns a button code via syscall_dispatch(...,6)=read_controller. THE cursor/input handler (confirms prior analysis); 11 callers. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3D287:wait_button_edge:[HIGH] Edge-detect on poll_input: spin while a button is held, then return the next press code. Debounce primitive; 10 callers. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3D29D:read_frame_timer:[MED] Branches on arg1 (0/1/2) then returns frame_counter; a timing/poll accessor. 19 callers. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3D2F9:clear_rect_left_upper:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] BLANKS a rect with tile $01: ppu_fill_rect_wrap(2,8,9,19,1) = cols 2-9, rows 8-19 (left-side panel, upper). Old comment had args reversed + miscategorized as 'window draw'. Renamed from clear_rect_left_upper.
NesPrgRom:3D309:clear_rect_left_lower:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] BLANKS a rect with tile $01: ppu_fill_rect_wrap(2,20,9,26,1) = cols 2-9, rows 20-26 (left-side panel, lower); 15 callers. Old comment had args reversed + miscategorized. Renamed from clear_rect_left_lower.
NesPrgRom:3D31A:clear_rect_left_lower_alt:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] Tail-calls clear_rect_left_lower (alias/same blank of cols 2-9, rows 20-26). Not a 'window draw'. Renamed from clear_rect_left_lower_alt.
NesPrgRom:3D586:count_decimal_digits:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] return number of base-10 digits in arg1: while(arg1){arg1/=10; n++}; return n (0 for arg1==0). Used to right-size/position a number for display. Renamed from count_decimal_digits (behavioral).
NesPrgRom:3D609:ui_prompt_redraw:[MED] UI prompt helper: reads ui state (cc7b/cc89/cce1), redraw_window, wait_button_edge. 5 callers. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3D628:count_6da2_set:[MED] Scans the $6DA2 per-fief byte array over scenario_fief_count, counting flagged entries. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3D677:draw_current_year:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] draw_message(0xF6C4, current_game_year) -- printf+draw the current year via msg $F6C4. Was 'draw_window_f6c4' (the value is current_game_year, not a fixed window).
NesPrgRom:3D687:draw_current_season:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] redraw_window with the season string selected by current_season (case 0/1/2/3 -> $F6C7/$F6CE/$F6D5/$F6DA). Renders the Spring/Summer/Fall/Winter banner. (This was a DREAM phi-clobber victim -- always showed $F6C7 -- fixed 2026-06-10; now value-correct.) Was 'redraw_window_f6c7'.
NesPrgRom:3D73E:delay_loop:[HIGH] Nested busy-wait: inner counts 240, outer decrements arg1 to 0. A frame/cycle delay. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3D78B:daimyo_name_width:[MED] Computes daimyo_name_table[owner] addr (*9+$77A8) then char_advance_width(44) -- measures/positions a daimyo name. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3D7AF:draw_daimyo_name:[MED] redraw_window on daimyo_name_table ($77A8 + owner*9) -- renders a daimyo's name. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3D7CD:daimyo_record_addr:[HIGH] Returns daimyo record base = arg1*7 + $752F (7-byte per-daimyo PERSON records, distinct from the 26-byte province/fief record at $7001). The daimyo-record accessor (40+ readers via fief_to_daimyo_record_addr/get_daimyo_stat4_by_fief). FIELD MAP (ground-truthed 2026-06-02 via cross-year save-dump comparison + the death-formula code): +0=AGE (CONFIRMED: monotonic +, uniform across all daimyo; check_daimyo_natural_death $9154 gates on age>=70), +1=HEALTH (CONFIRMED: declines over time; same sub uses health/4 in the death roll -> the cracked (age-10-health/4)/300 formula), +2=DRIVE (stable across years; drained -1 on marry-refusal; compared daimyo-vs-daimyo in a COMBAT context bank1 $8EB8), +3=LUCK (CONFIRMED behavior: wanders +/-5 each season via drift_daimyo_luck; marry-drained -- the random walk IS luck fluctuating), +4=CHARISMA (CONFIRMED: rises over time, the HOTTEST-read field ~9 reads -> income variance, event-boon size, event eligibility, marry; get_daimyo_stat4_by_fief), +5=IQ (stable; NOT marry-drained), +6=portrait/status flag (0=preset/historical, 1=composite/generated). Stat names (+2 Drive/+3 Luck/+4 Charisma/+5 IQ) per Chris/manual 2026-06-02. apply_scenario_starting_stat_boosts boosts +1..+5 (the 5 stats) by skill*5, leaving +0/+6. OPEN (footprint-with-combat): full per-stat impact map (which subsystem each of Drive/Luck/Charisma/IQ gates). [[project_nobunaga_daimyo_record_structure]]
NesPrgRom:3D7DA:fief_to_daimyo_record_addr:[HIGH] daimyo_record_addr(fief_to_daimyo_map[arg1]) -- the owning daimyo's record for a fief. 21 callers (hot). Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3D7F7:clear_econ_stats_if_no_output:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] On province arg1's $7001 record: if output (+8) == 0, zero loyalty (+12) and wealth (+14). I.e. when a province loses its economic base, clear its economic-derived stats. Field offsets per the province_table_live ($7001) map. Was 'province_clear_fields_d7f7'.
NesPrgRom:3D815:clear_military_stats_if_no_men:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] On province arg1's $7001 record (base $7011 = +16): if men (+16) == 0, zero morale (+18), skill (+20), arms (+22). I.e. when a province's army is gone, clear its military stats. Field offsets per the province_table_live ($7001) map. Was 'province_clear_fields_d815'.
NesPrgRom:3D8BA:develop_gain:[MED] Shared develop-family gain calc: math32_3arg over sqrt_int of two record fields (the floor(amount*5/sqrt(...)) idiom behind Grow/Give-Men). Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3D8F2:develop_gain_capped_loyalty:[MED 2026-06-10] return min(develop_gain(arg2, arg1+12, arg1+8), arg1->header - arg1->loyalty) -- a development gain clamped to the loyalty headroom (header minus current loyalty). Was 'record_grow_capped_d8f2'. (The +12/+8 field offsets tie to the $7001 province-record map -- pending.)
NesPrgRom:3D919:develop_gain_capped_wealth:[MED 2026-06-10] Sibling of develop_gain_capped_loyalty: return min(develop_gain(arg2, arg1+14, arg1+4), arg1->header - arg1->wealth) -- gain clamped to the wealth headroom. Was 'record_grow_capped_d919'.
NesPrgRom:3D940:record_apply_two_grows:[MED] Applies develop_gain_capped_loyalty and _d919 to two fields of a record (loyalty/wealth-like pair). Callers $8379,$8FF8. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3D962:set_6da1_bit7:[MED] Reads byte $6DA1, ORs in 0x80 (sets high/sign bit), stores back. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3D982:is_ai_count_ge_8:[MED 2026-06-10] return ai_player_count >= 8 (a >=8 threshold predicate on the $6E09 daimyo/AI count). Sharpens the old 'compares then returns mem_6E09' note (the comparison IS the return). OPEN: what 8 gates (likely a roster/slot cap). Was 'get_6e09'.
NesPrgRom:3D98D:get_province_ai_state:[HIGH] Returns province_ai_state[arg1] ($6CF7+arg1). 37 callers; canonical AI-state getter (pairs with province_state_is_FF). Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3D9A9:get_6da2_cur:[MED] Returns byte $6DA2 + selected_province_idx. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3D9C8:province_ai_state_addr:[HIGH] Returns &province_ai_state[arg1] ($6CF7+arg1); the pointer form used to WRITE state (e.g. apply_conquest_outcome). Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3D9D3:redraw_window_row:[MED 2026-06-10] redraw_window(0x7985 + arg1*10) -- draws the arg1-th entry of a 10-byte-stride row/string table at $7985. (The $7985 table's exact contents still open.) Was 'draw_window_row_7985'.
NesPrgRom:3D9E5:test_6f65_bit7:[MED] Returns true if bit7 of byte $6F65+arg1 is NOT set. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3D9F7:revolt_type_message:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] return ($7B79[arg1] == 7) ? msg_christns_f6f5 : msg_rioters_f6fe -- picks the uprising-type message string for province arg1 (the $7B79 byte: 7 = Christian uprising, else rioters/peasant revolt). Was 'classify_7b79'.
NesPrgRom:3DA24:scaled_force_transfer:[MED 2026-06-10] return min_word(pct_op(arg1, math32_2arg(arg4,arg3)) + pct_op(arg2|1, math32_2arg(arg3,arg4)), arg5) -- a proportional split of two quantities by a ratio (the two math32 terms are the complementary proportions arg3:arg4), clamped to arg5. Callers effect_move + transfer_force_triplet -> computes a transferred force/resource amount. Was 'scaled_transfer_da24'. OPEN: exact per-arg roles (which is men vs ratio).
NesPrgRom:3DAAB:load_daimyo_relation_row:[MED 2026-06-10] Loads daimyo arg1's 8-byte relation row (stride 8) from the bank-4 scenario relation table (scenario_fief_count==17 ? relation_sram_8300 : relation_sram_base) into the $6F4F buffer, returns $6F4F. Sharpens the old 'returns base $6F4F' note -- it FILLS the buffer first (the SRAM load was missed). Was 'relation_base_6f4f'.
NesPrgRom:3DB4B:draw_owner_name:[MED] Maps fief->owner (fief_owner) then redraw_window on daimyo_name_table ($77A8 + owner*9). Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3DB6E:draw_province_lord_name:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] If province arg1 has an owner (province_ai_state[arg1] != 255): redraw_window(daimyo_name_table + fief_owner(arg1)*9) -- the owner's name; else redraw_window(msg_no_lord). Was 'draw_window_f706'. (This was the DREAM phi-clobber that surfaced the fix -- 4-c used to always draw msg_no_lord; now value-correct.)
NesPrgRom:3DB97:assign_unique_daimyo_face_code:[HIGH 2026-06-01] The REPLACEMENT-daimyo portrait generator (called only by install_new_daimyo $E21B = death/succession). First SETS daimyo_record[+6] = 1 (the generated flag, so draw_daimyo_portrait takes the composite path), then rolls a unique base-5 RNG face code (rng_mod(5)*125 + *25 + *5 + *1 = 4 base-5 digits), dup-rejected vs the $6EB1 word table, stored at the owner slot. compose_upload_daimyo_portrait ($8086) later splits it into feature digits for the bank-8 composite face. The ORIGINAL 50 never run this -> they keep record[+6]=0 and the preset dedicated portrait. (was assign_unique_id_6eb1.)
NesPrgRom:3DC0E:pool_push_pop:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Stack op on the $6E4A pool (sp=$6E4A, elements @ $6E4B): if arg1<=49 PUSH arg1 (sp++ then store), else (sentinel >49) POP (sp-- then return [sp]). Confirms the old count-prefixed-list note as a push/pop stack keyed on arg1. 6 sites. Elements are ids 0-49 (fief range) -- the 'daimyo_pool' var label may be a misnomer; flag. Was 'list_op_6e4a'.
NesPrgRom:3DC3C:list_remove_matching:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Scans the $6E7F list (scenario_fief_count entries) and marks every entry == arg1 as 0xFF (remove-by-value). Confirms the old note. 6 sites. Purpose of the $6E7F list itself still open. Was 'list_remove_6e7f'.
NesPrgRom:3DC66:fief_to_mapid:[HIGH] Returns province_to_mapid_table[arg1] (arg1==0 passthrough; scenario_fief_count==50 selects extended path). Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3DC88:read_map_cell:[HIGH] sram_wrap read of a tactical map cell: $A57E + fief_to_mapid(battle_defending_province)*55 + row(arg2)*11 + col(arg1). The per-cell map source (matches the ROM->Map $A57E finding). Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3DCB2:generate_daimyo_name:[HIGH] Daimyo NAME GENERATOR: RNG-picks a row from each syllable table ($F930, $F95D), concatenates into a buffer, rejects duplicates vs daimyo_name_table ($77A8) via strcmp. The regenerator hypothesized in the $77A8 comment. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3DD81:init_new_daimyo_province_stats:[HIGH] Seeds a freshly-conquered province + new daimyo: daimyo byte = rng_mod(20)+20; per-field pct_op(rng+base) scaling; town($700D)+=50, rice($7013)+=50; $6D2D=20. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3DE78:select_uprising_message:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Picks the uprising/rebellion message for province arg1: if ai_turn_flags&32 -> msg_rebels_f72e; elif ai_turn_flags&16 -> $796A; else switch arg1: {7,23}->$F720, {13,30}->$F728 (specific provinces/sites), default -> revolt_type_message(arg1). 5 sites. Was 'select_message_string_de78'.
NesPrgRom:3DEC1:reassign_fiefs_to_conqueror:[HIGH] Loops all fiefs; those owned by the defending daimyo get fief_to_daimyo_map[fief] = conqueror and $6DA2 cleared. Post-conquest ownership transfer. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3DF3D:daimyo_stat_transfer:[MED] +1 to daimyo-record fields +2/+4/+5 of arg1's daimyo, -1 to arg2's (stat handoff via fief_to_daimyo_record_addr). Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3DF73:transfer_force_triplet:[MED] 3-iteration copy of a word triplet (via scaled_force_transfer) into the $7013 army/force region; selected->defending force transfer. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3DFBC:clamp_field_6d2d_to_30:[MED] For each tax-flagged fief (defender_owner_is_keyed_daimyo), caps the per-fief byte $6D2D at 30. ($6D2D unlabeled; init to 20 by init_new_daimyo_province_stats.) Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3DFFE:cap_arms_at_index:[MED 2026-06-10] cap = arg2->arms/50 + 20; if the $76AB[arg1] entry (stride 5) EXCEEDS cap, spill the excess (old-cap) into $76A9[arg1] and clamp $76AB[arg1] to cap. Caps a per-index arms value, moving overflow to the paired $76A9 table. Sharpens the old note ('if set' -> 'if > cap'). Was 'update_arms_table_dffe'.
NesPrgRom:3E03C:apply_conquest_outcome:[HIGH] Post-battle conquest orchestrator: rewrites the defending province stats from battle scratch ($6F7D-$6F87), updates fief_to_daimyo_map, calls daimyo_stat_transfer + reassign/neutralize helpers, caps via cap_fief_stats. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3E1E7:clear_fief_pair_matrix:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Plays sound 29 (call_bank10_entry), then zeroes BOTH the row and column of fief arg1 in the symmetric 54-stride fief×fief matrix at $6193 (clears [i][arg1] and [arg1][i] for all i < scenario_fief_count) -- removes fief arg1 from the pairwise adjacency/relations grid. Renamed from clear_fief_pair_6193 (drop addr suffix); sharpened (it clears a whole row+col, + the sound).
NesPrgRom:3E21B:install_new_daimyo:[HIGH] Installs a new daimyo on a fief: fief_to_daimyo_map[fief] = list_op_6e4a(0xFF), province_ai_state=0, $6DA2=0, then confirm_prompt. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3E275:announce_daimyo_death:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] The "a daimyo was killed" announcement: clear_fief_pair_matrix(arg1) (remove the fief from the pairwise grid + sound 29), message_display(daimyo_name_table + fief_owner(arg1)*9) (the slain lord's name), redraw_window(msg_was_killed); if the province is still active, draw_message(msg_in_fief_2d_in_the_year_d, arg1+1, current_game_year); confirm_prompt(). Was 'prompt_helper_e275' (wrong-category).
NesPrgRom:3E2AF:copy_arms_record_5:[MED] Copies a 5-byte record from arg2 into $76A9 + arg1*5 (the per-fief arms/force record, stride 5). Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3E2D6:draw_daimyo_name_menu:[MED] Thin wrapper: draw_message(daimyo_name_table $77A8, $F77F) -- renders the daimyo-name list/menu. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3E425:find_fiefs_of_owner:[HIGH] Resolves arg1->daimyo (fief_owner) then scans all fiefs collecting those with the same owner. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3E454:neutralize_fief:[MED] If province_ai_state != 0xFF: set state = -1, clear $6DA2, $6D2D = 20, copy_arms_record_5, recompute (record_sram_9e3c_alias). Depose/neutralize a fief. Session C 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3E4A2:build_owned_fief_list:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Builds the $6F89 list of fiefs passing get_6da2_cur(): iterate selected_province_idx 0..scenario_fief_count, append each that passes, FF-terminate; saves/restores selected_province_idx. (Same $6F89 candidate buffer build_eligible_province_list writes.) Renamed from build_owned_fief_list_6f89 (drop addr suffix).
NesPrgRom:3E554:redraw_fief_on_map:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Locate-and-redraw one fief on the current strategic-map section. If a section is loaded (selected_record_idx_9e3c<=8): load that section's 34-byte record list (record_sram_9e3c_alias + idx*34, bank 4), walk its (col,row,fief_id) triples until fief_id==arg1, then ppu_copy_rect the fief's ~8-wide label tile strip (from window_tile_gfx_8d5a_alias, the 0x1C0-stride section tile source) at (col,row) + draw_province_lord_name(arg1); restore the cursor. 10 sites (hot). Was 'find_record_9e3c' (it draws, not just finds). Pairs with render_map_section ($E5F2).
NesPrgRom:3E694:render_section_for_selected_province:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] render_map_section(province_to_map_section[selected_province_idx_latch_7fdd]) -- look up which map section contains the latched selected province (table province_to_map_section_50 or _17 by scenario) and render it. The 'jump the map to the selected province' entry. Was 'dispatch_map_helper_e694'.
NesPrgRom:3E6B9:unpack_composite_face_record:[MED->HIGH 2026-06-01] The COMPOSITE-portrait builder for GENERATED daimyo: called by draw_daimyo_portrait ($E76F) on the flag==1 path. Unpacks the base-5 face code $6EB1[$6F5B*2] via repeated div/mod into a 9-wide record, writes to SRAM (uses ppu_upload_block_wrap/sram_wrap) — the same base-5 face machinery as compose_upload_daimyo_portrait ($8086). (was unpack_composite_face_record.)
NesPrgRom:3F68A:msg_control_n:[ROM-STR] "Control %d" (poll_input prints player + 1)
NesPrgRom:3F6A1:cursor_nav_fmt_d_1:[ROM-STR] "%d" (cursor_nav_loop, 1st of 3)
NesPrgRom:3F6A4:cursor_nav_fmt_d_2:[ROM-STR] "%d" (cursor_nav_loop, 2nd of 3)
NesPrgRom:3F6A7:cursor_nav_space:[ROM-STR] " " (cursor_nav_loop; the tables lane read it as binary)
NesPrgRom:3F6A9:cursor_nav_fmt_d_3:[ROM-STR] "%d" (cursor_nav_loop, 3rd of 3)
NesPrgRom:3F6C4:draw_current_year_fmt:[ROM-STR] "%d" (draw_current_year prints current_game_year)
NesPrgRom:3F6C7:msg_spring:[ROM-STR] "Spring" (draw_current_season)
NesPrgRom:3F6CE:msg_summer:[ROM-STR] "Summer" (draw_current_season)
NesPrgRom:3F6D5:msg_fall:[ROM-STR] "Fall" (draw_current_season)
NesPrgRom:3F6DA:msg_winter:[ROM-STR] "Winter" (draw_current_season)
NesPrgRom:3F720:uprising_label_zealots:[ROM-STR] "Zealots" (select_uprising_message; bank 1 msg_zealots $BA43 is a different string, 'Zealots ')
NesPrgRom:3F728:uprising_label_monks:[ROM-STR] "Monks" (select_uprising_message)
NesPrgRom:3C4DC:ui_unused:Reserved.
NesPrgRom:3C537:wait_vblank:Spin until PPUSTATUS bit 7 set; early-out if skip_vblank_wait ($0080) non-zero. Calls music_driver during spin.
NesPrgRom:3C54F:nmi_off:Clear bit 7 of ppuctrl_shadow (disable NMI generation); used as the NMI re-entry guard
NesPrgRom:3C567:rendering_on:OR $18 into ppumask_shadow (enable BG + sprite rendering)
NesPrgRom:3C570:write_ppumask:Write A to PPUMASK ($2001) and update ppumask_shadow
NesPrgRom:3C628:controller_poll:Strobe $4016 and shift 8 bits into $006E (P1) or $006F (P2); X = player index
NesPrgRom:3C68A:nmi_on:Set bit 7 of ppuctrl_shadow (enable NMI generation)
NesPrgRom:3C693:ppu_safe_gate:Composite preamble for foreground PPU updates: nmi_off → wait_vblank → rendering_off
NesPrgRom:3C69D:rendering_off:AND $E7 into ppumask_shadow (clear BG + sprite enable; blank screen)
NesPrgRom:3C6A6:write_ppuctrl:Write A to PPUCTRL ($2000) and update ppuctrl_shadow
NesPrgRom:3C6AD:mul_xy_by_3:Helper used by BRK dispatcher: multiply X register by 3 with carry, used to scale task ID to table offset
NesPrgRom:3C6D4:palette_upload:If palette_dirty != 0: blank screen, set PPUADDR=$3F00, copy 32 bytes from palette_shadow to PPUDATA, restore rendering, clear palette_dirty
NesPrgRom:3C757:reset_ppu_init:Reset-path PPU init: ppu_safe_gate, then upload $30 bytes from tab_c775 to PPU $0000, then screen_on. Walked 2026-05-31; was the pre-identified reset_ppu_init.
NesPrgRom:3C7A5:music_driver:NMI music tick: jsr music_trigger_pass ($C7AC), jsr music_sequencer_pass ($C817), rts. Entry sits just past the 17-byte data pad tab_b15_c794 ($C794-$C7A4).
NesPrgRom:3C7AC:music_trigger_pass:music_driver pass 1: scan the 5 voices ($0734 + N*9); for each voice whose trigger byte (record+0) is 1-4 (a play request), program its APU channel registers from record bytes 1-4 and mark it played (trigger += 4 -> 5-8). Helpers: music_voice_step_trigger ($C7DE) per voice, music_start_voice ($C7EF) writes the channel. | Pass 1: scan 5 voices at $0734; for any voice with byte 0 in 1..4, write 4 APU register bytes and set byte 0 = byte 0 + 4 (one-shot)
NesPrgRom:3C7C9:music_advance_voice:music_ptr += 9 (advance to next 9-byte voice record); music_voice_idx++. The scan-step shared by trigger_pass and sequencer_pass. | Advance the music scan to the next voice: inc music_voice_idx, music_ptr += 9 (the 9-byte voice-record stride). Shared by both music passes. (also named music_next_voice)
NesPrgRom:3C7DE:music_voice_check:Per-voice trigger check: skip if byte 0 is 0 (idle) or >= 5 (dormant), else call music_voice_play
NesPrgRom:3C7EF:music_voice_play:Per-voice play: compute APU base from byte 0, optionally skip if triangle mute, write bytes 1-4 to APU registers
NesPrgRom:3C817:music_sequencer_pass:music_driver pass 2: scan the 5 voices; for each non-muted voice (audio_mute_triangle[idx]==0) advance its note sequence via music_voice_advance ($C83D). | Pass 2: for each active voice, decrement byte 8 (duration countdown). When zero, advance song pointer (bytes 6-7), load new pitch (bytes 3-4), trigger (byte 0), reset countdown (byte 8).
NesPrgRom:3C83D:music_voice_step:Per-voice sequencer tick (called from music_sequencer_pass for active voices). If stream byte < 5: load note (music_load_note). Else: countdown record[8] via music_dec_duration; on expiry, music_next_event drives the next stream event.
NesPrgRom:3C857:music_load_note:Start a note: music_load_voice_cfg then write 4 note-parameter bytes (from the stream) into record offsets [0,1,2,4] via music_read_stream_byte.
NesPrgRom:3C877:music_load_voice_cfg:Copy the voice's 3-byte instrument config from v0_config[voice_idx*3] ($0725) into record offsets [5,6,7] (bank + stream pointer).
NesPrgRom:3C894:music_read_stream_byte:Banked song-stream fetch: save current bank, switch to record[5] (song bank), read one byte via the record[6,7] pointer, increment that pointer (record[6,7]), restore bank. Returns byte in A. The cross-bank stream reader the whole driver runs on.
NesPrgRom:3C8C4:music_dec_duration:Decrement record[8] (note-duration countdown) and store back. Returns Z when it hits zero (time for next event).
NesPrgRom:3C8CE:music_next_event:Process one stream event: music_read_stream_byte; if < $F0 it's a note -> music_set_pitch + music_set_duration; if >= $F0 it's a command -> music_handle_command. Loops until a playable event is set.
NesPrgRom:3C8E4:music_handle_command:Stream control byte >= $F0. $F0 = note-off (silence the APU channel for this voice, clear its active flag, return C set = stop). Other values fall through to music_restart_stream (pattern loop/restart).
NesPrgRom:3C906:music_restart_stream:Reload the 3-byte voice config into record[5,6,7] and clear record[0] — i.e. restart the voice's pattern stream from its configured start (the loop command target). jmp-reached from music_handle_command.
NesPrgRom:3C929:music_set_pitch:Convert note -> APU timer period via music_note_to_period, then splice the period hi/lo into record[3,4] (the channel's timer bytes), preserving the low control bits of record[4].
NesPrgRom:3C94B:music_note_to_period:Note byte -> 16-bit APU period in $7E/$7F: low nibble indexes the 12-entry base-period table tab_c96f (2 bytes each); high nibble is the octave (right-shift the period that many times).
NesPrgRom:3C990:music_set_duration:Read the next stream byte (note length), shift left 3 (x8 = ticks), store into record[8] (the duration countdown).
NesPrgRom:3CA46:rng_next_wrapper:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Thin wrapper: syscall_rng_next() -- advances and returns the RNG.
NesPrgRom:3CA52:rng_mod:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] rng_mod(n): returns 0 if n<1, else rng_next() mod n = a uniform 0..n-1. THE randomness primitive, 155 callers.
NesPrgRom:3CB5E:min_word:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns min(a, b), SIGNED (gates.value_probe over $8000 / $FFFF, 2026-10-28; the June note said unsigned). Kernel primitive, 29 callers.
NesPrgRom:3CBBD:syscall16_sram_wrap:Thin wrapper around syscall 16 (sram_block_checksum/copy). Called by filter_province_list_by_owner after filtering the candidate list — plumbing, not scoring. Read 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3CBCD:sqrt_int:Integer square root (native code; chapter 9). Classic restoring algorithm, 2 bits per iteration, 8 iterations over 16-bit input. Called as host_call sqrt_int, $02 with one word arg on the data stack. Used by Grow/Dam/Build/Train effects to drive the diminishing-returns curve.
NesPrgRom:3CC35:palette_swap:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] return syscall_palette_swap(arg1) -- 1-op forward to the native palette-swap syscall (body @ $CC3A: PUSH local12; CALL syscall_palette_swap; RETURN). NOT marriage-related: 'palette_swap' was wrong-category (it appears in effect/marriage screens that swap palettes, e.g. palette_swap(1)/palette_swap(0) bracketing palette_write_wrap blocks). 91 call sites.
NesPrgRom:3CC69:clear_rect_right_panel:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] ppu_fill_rect_wrap(22, 7, 29, 18, 1) -- blanks the right-side panel (cols 22-29, rows 7-18) with tile $01. A fixed-geometry clear, sibling of clear_rect_top_strip/left_upper/left_lower. NOT trade-specific (wrong-category). Was 'trade_helper_cc69'.
NesPrgRom:3CC7B:set_cursor:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] set_cursor(col,row): ui_window_col=arg1; ui_cursor_row=arg2 -- 5-op setter (LOADL 12; STORE $7FCD ui_window_col; LOADL 13; STORE $7FCF ui_cursor_row; RETURN @ $CC80). The text-cursor/draw-origin positioning primitive (the 'locate(col,row)' every redraw_window then consumes; axes confirmed by consumers -- $7FCD=col/X line-wrap boundary, $7FCF=row/Y). Was 'ui_helper_cc7b' (TBD); 211 call sites. UI-primitive vocabulary -- chapter 18 section pending once the cluster (cc89/d134/...) is ground.
NesPrgRom:3CC89:open_message_window:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] open_message_window(): ppu_fill_rect_wrap(2, shift?20:22, 19, 25, 1); set_cursor(2, shift?20:22) (body @ $CC8E). Draws the standard bottom message-window rectangle and homes the text cursor to its origin -- the 'open/prepare the message window before printing' primitive (14 callers, command pre-roll). The shift coord (20 vs 22) is picked by ui_msg_col_shift_flag ($7FD1) and lands in set_cursor's ROW arg (see $7FD1 amend). Was 'ui_helper_cc89' (role TBD).
NesPrgRom:3CD20:repaint_screen:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Full-screen repaint + UI-state reset. Bracketed palette_swap(1)..(0); fill_nametable_wrap + fill_attr_wrap (clear scaffolding); then two DIRTY-FLAG-gated reloads: if ui_pending_flag_7fc9 -> rewrite sprite palette entries 7/11/15 + clear flag; if ui_pending_flag_7fc7 -> reload 4 bg palette entries from strategic_map_bg_palette + ppu_upload_block_wrap(strategic_map_chr_tiles) + clear flag. Finally latches+clears selected_record_idx_9e3c, resets ui_input_sel_latch_7fdf=255, set_cursor(2,20), clears ui_state_flag_7bf9 + combat_unit_window_mode_flag. ~18 call sites. Was 'ui_helper_cd20' (TBD); all callees grounded so this is a depth-0 leaf. Consumes the two dirty flags whose producers are noted at $7FC9/$7FC7.
NesPrgRom:3CEC4:redraw_window:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] redraw_window: renders a window/message string at the current UI position. 147 callers -- the core UI draw.
NesPrgRom:3D134:draw_message:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] draw_message(fmt, ...): format_string(&fmt, &msg_buf); return redraw_window(&msg_buf) -- printf-then-draw wrapper (body @ $D139). Formats a printf-style message (with its inline varargs) into the -150 frame msg_buf via format_string ($CFFC, the %C/%D/%S core), then draws the buffer. 193 call sites, all (msg_*_Nd, value) -- the '_2d/_4d' suffixes encode the printf width. AMENDS the old 'draw_message' note (REFUTED: d134 is NOT the substitution layer -- $CFFC is; d134 is the format+draw wrapper around it).
NesPrgRom:3D326:message_display:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] message_display: shows a message string (the 'show feedback' primitive). The single most-used helper, 159 callers.
NesPrgRom:3D351:prompt_ab_window:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] A/B prompt over a caller-supplied window (body @ $D356): redraw_window(arg1); read_frame_timer(1); poll wait_button_edge until A(64)/B(128)/btn(2); read_frame_timer(0); on A echo glyph 60 + return 1, on B echo glyph 62 + return 0, on btn-2 return 2; open_message_window() to restore. Confirms the old 'candidate: 2-choice prompt' note (it's 3-way incl. a cancel/btn-2). Sibling of prompt_y_n ($D3A7) but takes the window arg + has the 3rd exit. 7 sites. Was 'ui_helper_d351'.
NesPrgRom:3D3A7:prompt_y_n:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Y/N confirm prompt: redraw_window(msg_y_n_f695); poll wait_button_edge until A(64)/B(128); on A echo 'Y' (char_advance_width(89)) + return 1, else return 0 (body @ $D3AC). 8 callers. Was 'ui_helper_d3a7' (TBD). Sibling of confirm_prompt ($D766) -- this one draws the explicit 'Y/N' string + echoes the choice.
NesPrgRom:3D3ED:cursor_nav_loop:Menu/cursor navigation loop: switch(sub_D14E()) on NES button bits (1=R,2=L,16=Start,32=Sel,64=B,128=A) to move the selection cursor over candidates. The war-target PICK bottoms out HERE — controller input, not a target-scorer (read 2026-05-31). AI drives the same path via sub_D14E's AI branch.
NesPrgRom:3D59D:select_province_by_cursor:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] select_province_by_cursor(min,max): the number/cursor province picker -- prompts for a value in [min,max] and returns it (the shared selection primitive behind the command prompts).
NesPrgRom:3D5E9:number_input:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] number_input(min,max): the digit-entry prompt; reads a number in [min,max] (or 0/cancel). 27 callers -- every amount prompt.
NesPrgRom:3D6B8:math32_3arg:[HIGH CERTIFIED 2026-06-10] = (arg1*arg2)/arg3 in 32-bit. Oracle-proven. (bug 1.3 ext-op stub.)
NesPrgRom:3D6DE:math32_2arg:[HIGH CERTIFIED 2026-06-10] = (arg1*100)/(arg1+arg2) -- arg1's PERCENTAGE of the (arg1+arg2) total. Oracle CORRECTS the prior 'a*b/c' note (was wrong). (bug 1.3 ext-op stub.)
NesPrgRom:3D70D:pct_op:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Percentage op: returns a*b/100 (a scaled by b percent). The most-used arithmetic helper -- 60 callers across the game.
NesPrgRom:3D759:standard_delay:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] return delay_loop(delay_loop_count) -- 2-op wrapper (PUSH $6D65 delay_loop_count; CALL $D73E delay_loop; RETURN @ $D75E). Runs the standard configurable busy-wait; delay_loop_count ($6D65) is the user-adjustable message-speed setting. 3 callers. Was 'ui_helper_d759'.
NesPrgRom:3D766:confirm_prompt:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] confirm_prompt: shows a prompt and waits for the player to acknowledge. 89 callers.
NesPrgRom:3D772:fief_owner:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] return fief_to_daimyo_map[fief] -- 5-op accessor (LOADL 12 fief; LOADR_imm2 $6E15 fief_to_daimyo_map; ADD; BYTE_DEREF; RETURN @ $D777). Takes a fief id, returns its owning daimyo id. Was 'ui_helper_d772' (low-fidelity: NOT a UI helper, a data accessor; the 'fief->owner' note scattered in other comments is now ground-truthed).
NesPrgRom:3D77E:selected_province_owner:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] return fief_owner(selected_province_idx) -- 2-op accessor (PUSH $6F5F selected_province_idx; CALL $D772 fief_owner; RETURN @ $D783). The owning daimyo id of the currently-selected province. Called by 5 drivers (Marry/Pact diplomacy among them -- act on the selected province's lord). Was 'ui_helper_d77e' (TBD); NOT a UI helper (a data accessor, like fief_owner).
NesPrgRom:3D7EA:selected_province_daimyo_record:[CONFIRMED 2026-06-02] Returns fief_to_daimyo_record_addr(selected_province_idx) — the ACTIVE/attacker daimyo's 7-byte record. Used by ai_sum_battle_strength as the attacker side of the daimyo-stat comparison (vs the defending province's record); also 4 other drivers. (was selected_province_daimyo_record.)
NesPrgRom:3D836:cap_fief_stats:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] cap_fief_stats(fief): caps every field of the $7001 province record (offsets +0..+22) at the record's +24 cap field via min_word. Confirms $7001+24 = the per-fief stat CAP/header.
NesPrgRom:3D972:fief_owner_weakness:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Accessor: return daimyo_weakness_flag[fief_owner(arg1)] (body @ $D977) -- the weakness/condition mark of the fief's owning daimyo. Data accessor, NOT a 'war helper' (wrong-category, like fief_owner/selected_province_owner); built on the grounded fief_owner leaf. 9 sites. Semantic of daimyo_weakness_flag itself still inherited from its var label.
NesPrgRom:3D999:province_state_is_FF:Returns ($6CF7[arg1] == 0xFF) — province is in the EXCLUDED state. Eligibility filter used by filter_province_list_by_owner. Read 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3D9B7:is_enemy_owned:Candidate target predicate: returns (fief_to_daimyo_map[selected_province_owner()] == arg) — i.e. the candidate fief's owner matches the target daimyo (enemy-ownership match). Eligibility, not strength. Read 2026-05-31.
NesPrgRom:3DA4F:set_pact_relation:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Sets the relations_matrix ($6193 stride-54) cell between selected_province_idx and battle_defending_province to 70 -- establishing a non-aggression pact. (was diplomacy_helper2.)
NesPrgRom:3DA7D:set_marriage_relation:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Sets the relations_matrix ($6193) cell between the two daimyo (selected_province_owner / fief_owner(defender)) to 90 -- the marriage alliance bond. (was diplomacy_helper3.)
NesPrgRom:3DAD7:compact_relation_list:[MED 2026-06-10] load_daimyo_relation_row(selected_province_idx) into the $6F4F buffer, then compact it in place: keep only entries whose province still exists (get_province_ai_state != 255), FF-terminate. Builds the active-daimyo relation list. NOT a 'combat pre-roll' (wrong-category). Was 'combat_helper_dad7'.
NesPrgRom:3DB12:defender_owner_is_keyed_daimyo:[MED PROBABLE 2026-06-10] Combat predicate (NOT tax -- wrong-category): return fief_owner(battle_defending_province) == (scenario_fief_count==17 ? 3 : 20). I.e. is the defending province owned by the scenario's keyed daimyo (index 3 in the 17-fief scenario, 20 in the 50-fief). OPEN: confirm who daimyo 3/20 is (likely the scenario protagonist/Nobunaga) via the daimyo table. Was 'tax_helper_db12'.
NesPrgRom:3DB35:increment_ai_player_count:[MED 2026-06-10] ai_player_count++; if (is_ai_count_ge_8()) set_6da1_bit7(). Bumps the daimyo/AI count and sets the $6DA1 bit-7 flag once it reaches 8 (the >=8 threshold). NOT a UI helper (wrong-category). Was 'ui_helper_db35'.
NesPrgRom:3DD3A:filter_province_list_by_owner:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] In-place filter of a province-id list: walks out_list (FF-terminated), keeps each province whose is_enemy_owned(p) matches arg1 (match_enemy) AND that still exists (!province_state_is_FF), into a scratch buf, FF-terminates, then writes buf back over out_list (syscall16_sram_wrap bank 0). NOT a 'combat pre-roll' (wrong-category) -- a list-prune by ownership. Was 'combat_helper_dd3a'.
NesPrgRom:3E315:marriage_pact_handler:[MED 2026-06-10] Marriage-pact logic, two paths on whether battle_defending_province has an owner. OWNED (interactive): set ui_input_mode=2, draw_daimyo_name_menu(msg_marriage_pact) + redraw_window(msg_accept) + prompt_y_n; on yes, demand gold via number_input(1..9999); returns the entered amount (0 on decline). UNOWNED (auto/AI): 50% gate (rng_mod 2), then weakness/rng test (fief_owner_weakness(selected) or rng_mod(3)); if the province's $7001 stat > 200 returns pct_op(stat, rng_mod(30)+50)+200, else 0. Was 'marry_helper_e315'.
NesPrgRom:3E3A4:prompt_diplomacy_pact:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Pact negotiation prompt: if the defender is AI, draws the pact menu (draw_daimyo_name_menu(msg_pact)), demands gold (number_input up to 9999), and runs the accept/reject flow. The diplomacy negotiation UI. (was diplomacy_helper.)
NesPrgRom:3E4DC:build_fiefs_excluding_daimyo:[MED 2026-06-10] build_owned_fief_list() into $6F89, then compact it in place keeping only fiefs whose owner (fief_owner) != arg1 -- the owned fiefs NOT held by daimyo arg1. Used in the marriage flow (candidate target list excluding a given daimyo's holdings). Was 'marry_helper_e4dc'.
NesPrgRom:3E510:build_eligible_province_list:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] build_eligible_province_list(enemy_flag): scans all fiefs [0, scenario_fief_count); keeps those that EXIST (!province_state_is_FF), match the ownership filter (is_enemy_owned(i) == enemy_flag), and are NOT selected_province_idx; appends each idx to the $6F89 buffer, FF-terminates it, returns the count (body @ $E515). The candidate-list BUILDER the Send/Pact/View/Marry target-select commands then pick from (confirms the prior caller note -- it builds the list, isn't a 'cursor/menu enter primitive').
NesPrgRom:3E5F2:render_map_section:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] The strategic-map SECTION renderer. If arg1 != the current section: palette_swap(1); clear the right margin (ppu_fill_rect 30,4..31,19); ppu_copy_rect the section's 28x16 tilemap (strategic_map_section_tilemaps + arg1*0x1C0, bank 4) to cols 2-29 rows 4-19; ppu_upload_block the section's 32-byte attribute table (strategic_map_section_attributes + arg1*32 -> PPU $23C8); mark selected_record_idx_9e3c=arg1; then walk the section's 34-byte record list and draw every fief's lord name (draw_province_lord_name); palette_swap(0). A 'map section' = tilemap(0x1C0) + attributes(32) + fief records(34). 8 sites. Was 'map_helper_e5f2'. The graphics-thread keystone; see ch.16/19.
NesPrgRom:3E76F:draw_daimyo_portrait:[HIGH 2026-06-01] Draws the daimyo portrait (stat-roll/info screens; caller sets active_province_idx_copy $6F5B first). Loads a 4-entry palette, then BRANCHES on the daimyo record's status/generated flag (record[+6], the 7th byte of daimyo_table_17): flag==0 (an ORIGINAL scenario daimyo) -> PRESET path: descriptor table at $BBD0 (graphics bank, NOT the string bank the decompiler resolves it to) indexed by fief_to_mapid*4, read 8 bytes, upload that daimyo's DEDICATED portrait CHR to $15B0; flag==1 (a GENERATED/replacement daimyo) -> COMPOSITE path: unpack_composite_face_record builds the base-5 face from $6EB1. Then blits the 8x8 portrait. THIS is why the original 50 have fixed faces (preset) while death-replacements get random composite faces. (was the mislabeled 'draw_daimyo_portrait'.)
NesPrgRom:3E80C:trigger_cutscene:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] If the AI-turn cutscene flag is set (ai_turn_flags & 4): store the cutscene id (arg1) into cutscene_id ($7FCB), then run the bank-14 cutscene engine via call_bank_wrap(14) -> run_cutscene ($80AD); else return 0. ~34 sites. Was 'ui_helper_e80c' (TBD) -- the long-open bank-14 cross-bank case, now resolved by folding bank 14 into the corpus (ch.19). (Its call was the one made unconditional by the return_phi bug, fixed f50d874.)
NesPrgRom:3F7D4:governance_policy_name_ptrs:[ROM-DATA 2026-06-10] Word-ptrs to the AI governance-policy names: Home fief/Industrial/Military/Balanced/Farming/Direct (driver_grant). (was grant_menu_str_ptrs.)
NesPrgRom:3F816:lord_command_name_ptrs:[ROM-DATA 2026-06-10] Word-ptrs to the 14 lord-command names: Move/War/Tax/Send/Dam/Pact/Grow/Marry/Trade/Hire/Train/View/Build/Give. REFUTES the prior fief_stat_label name -- these are COMMAND names (its reader fief_info_display draws the command menu).
NesPrgRom:3F8AE:fief_stat_name_ptrs:[ROM-DATA 2026-06-10] Word-ptrs to fief/daimyo stat names: Age/Hlth/Driv/Luck/Char/IQ (daimyo record +0..+5) then Gold/Debt/Town/Rice/Output/Dams/Lylty/Wealth (province record).
