NesPrgRom:0000:bank0_entry:Bank 0 entry point. 3 bytes: JMP $A778. The 'rest of bank 0' is data — VM bytecode, sprite/tile data, and a few small native helpers callable from bytecode.
NesPrgRom:2778:vm_bootstrap:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] THE game entry point and main loop (the first sub the VM runs after RESET / JSR vm_entry $E823) -- the ROOT of the entire corpus. Outer loop: init_new_game_state, then per turn: ai_strategic_turn_planner; when it signals a pending battle (ai_turn_planner_resume_flag==1) stage the defender and call_bank_wrap(2) to dispatch into bank 2 (combat), then re-plan; loops until ai_turn_flags bit7 (game over). Dispatches into bank 1 (commands) + bank 2 (combat); banks 1/2 are the engines, bank 0 the main loop.
NesPrgRom:0003:display_fullscreen_graphic_sequence:[MED AMENDED] ~530-byte multi-phase full-screen graphic/cinematic presenter: PPU blob uploads (ppu_upload_block_wrap) + 4 palette-fade loops + input-gated phase transitions + audio; ends two conditional message_display + infinite-hang JUMP. Proposer's cited calls were fabricated/mis-tiled; corrected from bytecode.
NesPrgRom:021E:verify_sram_save_integrity:[MED CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] load-game gate: strcmp magic-string vs $7FED + running-sum checksum over $6001-$7FFF compared to stored $7FEB; match -> continue (ret 1), mismatch -> rewrite signature/flags + reformat prompt. Caller $89C9 (load path, $89A3).
NesPrgRom:0377:transfer_arms_field_pct:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] moves arg3% of source byte field (*arg2) into dest field (*arg1) via pct_op; caller $839A specializes it on the $76A9 per-fief arms record (stride 5).
NesPrgRom:05FC:prompt_roll_stat_value:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] rolls a stat = rng_mod(50)+60 (60-109) with a roll/keep input loop; caller $8763 rolls the 5 daimyo stats.
NesPrgRom:062B:prompt_select_scenario_size:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] 17-vs-50 fief scenario-size prompt; sets scenario_fief_count $6D9D = 17 or 50 + the map pointer, then SRAM init via syscall16_sram_wrap.
NesPrgRom:067F:prompt_player_choose_fief:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] message_display(msg_player) + draw_message(msg_d_which_fief_would_you_like_to, arg1) -- the new-game 'Player N, which fief would you like to start in' prompt. arg1 = player number. (was msg_d_which_fief_would_you_like_to.)
NesPrgRom:08AC:render_boot_title_screens:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] boot/title two-screen opening (nametable+attr+tile blits, palette loops, press-A continue); reached only from vm_bootstrap via $89A3. NOT the Marry screen - cc35 is a generic screen enter/exit primitive (20 callers).
NesPrgRom:0B70:select_rebellion_message:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Selects the uprising message by the $7B79 state byte: byte[arg1+$7B79]==7 -> msg_christns (Christian/ikko uprising) else msg_rioters. (was select_msg_by_state_7b79.)
NesPrgRom:0B9D:select_message_string_by_flags_and_arg:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] picks a $BA-region message string by $6DA1 flag bits, then a 4-key switch on arg, default delegates to select_msg_by_state_7b79; feeds message_display.
NesPrgRom:0BE6:find_first_enemy_owned_fief:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] scans the FF-terminated owned-fief list ($6F89) and returns the first fief INDEX where is_enemy_owned; returns a province index, not an owner id.
NesPrgRom:0C0E:is_selected_province_ai_state_5:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] pure predicate: province_ai_state[$6CF7][selected_province_idx $6F5F] == 5.
NesPrgRom:0C35:relations_matrix_cell_addr:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] &relations[arg1][arg2] = arg1*54 + arg2 + $6193 (relations-matrix base, row stride 54; sibling of relations_matrix_get $8250).
NesPrgRom:0DE1:dedup_owners:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Reads the 0xFF-terminated fief list arg1 and builds a de-duplicated-by-OWNER list into the $6F4F dedup buffer (skips a fief whose fief_owner already appears). (was dedup_owners_to_6f4f.)
NesPrgRom:0E99:append_candidate_pair:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Appends a 2-byte (value=arg1, flag=arg3) record at index arg2 into the $6F67/$6F68 dual-lane candidate list, then rewrites the 0xFF terminator at index arg2+1; callers push flag 0 / 1. (was append_candidate_entry_6f67.)
NesPrgRom:0EBC:compare_greater_with_coinflip_tiebreak:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] returns (arg_a > arg_b) signed (SCMPLT); on equal returns a 50/50 rng_mod(2) coinflip.
NesPrgRom:0FE0:stat_above_threshold_and_gap_predicate:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] returns 1 iff (hi > 25) AND (hi - lo > 5); an absolute-threshold(25) + gap(5) test (not a truncation).
NesPrgRom:10C6:reset_byte_if_ge_100:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] if *ptr >= 100 then *ptr = 0 (carry/wrap of a 0-99 stat, NOT a clamp-to-100); wrapper $90D7 = bump-then-wrap.
NesPrgRom:1154:check_daimyo_natural_death:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] the VERIFIED natural-death formula: gated age>=70, triggers when (age-10-health/4) < rng_mod(300); returns weakness_flag[$6DD4]+1 on death, 2 if health==0. Caller $9194 runs the death-removal path.
NesPrgRom:11FD:clamp_value_to_range:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] clamp arg2 to [arg1, arg3] (median-of-three); pure arithmetic.
NesPrgRom:1214:calc_year_scaled_random_value:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] ((year $6D9F - 1560)/2 + 2)*10 + rng_mod(51); deterministic part grows +5/year, plus 0-50 noise.
NesPrgRom:122E:roll_small_or_large_random:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] coinflip rng_mod(2) selects a small roll (5-10) vs a large roll (30-39); bimodal RNG helper.
NesPrgRom:039A:init_daimyo_arms_record:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] makes FOUR transfer_arms_field_pct ($8377) calls over one daimyo arms record (idx*5+$76A9): two fixed 30% + two randomized rng_mod(20)+20 (20-39%) transfers of reserve fields +3/+4 into active +0/+1. Caller $858F inside the per-daimyo difficulty-scaling init loop $8507-$8593. Proposer undercounted (1 transfer); domain correct.
NesPrgRom:03E2:apply_scenario_starting_stat_boosts:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] outer loop over scenario_fief_count: per non-AI fief, on a fief-id whitelist (50-fief {5,9,13,14,19,23,26,21,38,42,49,24} / 17-fief {1,2,4,7,10,15,16}) AND rng_mod(2), multiplies province record fields gold*2/men*4(or*3 17-fief)/+12*2/+18*2/+16*2; then pct-scales header(+24) by rng_mod(20)+80 for every fief. Scenario-init stat boosts. Opcode-exact.
NesPrgRom:0694:prompt_select_player_daimyo:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] setup-time daimyo-selection prompt (called per player slot from $8AB3): reads number_input, validates province_ai_state[$6CF7]==5 (available marker), displays chosen daimyo name ($77A8), commits by WRITING ai_state=5 + selected_province_idx $6F5F. Verifier corrected proposer/decompiler (gate is ==5 and commit writes 5, not 0).
NesPrgRom:0763:daimyo_creation_stat_roll_screen:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] full daimyo creation/edit screen ($8768-$88AB): palette/rect chrome, name draw ($77A8), field values ($7985), label loop over $F8AE; interactive climax = roll 6 stats into daimyo record (idx*7+$7530) via prompt_roll_stat_value ($85FC) with confirm/reroll-all (prompt_y_n). Proposer name too narrow (just the roll).
NesPrgRom:09A3:init_new_game_state:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] top-level new-game/scenario init: gated on verify_sram_save_integrity ($821E, bails via syscall on fail); fills $7FD5[0..8)=-1, $6F1B[i]=i per fief, zeroes $6CF7 province_ai_state over fiefs+4 daimyo slots, seeds $6E0B[i]=rng_mod(10)+8; drives scenario-size prompt + per-player init ($8694/$8763) + render_boot_title_screens. 18+ CALLs; call-index 0-edge artifact.
NesPrgRom:0C1E:cur_flag_and_selected_ai_state5:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] predicate: returns get_6da2_cur ($D9A9) AND is_selected_province_ai_state_5 ($8C0E) as 1/0. Verifier corrected proposer prose (true path returns 1 not 0 - decompiler drops the LOADL accumulator across labels). Caller $8C45 scans fiefs for cur-flag AND ai_state==5.
NesPrgRom:0C45:flag_turn_abort_if_no_state5_province:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Scans all fiefs (via $6F1A turn-order) for any in ai_state 5 (actable); if NONE found, sets ai_turn_flags ($6DA1) bit 7 (the turn-abort / game-over gate). (was set_6da1_bit7_if_no_ai_state5_province_found.)
NesPrgRom:0C75:resolve_ownerless_province_succession:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] picks who inherits a vacated province: if <2 candidates install_new_daimyo($6F63); else walk the $00FF-terminated candidate list at $6F4F, pick max province-value daimyo, install + mutate ai-state ($6CF7/$6DA2/$6E15) + name table $77A8. Sole caller $8E63. Proposer had the max-value mechanic; succession is the right frame.
NesPrgRom:0E63:process_fiefs_with_state_ff:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] loops all fiefs; for each ownerless one (province_state_is_FF $D999), builds the deduped owners list (dedup_owners_to_6F4F $8DE1) and calls resolve_ownerless_province_succession ($8C75). Action loop, NOT a finder (proposer mistook the trailing decompiler RETURN for a found-index).
NesPrgRom:0ED3:display_two_message_prompt_then_compare:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] selects two message strings ($DE78/$8B9D), renders a formatted two-message prompt + confirm (message_display + draw_message x2 + confirm_prompt), then RETURNS compare_greater_with_coinflip_tiebreak ($8EBC) of two PASSED-IN args (slots 12/13), not the message values. Proposer conflated the displayed strings with the compared values.
NesPrgRom:0F0A:ai_resolve_province_takeover_attempt:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] contest on a target province: strength = sqrt(output+8)+sqrt(arms+14)+rng_mod(20)+10 vs defender field+16, decided by the $8ED3 UI contest. WIN ($8F51) -> conquer (install_new_daimyo/neutralize_fief + list ops); LOSS ($8F96) -> erode arms+16/output+8 by pct rng_mod(50)+10. Proposer only documented the loss branch.
NesPrgRom:0FD3:append_candidate_zero_priority:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] thin wrapper: append_candidate_entry_6f67 ($8E99) with priority/score field = 0. PUSH 0/13/12 -> CALL $8E99. No other logic.
NesPrgRom:0FF8:collect_high_loyalty_provinces_to_candidate_list:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] walks province-index list $7BAD; for AI-owned fiefs (via $8C1E) qualifies on field+12 LOYALTY (verifier corrected proposer +12=men): loyalty>25 AND (loyalty-arg1)>5, appending via $8FD3. Interactive (message/redraw/confirm) + applies a loyalty/wealth grow ($D940). Non-AI branch bumps +12 by rng_mod(30)+50.
NesPrgRom:10D7:saturating_sub_byte_then_reset_if_ge_100:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] *ptr(local12) = max(0, *ptr - local13) via $CA12, THEN reset_byte_if_ge_100 ($90C6) clamps to 0 if >=100. NOT a thin wrapper (proposer missed the $CA12 saturating-sub the lossy C renders as ?). Called from the relations-matrix decay loops $90E8/$911E (decay-by-N across fief pairs).
NesPrgRom:10E8:normalize_relations_matrix_lower:[MED CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] nested i/j loop bounded by scenario_fief_count, gated j>i (lower triangle): cell = relations_matrix_cell_addr ($8C35, arg1*54+arg2+$6193), apply $90D7 (bump-then-wrap-at-100). 4 callers in the AI turn region ($9F9C/$A06C/$A275/$A392). Per-cell op is bump+wrap not pure clamp (MED).
NesPrgRom:111E:normalize_relations_matrix_upper:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] byte-identical to sibling $90E8 except the two index pushes are swapped (cell i*54+j vs j*54+i) = the transposed/other triangle of the stride-54 relations matrix at $6193. Gated i<j, apply $90D7 per cell.
NesPrgRom:1194:check_and_process_daimyo_natural_death:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] per-daimyo (gated on $6DA2 active set): runs check_daimyo_natural_death ($9154, the verified (age-10-health/4)/300 age>=70 roll); on death removes from list ($DC0E/$DC3C), announces via name table $77A8 + death-type table $BBA5, clears fief pairs ($E1E7), reassigns territory (find_fiefs_of_owner $E425). Natural-death + succession handler. Called per-daimyo by an outer turn iterator.
NesPrgRom:124A:roll_period_market_rates:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Rolls the per-period market rate table ($6E0B): loan_rate (rng 1-10), gold_rice_exchange_rate (clamped 10-30 drift, or roll_small_or_large), arms_buy_price_rate (year-scaled/2), gold_men_hire_rate (70% of year-scaled), hire_gold_rate (year-scaled). (was roll_period_rate_table_6e0b.)
NesPrgRom:12A9:repay_province_debt_from_gold:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] amt = min(debt@+2, gold@+0, cap arg2); gold -= amt; debt -= amt; early-return 1 if no debt. Field +0=gold/+2=debt match live $7001 record (loan/debt mechanic). Caller $A2C5 sweeps every fief paying down debt (with cap_fief_stats $D836).
NesPrgRom:12D9:deduct_b_from_a_void_b_if_overdrawn:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] *A(local12) -= *B(local13); if *A<=0 going in OR *A<0 after, zeroes *B (the source/charge), leaving *A negative. Verifier REFUTED the 'clamp_negative' framing (A is never clamped; B gets voided on overdraft). Leaf, no host_calls.
NesPrgRom:12F9:random_ravage_province_field:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] generic probabilistic field reducer: 50% no-op (rng_mod 2), else *field = pct_op(rng_mod(30)+40, *field) (40-69% of original), returns 1/0. Built into the defending-province ravage sweep: 6 field wrappers ($9323..$93AA over $6F63 record) + orchestrator $93BF. Decompiler C lossy here; bytecode authoritative.
NesPrgRom:1323:ravage_defender_field_off10:[HIGH CONFIRMED] wrapper: random_ravage_province_field on battle_defending_province ($6F63) record field +10 ($700B). 1st call in the $93BF ravage sweep.
NesPrgRom:1338:ravage_defender_output_and_bump_selected_arms:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] ravages defender output@+8 ($7009); on a fire, also adds rng_mod(100)+100 to the ATTACKER (selected_province_idx) arms@+14 ($700F). The plunder-transfer member of the $93BF sweep.
NesPrgRom:136B:ravage_defender_town:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] random_ravage_province_field on battle_defending_province record +4 ($7005 = TOWN). (was ravage_defender_field_off4.)
NesPrgRom:1380:ravage_defender_wealth:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] random_ravage_province_field on battle_defending_province record +14 ($700F = WEALTH). REFUTES the old name 'ravage_defender_arms' -- $700F is wealth (arms is +22/$7017).
NesPrgRom:1395:ravage_defender_morale:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] random_ravage_province_field on battle_defending_province record +18 ($7013 = MORALE). (was ravage_defender_field_off18.)
NesPrgRom:13AA:ravage_defender_loyalty:[HIGH CONFIRMED] wrapper: random_ravage_province_field on defender ($6F63) loyalty@+12 ($700D). Member of the $93BF sweep.
NesPrgRom:13BF:ravage_defending_province_sweep:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] post-combat pillage: opens UI over the loser (message/daimyo-name/confirm), then calls the 6 single-field ravage wrappers ($9323/$936B/$93AA/$9395/$9380/$9338, offsets +10/+4/+12/+18/+14/+8) in sequence, early-out on first fire; fallthrough harsher-ravages field+10 (rng_mod(30)+60) or scribbles the daimyo record if already razed. Sole caller driver_war.
NesPrgRom:146D:get_fief_daimyo_charisma:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns *(byte*)(fief_to_daimyo_record_addr(arg1)+4) = the owning daimyo's CHARISMA (daimyo record +4). (was get_daimyo_stat4_by_fief; +4 = charisma per the daimyo field map.)
NesPrgRom:147A:avg_daimyo_charisma_over_fief_list:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] populates the $00FF-terminated $6F89 list (marry_helper $E4DC), then averages get_daimyo_stat4_by_fief (=owner CHARISMA@+4) over it = sum/count. The marriage subsystem averaging owner charisma across candidate fiefs. Proposer's generic stat4 -> charisma.
NesPrgRom:14B1:announce_seasonal_event:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Announces a seasonal event by arg1: 1 -> summer typhoon, 2 -> plague, etc. (message_display + confirm_prompt per case). REFUTES the old 'by_ai_state_mode' framing -- arg1 is the event id, not an AI state. (was announce_provinces_by_ai_state_mode.)
NesPrgRom:152F:avg_fief_tax_rate:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Sums fief_tax_rate ($6D2D) across all active fiefs and divides by scenario_fief_count -- the average tax rate. (was avg_byte_array_6d2d_over_fiefs.)
NesPrgRom:1558:avg_province_wealth_over_fiefs:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] split-mean (UDIV+UMOD) of province field +14 ($700F) over all fiefs = floor(sum/count). Field +14 = WEALTH (proposer said arms; 3 field-map sources - dashboard.lua/sram-decode-province.py/vm_decompile.py - agree +14=wealth, +22=arms).
NesPrgRom:1595:province_conquest_roll_predicate:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] displays + computes a weighted random score from province field+18, field+16, and random daimyo charisma(+4) terms; returns TRUE when 2*score < field+16 (via SCMPLT, coinflip on tie). Single caller $97B2 gates daimyo-elimination/conquest on TRUE. Proposer mechanism right; 'below_threshold' imprecise (test is 2*score<field16).
NesPrgRom:1614:append_candidate_priority1:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] priority-1 counterpart of $8FD3: append_candidate_entry_6f67 ($8E99) with the priority/flag field = 1 (vs 0). Thin wrapper.
NesPrgRom:1621:reassign_daimyo24_fiefs_to_owner50:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] loops fiefs; for each owned by daimyo 24 with $6DA2 flag clear, sets fief_to_daimyo_map ($6E15) = 50 + refreshes via find_record_9e3c ($E554); then zeroes province_ai_state[selected], sets $6DA1 bit, UI. Byte-symmetric mirror of $99AB (owner 50->24). A scripted 50-fief reassignment event; literal owner-IDs (proposer's 'zealot' unsupported by bytecode).
NesPrgRom:16B0:scenario50_fief30_event_eligible:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] eligibility predicate for a scripted 50-fief event: hard-gates scenario_fief_count==50 AND fief==30 AND owner==24 AND daimyo-record(30) >= 40 (proposer had <=40, direction inverted) AND flags clear; then a combat-strength accumulation ($6F81 vs $270F cap) + RNG roll; on full pass triggers $9621 + sets $6E48=1, returns 1. 'zealot/uprising' semantics dropped (no bytecode support).
NesPrgRom:1778:revolt_spread_sweep_flip_fief_ownership:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] walks the $00FF-terminated $7BAD fief list; per fief: $96B0 true aborts the sweep; $8C1E true counts/collects via $9614; else $9595 spread predicate -> on TRUE flips fief ownership + install_new_daimyo ($E21B) + zero ai_state (defection), on FALSE grows field+18 / decays field+16 (rebellion-pressure meter). Confirmed ownership-flip; 'zealot' dropped (no religion marker, message-string IDs undecodable here).
NesPrgRom:1879:mark_fief_list_entry_removed:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Scans the $6F89 fief list for an entry == arg1 and marks it removed (sets it to 200, the off-list sentinel). (was mark_6f89_list_entry_by_value.)
NesPrgRom:18A3:set_fief_ownership_record:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] canonical parameterized fief-ownership writer: by index arg, stores fief_to_daimyo_map[$6E15]=owner, $6DA2[]=flag, province_ai_state[$6CF7]=ai_state, then find_record_9e3c ($E554) to recompute. Real callers $9963/$9996 (grep; call-index misses CALL_abs_imm1). Sibling idiom of install_new_daimyo/neutralize_fief/reassign_fiefs_to_conqueror.
NesPrgRom:18C6:select_provinces_and_assign_ai_state:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] 3 phases: walk $6F4F candidate list into a stack buffer (marking matched $6F89 entries 0xC8 via $9879); append more from arg2's list; then for each buffered entry COMMIT via set_fief_ownership_record ($98A3) with ai_state preserved + role constant 51. Proposer captured only the list-build phases, missed the consequential state-mutation phase 3.
NesPrgRom:1974:process_first_n_unmarked_list_entries:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] iterate the byte-list (cursor arg) for N (arg) entries: stop on $00FF, skip 0xC8-marked; for each unmarked entry CALL set_fief_ownership_record ($98A3) THEN mark it 0xC8 + decrement remaining. The $98A3 record-processing is the work; 0xC8 is a 'done' marker (proposer's 'mark' undersold it).
NesPrgRom:19AB:reassign_owner50_fiefs_to_daimyo24:[MED CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] byte-symmetric mirror of $9621: loops fiefs, where owner==50 sets fief_to_daimyo_map ($6E15)=24 + find_record_9e3c ($E554); two-path event handler (Path B sets selected=+30, runs $98C6/$9974, sweeps $7FD5 24->51). Verifier corrected: ai_state set to 5 not 0 (decompiler mis-renders the qimm).
NesPrgRom:1AAC:driver_diplomacy_gold_transfer:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] diplomacy effect: gated on diplomacy_helper ($E3A4) + confirm; inputs amount, then selected-province gold@+0 += amount and battle_defending_province gold@+0 -= amount (gold moves target->self). Sibling of the marry variant $9B7F. Caller $9B55 in $9B12.
NesPrgRom:1B12:ai_scan_idle_fiefs_run_diplomacy_action:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] scans fiefs (flag $6DA2 set AND ai_state==0 idle), builds a candidate list via compact_relation_list ($DAD7), and on the first eligible target DISPATCHES the diplomacy action $9AAC (not just a finder, per proposer). Sequential-scan twin of the random-pick $9BE5.
NesPrgRom:1B7F:marry_transfer_gold_between_provinces:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] marriage gold transfer: gated on marriage_pact_handler ($E315); selected-province gold@+0 += amt, battle_defending_province gold@+0 -= amt (target->self). Byte-mirror of diplomacy $9AAC. Leaf effect inside the marriage loop (caller $9BE5), NOT a driver (the Marry driver is $9DC4); dropped the driver_ prefix.
NesPrgRom:1BE5:ai_event_marry_random_eligible_fief:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] picks a random fief (rng_mod scenario_fief_count), skips ai-state-set or rest-blocked fiefs, sets it as battle_defending_province and INVOKES the marriage action $9B7F on the first eligible candidate. Random-pick variant of $9B12. Reached from $9C84 switch branch 0.
NesPrgRom:1C22:random_ravage_sweep_bounded_fiefs:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] 50%-gated sweep over fiefs (rng_mod(20)<3 ~15% per fief, skip ai-state-set, action count bounded by 8-$6E09): on a hit swaps selected<->defending and runs ravage_defending_province_sweep ($93BF). Loop bound is $6D9D not $6E09 (proposer wrong). $9C84 switch default branch.
NesPrgRom:1C84:random_event_type_dispatch:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] 50%-gated (rng_mod 2) random-event selector: rng_mod(4) switch dispatching one of three event handlers ($9BE5 marriage / $9B12 diplomacy / $9C22 ravage), each a distinct CALL+RETURN. Verifier REFUTED the lossy-C 'all converge to $9BE5' artifact (coincident JUMP targets hid the other two CALLs). Pure dispatcher.
NesPrgRom:1CB3:decay_fief_list_wealth_and_output_disaster1:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] AI disaster effect handler #1: over the $7BAD fief list, wealth@+14 -= rng_mod(4)+1 and output@+8 = pct_op(pct_op(90, +10 header), output). Planner-selected (pointer loaded at $A4DA in the $A4AB planner, type 1 of 3 vs $9D00/$9ED9). Proposer's mechanics right; 'sabotage' too specific -> disaster type 1.
NesPrgRom:1D00:random_event_ravage_output_hidden_mark_weakness:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] disaster effect handler #2 (msg #31): over the $7BAD list, hidden field+16 and output+8 each scaled to 50-99% (pct_op rng_mod(50)+50); conditionally writes daimyo_weakness_flag $6DD4[owner] from a daimyo-record byte vs 50, plus a deduct_byte_at side-write. Planner-selected (pointer at $A4F0). Proposer missed the $6DD4 weakness write.
NesPrgRom:1D86:square_over_2025_probability_roll:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] clamps arg1<=50, returns (arg1*arg1) < rng_mod(2025) = the verified event-spawn probability x^2/2025 capped at 50 (rediscovered blind from bytecode; matches event_spawn_formula memory). Pure predicate. Used by $9DA3/$9E21 as per-stat eligibility rolls.
NesPrgRom:1DA3:ai_event_eligibility_check_loyalty_variant:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] per-fief event-eligibility predicate: three $9D86 (x^2/2025) rolls on loyalty@+12 ($700D), (100 - $6D2D[fief]), and daimyo charisma@+4; any TRUE -> gate block (output>0, +16>2, !defender_owner_is_keyed_daimyo, !state_FF, rng_mod(4)==0) -> return 1. Loyalty variant; sibling $9E21 keys on +18. Dispatched by $9E7C (arg1==1).
NesPrgRom:1E21:ai_event_eligibility_check_morale_variant:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI event (uprising) eligibility, morale variant: square_over_2025 rolls on morale ($7013/+18) or the owner's charisma, gated on men>2 and not-already-FF; sets battle_defending_province=fief. (was ..._field18_variant; field18 = $7013 morale.)
NesPrgRom:1E7C:select_event_eligibility_check_by_type:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] dispatcher: returns 0 if province_state_is_FF; else arg1==1 -> $9DA3 (loyalty variant) else $9E21 (+18 variant). Caller $9E9D sweeps fiefs calling this per-fief.
NesPrgRom:1E9D:build_event_eligible_fief_candidate_list:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] scans all scenario fiefs (source list $6F1B), filters by per-type eligibility ($9E7C), appends survivors to the $00FF-terminated candidate list at $7BAD, returns any-found flag. Caller $9ED9 (event-handler driver). Proposer swapped the in/out list bases (corrected).
NesPrgRom:1ED9:ai_event_build_two_batches_dispatch_or_announce:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] disaster/event handler type-3 (pointer-selected at $A4FA in the planner): builds 2 eligible-fief batches ($9E9D for both event types); if BOTH eligible -> random_event_type_dispatch ($9C84); else FALLBACK switch fires a UI-announced event ($8FF8 loyalty-grow or $9778 revolt). Sibling of $9CB3/$9D00.
NesPrgRom:1F57:event_boost_province_wealth_loyalty:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] 50%-gated positive event: arg2-province WEALTH@+14 += rng_mod(10)+charisma/10, LOYALTY@+12 += rng_mod(40)+charisma/10 (charisma via get_daimyo_stat4_by_fief). Per-turn sweep caller $9FE5 in $9F8C. Sibling of the gold/output variant $A128.
NesPrgRom:1F8C:per_turn_age_daimyo_decay_health_and_province_stats:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] per-period driver (turn-dispatch case0 from $A30D switch): normalizes relations matrix, then per daimyo record AGE@+0 ++ and HEALTH@+1 -- (7-byte stride; fields per verified $9154 natural-death), then per AI-province decays loyalty@+12/wealth@+14/hidden@+16. Proposer's 'decrement_debt' REFUTED (it's health+stat decay, no debt touched).
NesPrgRom:2066:init_province_highwater_from_records:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] per fief, copies 4 words from province record +8/+10/+12/+14 (output/dams/loyalty/wealth) into the stride-8 fief_history_table ($6003). Plain snapshot/init; sibling $A0A9 does the max-UPDATE. The documented high-water-mark mechanic.
NesPrgRom:20A9:update_province_highwater_marks:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] monotonic high-water update: for province fields +8/+10/+12/+14, if field >= stored table value ($6003/$6005/$6007/$6009 stride-8) store field. Pure leaf, paired with the $A066 initializer.
NesPrgRom:2128:event_boost_province_gold_output:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] positive event: arg2-province GOLD@+0 += rng_mod(10)+charisma/10 unconditionally, then 50%-gated OUTPUT@+8 += same. Caller $A295 in $A26F, only for non-owned provinces. Gold/output sibling of the wealth/loyalty variant $9F57.
NesPrgRom:215B:consume_province_army_upkeep:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] army upkeep: drains MEN@+16 /2 from BOTH gold@+0 and rice@+6; if min(rice,gold) < men/2, starves the army down to 2*available (men = avail<<1). The '-MEN/2' term of the harvest formula. Drains gold too, not just rice (proposer's 'food' -> 'upkeep').
NesPrgRom:2191:calc_charisma_scaled_income_variance:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] returns pct_op(input, charisma/2) = the half-charisma-scaled RNG spread bound for harvest income variance. charisma via get_daimyo_stat4_by_fief(+4). Called by $A1E2 (gold) and $A21F (rice) as the rng_mod range.
NesPrgRom:21AA:calc_fief_harvest_base_term:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] base yield term = pct_op(mult_6D2D, hiwater_6009) + pct_op(mult_6D2D, pct_op(40, hiwater_6007)); no men-sub, no RNG (those live in callers $A1E2/$A21F). The '$A1AA' base term of the cracked harvest formula; feeds both gold and rice.
NesPrgRom:21E2:calc_fief_gold_income:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] gold harvest term: calc_fief_harvest_base_term ($A1AA) + town-pct + rng_mod(charisma-variance $A191), clamped to header@+24 (dev ceiling). Result added to gold@+0 by the $A26F sweep. Town/dev high-water pair $6007/$6009.
NesPrgRom:221F:calc_fief_rice_income:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] rice harvest term: same shape as $A1E2 but reads the OUTPUT high-water pair $6003/$6005; base + 2 rng_mod terms, clamped to header@+24. Result added to rice@+6 by the $A26F sweep. (Note: live map has rice@+6, men@+16 — not the ROM-defaults shorthand.)
NesPrgRom:226F:harvest_income_sweep_all_fiefs:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] the per-turn harvest driver: loops all fiefs, gates on ai_state + loyalty@+12 != 0, adds calc_fief_gold_income ($A1E2) to gold@+0 and calc_fief_rice_income ($A21F) to rice@+6, then per fief repay_province_debt_from_gold ($92A9) + consume_province_army_upkeep ($A15B) + cap_fief_stats ($D836). The cracked harvest formula, as named code.
NesPrgRom:22DF:roll_3pct_event_chance:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] 4-instruction predicate: returns rng_mod(100) < 3 = fixed 3% probability. No records touched. Event-gate used by the planner's candidate-list build.
NesPrgRom:22ED:drift_daimyo_luck:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Per-season LUCK drift: daimyo record byte +3 (LUCK) perturbed by -5..+5: *ptr += rng_mod(11); *ptr -= 5 (ptr = daimyo_record_addr(idx)+3). Called in the $A30D loop. Luck being a random walk is why field +3 wanders across save dumps (resolves the old '+3 dropped 105->26' = a random walk, not stat depletion). Stat names per Chris/manual: +2 Drive, +3 Luck, +4 Charisma, +5 IQ. (was drift_daimyo_stat3_random.)
NesPrgRom:230D:per_period_fief_daimyo_update_driver:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10] multi-stage per-period driver: loop1 per fief calls drift_daimyo_luck ($A2ED) + (if $6D2D<88) decays loyalty@+12 to 90%; then UI + process_fiefs_with_state_ff ($8E63); then a $6D5F (period mod-4) switch dispatching $9F8C/$A066/$A26F/$90E8; loop2 per fief check_and_process_daimyo_natural_death ($9194). Proposer wrongly called the switch handlers 'no-op' (lossy C) and named only the loyalty branch.
NesPrgRom:23AA:write_sram_save_checksum_and_signature:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] the WRITE/STAMP side of save integrity: accumulates the syscall-22 checksum over SRAM and STORES it to $7FEB, strcpy's the signature to $7FED, then UI. Sibling of verify_sram_save_integrity ($821E) which READS+compares the same. Proposer's 'compute checksum' missed the store.
NesPrgRom:2455:ai_strategic_turn_planner:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] THE AI per-turn driver root (JMP'd from vm_bootstrap): clears daimyo_weakness_flag, gates on $6DA1 bit7, advances period ($6D5F/$6D9F + roll_period_rate_table $924A + sub-driver $A30D), pointer-selects a disaster/event handler ($9CB3/$9D00/$9ED9), builds the event candidate list, then the WAR-TARGET loop at $A581: daimyo_weakness_flag[i] = (rng_mod(400) < (100-health)) | flag = the (100-health)/400 weakest-enemy weighting (matches ai_war_architecture), gated by fief_owner_weakness + $8C1E, with daimyo-name war-declaration UI.
NesPrgRom:25D5:rng_mod_30:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] returns rng_mod((const_two+1)*10) = rng_mod(30) = 0..29. Pure RNG tail-call helper (proposer's '0_to_30' was off-by-one; rng_mod(n) is 0..n-1). Used by $A5E6.
NesPrgRom:25E6:spawn_uprising_force_from_province:[MED AMENDED 2026-06-10; flavor-corrected 2026-06-12] The GENERIC uprising-attacker spawner, not zealot-specific. Populates the uprising attacker slot (idx 50 / record $7515) by scaling the target province's record (8 pct_op entries = 40-59% of defender stats) while depleting its output@+8/hidden@+16/men@+6; charisma-gated transfers; sets selected_province_idx=50; ai_turn_flags bit 64 (uprising) / 32 (revolt). The 'zealot/monk/rebel' wording is cosmetic and keyed by FIEF INDEX downstream (select_message_string_by_flags_and_arg: fiefs 7/23='zealots', 13/30='monks', else rebels) — see appendix-events.md. PRE-battle setup (scratch $6F7D-$6F81 consumed later by apply_conquest_outcome). Sole caller vm_bootstrap $A7E5. Renamed 2026-10-28 (was spawn_zealot_uprising_force_from_province): select_message_string_by_flags_and_arg picks the flavor by fief index (case 7/23 zealots, 13/30 monks, default rebels), and the one caller passes the revolt kind as arg1.
NesPrgRom:2742:shuffle_fief_turn_order_array:[HIGH AMENDED 2026-06-10] Fisher-Yates shuffle of the turn-order byte array at $6F1B (identity-init'd by init_new_game_state): per fief, cap_fief_stats ($D836) + two rng_mod($6D9D) draws + swap_byte ($CB80). The documented per-turn turn-order randomization. Caller vm_bootstrap $A803 (once per turn). Proposer's 'no-ops' REFUTED (host_calls hidden by lossy C).
NesPrgRom:4D5A:window_tile_gfx_8d5a:[GFX-TILES 2026-06-10] Window/menu tile source (ppu_copy_rect_wrap, fief_select_input_loop); shared $8D5A blob.
NesPrgRom:5E3C:record_sram_9e3c:[SRAM-ADDR 2026-06-10] SRAM record-area address (syscall16_sram_wrap, fief_select_input_loop).
NesPrgRom:79DC:jumptab_b9dc:[ROM-DATA] pointer/dispatch table; read by driver_trade via imm-word ptr; bytes: 04 9f af 9f 03 a0 68 a0 13 a1 af a1
NesPrgRom:79E8:jumptab_b9e8:[ROM-DATA] pointer/dispatch table; read by driver_other via imm-word ptr; bytes: 66 b0 9d b0 d2 b0 09 b1 2b b1 4b b1
NesPrgRom:7A10:str_market_panel_nl2:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] market panel pad-alias of $BA12
NesPrgRom:7A11:str_market_panel_nl1:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] market panel pad-alias of $BA12
NesPrgRom:7A12:str_market_panel:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] '__Market__','Rate/Rice/Arms/Men %2d.%1d'
NesPrgRom:7A69:str_fief_list_columns:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] '-','%4d','----','%3d','Home fief','Direct','Empty','Fief'
NesPrgRom:7A6F:str_field_dashes:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] "----" (4 dashes), the empty/blank placeholder drawn by draw_province_stat_or_dashes ($83A2) for inactive provinces. bytes: 2d 2d 2d 2d 00 ... (followed by a "%3d" string).
NesPrgRom:7A78:str_field_dashes3:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] "---" (3 dashes), the 3-digit empty placeholder drawn by draw_province_stat3_or_dashes ($83D5). bytes: 2d 2d 2d 00 (followed by "Home fie...").
NesPrgRom:7A9C:str_fief_info_labels:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] 'Sick','Home','Fief','Gold','Town','Rice'...
NesPrgRom:7B26:str_not_home_and_status:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] 'Not home fief',' has lost'
NesPrgRom:7B3E:str_daimyo_status_msgs:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] ' has lost',' has retreated',' has fled'
NesPrgRom:7BE2:str_is_this_ok:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] 'Is this OK'
NesPrgRom:7BEE:str_dams_value_label:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] 'Dams value'
NesPrgRom:7BFA:str_output_label:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] 'Output'
NesPrgRom:7BFB:str_output_label_alias1:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] 'Output' (alias of $BBFA)
NesPrgRom:7BFC:str_output_label_alias2:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] 'Output' (alias of $BBFA)
NesPrgRom:7C04:str_treasure_room_full:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] 'The treasure room is already full!'
NesPrgRom:7C05:str_treasure_room_full_alias:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] alias of $BC04
NesPrgRom:7C06:msg_loan_prompt:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] loan prompt ('The treasu[re room]...'); read by effect_loan ($9F04). bytes: 00 0a 54 68 65 20 74 72 65 61 73 75 = \0\nThe treasu.
NesPrgRom:7C59:msg_repay_debt:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] The debt-repayment prompt strings ("...No gold..."), message_display'd at the top of prompt_repay_debt ($9FAF). bytes: 00 0a 4e 6f 20 67 6f 6c 64 00 ... = \0\n'No gold'\0...
NesPrgRom:7C75:msg_sell_rice_prompt:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] '%s rice\nwil[l]...' sell-rice prompt; read by effect_sell_rice ($A003). bytes: 00 25 73 20 72 69 63 65 0a 77 69 6c.
NesPrgRom:7CA2:msg_buy_rice_prompt:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] "...rice\nwill..." — the buy-rice prompt drawn by effect_buy_rice ($A068). bytes: 00 20 72 69 63 65 0a 77 69 6c 6c 20.
NesPrgRom:7CE9:msg_buy_arms_prompt:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] "Armory full..." — the buy-arms prompt/strings drawn by effect_buy_arms ($A113). bytes: 00 41 72 6d 6f 72 79 20 66 75 6c 6c = \0'Armory full'.
