NesPrgRom:79B2:command_driver_table:34-entry pointer table — entry N points to the bytecode subroutine that drives menu command N+1. Entries 0-20 are the 21 lord commands, 21-33 are sub-handlers reachable from within those drivers. See command-table.txt for the full listing. Chapter 9's foundational find.
NesPrgRom:56D1:driver_move:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Move command (cmd 1): requires men (effect_war_combat_prep_b); filters the player's own provinces, province_select_helper/prompt for the destination, then relocates troops (effect_move blends unit quality).
NesPrgRom:5850:driver_war:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] War command (cmd 2): capital-only + not-too-weak (prep_d); requires gold/rice/men (prep_c/a/b); marks relations (effect_war_e); province_select for the target fief, then launches the battle. The main offensive command.
NesPrgRom:599A:driver_tax:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Tax command (cmd 3): shows current fief_tax_rate ($6D2D), number_input new rate (cap 30 if keyed-daimyo defender else 100); peasant reaction (protesting cutscene 19 if raised); calls effect_tax. Chapter 11.
NesPrgRom:5A5D:driver_send:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Send command (cmd 4): build_eligible_province_list, province_select_helper/prompt for the destination, then transfers rice/gold to it (effect_send caps the amount).
NesPrgRom:5B7E:driver_dam:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Dam command (cmd 5): blocks if no peasants/output ($7009) or at the dam limit ($7001+10 dams field >= 100) (the at-our-limit message); else prompts spend, debits gold, and applies effect_dam + add_effect_gain_clamped to the dams field. Two-effect command.
NesPrgRom:5C4F:driver_pact:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Pact command (cmd 6): build_eligible_province_list, province_select for the target fief; spends a point of the daimyo DRIVE (record +2) and forms a non-aggression pact.
NesPrgRom:5D3D:driver_grow:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Grow command (cmd 7): blocks if at limit ($7001+24 cap <= +8 output) ('we're at our limit') or no gold; else 'spend how much on output', number_input(1, gold), debits gold and calls effect_grow. The fully-traced reference command (Chapter 9).
NesPrgRom:5DC4:driver_marry:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Marry command (cmd 8): capital-only; build_fiefs_excluding_daimyo, province_select for the target fief; spends a point of daimyo DRIVE (record +2); alliance-by-marriage (outcome not guaranteed).
NesPrgRom:61B6:driver_trade:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Trade command (cmd 9): if effect_trade() (merchant present / port fief), draws the 6-item trade submenu (buy/sell rice/arms/men) in the right panel and dispatches. Chapter 11.
NesPrgRom:65F4:driver_hire:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Hire command (cmd 10): requires gold (effect_war_combat_prep_c); recruit-which prompt Men/Ninja -> effect_hire_men (recruit soldiers, dilute army stats) or effect_ninja_sabotage (covert mission).
NesPrgRom:6637:driver_train:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Train command (cmd 11): if skill ($7001+20) < cap (+24); needs men (+16) else 'you have no soldiers' + clear_military_stats_if_no_men; else cutscene 10, effect_train (skill += rng), clamp skill to cap. Chapter 10+11.
NesPrgRom:66C7:driver_view:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] View command (cmd 12/19): build_eligible_province_list; views own fief stats or (if gold >= 10 and targets exist) spies on an enemy fief's stats. Calls effect_view_a / effect_view_defending_province.
NesPrgRom:6853:driver_build:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Build command (cmd): blocks if at the town limit ($7001+24 cap <= +4 town) (we-are-at-our-limit) or no gold; else spend-how-much prompt, debits gold, calls effect_build (raises the town field). Confirms $7001+4 = town.
NesPrgRom:6A1F:driver_give:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Give command (cmd): effect_give_a + effect_give_c eligibility (gold/rice/peasants/men); if a resource is givable, prompts the type and recipient and applies give_transfer_apply (which develops the recipient).
NesPrgRom:6AAE:driver_bribe:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Bribe command (cmd 15): requires gold > 10; build_eligible_province_list, province_select for the target enemy fief, then effect_bribe (siphons the enemy's output if the loyalty/charisma contest succeeds).
NesPrgRom:6D67:driver_assign:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Assign command (cmd): needs men ($7001+16) else you-have-no-soldiers; needs >= 30 gold, then effect_assign(30) (the arms editor) and debits 30 gold on commit.
NesPrgRom:6DB3:driver_rest:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Rest command (cmd 17): only at the capital (fief_is_daimyo_capital) — number_input(1,10) seasons -> rest_turns_remaining[owner], 'it will do you good' + cutscene 32; else show_not_home_fief. Skips turns to recover.
NesPrgRom:6F38:driver_map:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Map command: repaint_screen, render the selected province's map section (via province_to_map_section_17/50 table), then browse_map_sections to scroll the strategic map.
NesPrgRom:6F66:driver_grant:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Grant command (cmd 19): capital-only (else show_not_home_fief); build_eligible_province_list and a province-select loop to grant/appoint a fief to a retainer.
NesPrgRom:723E:driver_other:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Other command (cmd 20): draws the 7-item settings submenu (msg_change_which), submenu_prompt(7), and dispatches to the setting_* handlers (sound/animation/speed/save/watch + save/end-game). Chapter 11.
NesPrgRom:72A1:driver_pass:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Pass command driver (cmd 21): message_display(msg_what_a_waste) + confirm_prompt; returns 1. Ends the fief's turn without acting. Chapter 11.
NesPrgRom:5F04:effect_loan:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Loan command (driver 21): if gold is at the treasure-room cap (gold >= header) refuse (treasure room already full); else compute the max loan via ratio_times10_capped(town-debt, loan_rate+10, header-gold), number_input, and take it (effect_take_loan adds the interest to debt). (was subhandler_9F04.)
NesPrgRom:5FAF:prompt_repay_debt:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Debt-repayment handler (driver-table 22): message_display(prompt); if the record has debt (arg1->debt) and gold (*arg1), number_input(1, min(debt, gold)) for the amount, then gold -= amount and arg1->debt -= amount; returns 1 on a paid amount, 0 on cancel. (was 'subhandler_9FAF'.)
NesPrgRom:6003:effect_sell_rice:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Sell-rice command (driver 23): max = ratio_times10_capped(header-gold, gold_rice_exchange_rate, rice); how-much-rice-will-you-sell, number_input; effect_sell_rice_for_gold(n), clamp gold, cycle_economy_rate(1). Pairs with effect_buy_rice. (was subhandler_A003.)
NesPrgRom:6068:effect_buy_rice:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Buy-rice effect (driver 24): if province has gold, max = ratio_times10_capped(gold, gold_rice_exchange_rate, header-rice), 'how much rice will you buy', number_input; gold -= math32_muladddiv(exchange_rate, n), rice += n, clamp_amount_to_province_max(rice). (was 'subhandler_A068'.)
NesPrgRom:6113:effect_buy_arms:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Buy-arms/weapons effect (driver 25): 'weapons for who?' if no men; else max = ratio_times10_capped(gold, arms_buy_price_rate, header-arms), 'how many', number_input; gold -= cost, arms += n. (was 'subhandler_A113'; calls amount_div_force_factor $A0ED.)
NesPrgRom:61AF:noop_command_handler:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Do-nothing command handler: returns 0 (body is just clearA + vm_return). Occupies driver-table indices 26 and 33 — the disabled/reserved command slots. (was 'subhandler_A1AF'.)
NesPrgRom:7066:setting_sound_on_off:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Settings-menu Sound toggle (driver 27): message_display(msg_sound), prompt_ab_window(msg_on_off); B-cancel returns; else audio_wait_gate = choice, and stop audio (syscall_audio_control(0,0)) if Off, else call_bank10_entry(1).
NesPrgRom:709D:setting_animation_on_off:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Settings-menu Animation toggle (driver 28): message_display(msg_animation), prompt_ab_window(msg_on_off); sets ai_turn_flags bit 2 (|4 on, &~4 off) — the battle-animation flag.
NesPrgRom:70D2:setting_message_wait_speed:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Settings-menu message-wait/speed (driver 29): shows current speed sqrt(delay_loop_count/2), number_input(1,10); sets delay_loop_count = (n*n)<<1 (= 2*n^2). The message/game pacing knob.
NesPrgRom:7109:setting_save_game:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Settings-menu Save (driver 30): 'are you sure' prompt_y_n; on yes sets sram_save_pending_flag=1 + 'game will save at end of season' + confirm_prompt. Deferred save.
NesPrgRom:712B:setting_watch_battles:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Settings-menu watch-other-battles toggle (driver 31): message_display(msg_watch_others_battle), prompt_ab_window(msg_y_n); B-cancel keeps current, else ui_confirm_flag_6e7d = choice.
NesPrgRom:714B:command_end_game:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] End-game/resign command (driver 32): 'do you really want to end the [game]' prompt_y_n; on yes, increment_ai_player_count, and if ai_turn_flags bit7 (abort/game-over gate) shows the 'game over' screen + hangs; else resigns the player's province. (was 'subhandler_B14B'.)
NesPrgRom:47F0:effect_grow:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Grow (develop) command effect: guard amount<1; gain = 2 * math32_3arg(amount, 6-const_two, sqrt_int(fief->output+amount)) = 2*amount*(6-skill)/sqrt(output+amount) (const_two = skill level 1-5, so higher skill = less gain); min 1; clamp to headroom (fief->header - fief->output); flat 100 if gain/2>output else math32_2arg refinement; drains loyalty + dams; output += gain. Returns gain/2 for display. The canonical Grow formula (chapter 9).
NesPrgRom:48A6:effect_build:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Build (town) command effect: guard amount<1; gain = math32_3arg(amount, 6-const_two, sqrt_int(fief->town + amount)) (min 1), capped at headroom (header-town); fief->town += gain. The Grow shape applied to the TOWN field; const_two = skill.
NesPrgRom:47D8:effect_dam:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Dam (flood-control) command effect: returns 0x2710 (10000, the no-data sentinel) if the fief's output is 0, else sqrt_int(output) — the dam benefit scales with sqrt(output). Two-step command (driver also calls helper_dam_rounding $887D).
NesPrgRom:487D:add_effect_gain_clamped:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Applies an effect gain to a province field: gain = arg1, halved (round-up) if fief_owner_weakness(selected_province); *arg2 += gain; then clamp_amount_to_province_max(arg2). The layered 'capped add' on top of the sqrt-driven main gain, used by Dam + Build. (was 'helper_dam_rounding'.)
NesPrgRom:42D6:effect_tax:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Applies a signed tax_delta percent to a stat: delta% = pct_op(stat, abs16(tax_delta)); returns stat - delta% if tax_delta<0 (decrease) else stat + delta% (increase). Called twice from driver_tax (rate-set + peasantry-reaction).
NesPrgRom:4BE5:effect_send:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Send (gift/transfer) effect: returns min_word(ceiling - current, budget) — the amount that can be sent = the gap to the destination's ceiling, capped at the sender's available budget.
NesPrgRom:4CA5:effect_move:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Move command: relocates `amount` men from the donor (selected_province) to the target (battle_defending_province) — both men fields at record +$7011 (+16). First blends the 3 unit-quality stats (morale/skill/arms) into the target via scaled_force_transfer weighted by the moving men, then target.men += amount, donor.men -= amount.
NesPrgRom:4A15:effect_trade:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Trade availability: the two port fiefs (13 & 14 in the 17-fief scenario; 30 & 32 in the 50-fief) always allow trade (return 1); otherwise gated on ai_turn_flags bit 0 (the per-period trade flag).
NesPrgRom:62D2:effect_ninja_sabotage:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Ninja/sabotage command (Hire->Ninja path): hire ninjas (max via hire_gold_rate), pick target fief + mission (uprising/revolt/dams/assassin/arson) via the msg menu; field drains via hire_stat_drain_rng; on failure effect_ninja_failed ($A29B). The covert-action command.
NesPrgRom:5586:effect_train:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Train command effect: raises the selected province's skill field ($7015 = $7001+20) by (rng_mod(20)+10)*4; +10 bonus if the daimyo's (IQ + LUCK) [daimyo record +5 + +3] exceeds rng_mod(10)+90. Returns 11. Chapter 10.
NesPrgRom:4D4D:effect_bribe:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Bribe command: if bribe_success_check(selected, defender), defect_amount = sqrt_int(gold_amount); compute_bribe_effect_value on the target's loyalty, target output ($7009) -= defect, own output ($7001+8) += defect; play_result_jingle(0), trigger_cutscene(26), success message. Siphons output by bribing the enemy fief.
NesPrgRom:6C11:effect_assign:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Assign command: renders the arms-allocation edit screen (render_arms_edit_screen) and runs a cursor input loop letting the player redistribute arms across the 5 unit types (province_unit_type_pct; arms field $7017=+22). REFUTES the old note 'places a retainer' — it is the arms-assignment editor.
NesPrgRom:43FA:effect_view_a:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] View command screen setup (variant A): repaint_screen, palette_swap + 3 palette writes, draws the View window frame (6 ppu_render_rect_wrap panes), sets ui_pending_flag_7fc9=1. The own-fief detail-view layout.
NesPrgRom:45EA:effect_view_b:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] View command (others variant B): builds a 0xFF-terminated list at $6F89 of all enemy-owned, active (province_ai_state != 255) fiefs — the targets the player can View/spy on.
NesPrgRom:45A7:effect_view_c:View effect, variant C.
NesPrgRom:66B3:effect_view_d:[MED CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns rng_mod(record[arg1+3]) + record[arg1+5] — a randomized value from two byte fields of the record at arg1 (if a daimyo record, +3=LUCK and +5=IQ -> rng(LUCK)+IQ). View-command variant D; the displayed quantity's exact meaning is open.
NesPrgRom:693A:effect_give_a:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Give-eligibility: returns give_eligibility_flags(fief->output, fief->men) — the 2-bit flag of which resources (output / men) the fief can give. Variant A of the Give command.
NesPrgRom:695E:effect_give_b:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Give command variant B (gold/rice): give_rice_gold_eligibility(fief), prompt gold-or-rice (prompt_ab_window msg_gold_rice), then give_transfer_apply for the chosen resource.
NesPrgRom:69D5:effect_give_c:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Give command variant C (peasants/men): effect_give_a(fief) eligibility, prompt peasants-or-men (prompt_ab_window msg_peasnts_men), then give_transfer_apply.
NesPrgRom:41FC:effect_war_a:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] War-declaration effect: zeroes two relations_matrix ($6193 stride-54) entries — between the attacker (selected_province_idx) & defender (battle_defending_province) provinces, and between their two owning daimyo (selected_province_owner / fief_owner(defender)). Declaring war resets those relations to 0.
NesPrgRom:4172:count_eligible_targets:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Counts (arg3=0) or draws+counts (arg3=1) the eligible target fiefs for command arg1: walks the 0xFF-terminated candidate list (arg2), keeping each that passes target_eligible_by_cmd AND has province_state ($6CF7[cand]) != 0xFF; returns the count (page-limited to 18 when drawing).
NesPrgRom:412F:target_eligible_by_cmd:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Per-command target-fief validity: switch(cmd) -> cmds 1/4/19 (war-type) return is_enemy_owned(fief); cmds 2/6/8/15/255 apply their own enemy/own-owned test; default ineligible. Returns 1/0.
NesPrgRom:4DE1:dedup_owners:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Reads the 0xFF-terminated fief list arg1 and builds a de-duplicated-by-OWNER list into the $6F4F dedup buffer (skips a fief whose fief_owner already appears). (was dedup_owners_to_6f4f.)
NesPrgRom:5323:effect_war_combat_prep_a:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] War-prep rice check: war_prep_clamp_depleted_field_notify(msg_you_have_no_rice, fief, fief*26 + $7007) — zero-clamps the fief's rice ($7001+6) and notifies if depleted. (Bank-1 $9323; a different bank's $9323 is ravage_defender_field_off10 — cross-bank pair.)
NesPrgRom:533A:effect_war_combat_prep_b:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] War-prep men check: war_prep_clamp_depleted_field_notify(msg_you_have_no_soldiers, fief, fief*26 + $7011) -> zero-clamps the fief's men ($7001+16) and notifies if depleted. (Sibling of prep_a=rice $7007 / prep_c=gold $7001.)
NesPrgRom:5351:effect_war_combat_prep_c:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] War-prep gold check: war_prep_clamp_depleted_field_notify(msg_you_have_no_gold, fief, fief*26 + $7001) -> zero-clamps the fief's gold ($7001+0) and notifies if depleted. (Sibling of prep_a=rice / prep_b=men.)
NesPrgRom:5368:effect_war_combat_prep_d:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] War-prep weakness gate: is_too_weak = fief_owner_weakness(fief); if set, redraw_window(msg_lord_you_are_too_weak_for_batt) + confirm_prompt. Returns the weakness flag (1 = abort the attack).
NesPrgRom:5814:effect_war_e:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] War-prep variant E: walks the 0xFF-terminated fief list at $6F4F and writes 1 into the parallel relation-flags output array (relation_flags_out[i]) for each entry. Marks all listed fiefs.
NesPrgRom:4B0A:effect_sell_rice_for_gold:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Sell-rice trade effect: province gold ($7001+0) += math32_muladddiv(gold_rice_exchange_rate, rice_amount); province rice ($7001+6) -= rice_amount; cycle_economy_rate(1). (was 'effect_subhandler_A003'.)
NesPrgRom:4B40:effect_take_loan:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Loan command effect: rate = loan_rate+10; if amount<=0 (max loan) amount = ratio_times10_capped(town, rate, town-debt) with 0 interest, else interest = math32_muladddiv(rate, amount); province debt ($7001+2) += interest, gold += amount. Borrow gold at interest. (was 'effect_subhandler_9F04'.)
NesPrgRom:60ED:amount_div_force_factor:[MED CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns amount / divisor where divisor = math32_3arg(fief->arms + fief->men, 5, fief->header) = (arms+men)*5/header (floored to >=1) — scales `amount` down by the army's relative size. (was 'effect_subhandler_A113' — misnamed AND mis-addressed: this is $A0ED, not $A113. Exact role of the quotient still open.)
NesPrgRom:404C:province_select_prompt:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] 'Select a fief' picker: loops select_province_by_cursor(1, scenario_fief_count), accepting only a pick that is in the eligible_fief_list (arg1, 0xFF-terminated) AND not province_state_is_FF; returns the 1-based picked fief. Called by 7 lord-command drivers (Move/War/Send/Pact/Marry/View/Bribe).
NesPrgRom:479F:province_select_helper:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Province-select orchestrator: if count_eligible_targets(cmd,list,0)==0, show msg_no_fiefs + confirm and return 0; else draw the prompt and return count_eligible_targets(cmd,list,1) (the drawn/committed count). Companion to province_select_prompt; called by the 7 target-taking drivers.
NesPrgRom:471E:fief_info_display:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Renders the fief stat panel (right side, cursor col 22): sets fief_menu_info_mode_flag=arg1, redraws msg_menu, clears the panel, then draws a numbered list of stat labels ("%2d" + label from the $F816 table) — mode 0 shows items 1..12, mode 1 shows items 13..24 (paged). Called by 3 drivers.
NesPrgRom:47CB:show_not_home_fief:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Thin wrapper: message_display(msg_not_home_fief) — the 'this is not your home fief' error shown by 3 command drivers when a command requires the daimyo's capital. (was 'helper_87CB'.)
NesPrgRom:4B8F:play_result_jingle:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Plays a command-result audio cue: syscall_audio_control(0,0) (stop), call_bank10_entry(arg1 ? 8 : 7) (sound 8 vs 7 = success vs failure), waits while audio plays if audio_wait_gate==1, then call_bank10_entry(1). Used by Pact/Marry to signal accept/reject. (was 'helper_8B8F'.)
NesPrgRom:71A6:submenu_prompt:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Submenu prompt at (21,7): waits, then polls until A (confirm -> selection 0) or B (cancel -> arg1-1), then open_message_window and returns the selection. arg1 = option count. The 'pick from a few options' primitive (Trade buy/sell, etc.).
NesPrgRom:42AC:clamp_amount_to_province_max:[MED CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] In-place caps *arg1 at the selected province's record field $7019 (= $7001 + 0x18, the +24 word): *arg1 = min(*arg1, province[selected_province_idx].field[+24]), floored at 0. The +24 field is not yet grounded (a per-province ceiling — re-confirm when the $7001 record map reaches +24). (was 'helper_82AC'.)
NesPrgRom:4357:ratio_times10_capped:[HIGH CERTIFIED 2026-06-10] = min((arg1*10)/arg2, arg3). Oracle-proven. (bug 1.3 ext-op stub.)
NesPrgRom:4A4E:cycle_economy_rate:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Cycles an economy rate field selected by arg1 (switch): e.g. arg1=0 increments loan_rate (wrap >15 -> rng_mod(15)), arg1=2 increments gold_rice_exchange_rate; sets ui_window_col=26 + a cursor row, redraws the new value, then restores the saved cursor. The +1/wrap rate adjuster behind the economy command menus. (was 'helper_8A4E'.)
NesPrgRom:43C7:draw_selected_province_stat:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Thin wrapper: draw_province_stat_or_dashes(selected_province_idx, arg1) — draws stat value arg1 for the currently-selected province (or '----' if inactive). (was 'helper_83C7'.)
NesPrgRom:6F10:browse_map_sections:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Strategic-map section browser: message_display(msg_arrows_other_sections) + redraw_window(msg_a_button_menu), then loops fief_select_input_loop + render_map_section to scroll between map sections until the A-menu input (10) exits. arg1 = anchor fief. (was 'map_helper_af10'.)
NesPrgRom:4250:relations_matrix_get:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Pure getter into the 54-stride relations matrix at $6193: dsel = (party_a < party_b) ^ order_flag canonicalizes which party is row vs col, then returns byte[$6193 + row*54 + col]. 3 args (party_a, party_b, order_flag); no side effects. (cf. clear_fief_pair_6193 $E1E7.)
NesPrgRom:4271:relations_rng_predicate:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Probabilistic relations gate: returns 1 iff EITHER rng_mod(100) < relations_matrix_get(fief_owner(arg1), fief_owner(arg2), 1) (owner relation) OR rng_mod(100) < relations_matrix_get(arg1, arg2, 0) (province relation). An OR of two relation-vs-roll checks; AI-decision gate.
NesPrgRom:4303:math32_muladddiv:[HIGH CERTIFIED 2026-06-10] = (rate*amount + 9) / 10 (rounded scale-by). Oracle-proven vs ROM. DREAM renders this as ext-op stub 'return rate' (bug 1.3).
NesPrgRom:4327:scale_div10_capcheck:[HIGH CERTIFIED 2026-06-10] v=(arg1*arg2)/10 (FLOOR, no rounding); returns 0xFFFF if v >= arg3 (cap exceeded) else v. Oracle-proven. (bug 1.3 ext-op; DREAM stubs it.)
NesPrgRom:4379:apply_two_grows_const1_override:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Saves const_two (skill 1-5), forces it to 1 (max, skill-INDEPENDENT grow), calls record_apply_two_grows(arg1,arg2), then *arg1 -= arg2 (floor 0), restores const_two, returns the saved value. The temporary skill override makes this grow deterministic regardless of difficulty (events/scenario effects). (Returns saved const_two, NOT 2.)
NesPrgRom:43A2:draw_province_stat_or_dashes:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] If province arg1 is active (province_ai_state[arg1] != 255), draws the stat value arg2 as draw_message(msg_fmt__4d "%4d"); else (empty province) redraws str_field_dashes ($BA6F = "----"). Used by the View driver + AI ($B79B) to render a fief stat cell or a blank. (was 'province_window_redraw_ba6f'; the _ba6f suffix was the data table.) Bank-1 $83A2; bank-2 $83A2 is calc_tactical_cell_coords (cross-bank pair).
NesPrgRom:43D5:draw_province_stat3_or_dashes:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] 3-digit sibling of draw_province_stat_or_dashes ($83A2): if province arg1 active (province_ai_state[arg1]!=255), draws arg2 as draw_message(msg_fmt__3d_ba74 "%3d"); else redraws str_field_dashes3 ($BA78 = "---"). (was 'province_window_redraw_ba78'.)
NesPrgRom:4003:prompt_message_and_redraw:[CONFIRMED/MED] Verified at bytecode altitude. True body is small: $8008-$804B (RETURN at $804B), next sub starts $804C. Body: $8008 PUSH $BA10 -> CALL message_display ($D326, 2 args); $800F-$8014 compare arg1(local12) to $00FF, JUMPF $8021; taken-false path $8017 PUSH $B9FD …
NesPrgRom:4094:draw_market_rates:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Draws the 5 market rates panel (cursor col 20, rows 21-25) each as "%2d.%1d" (value/10 . value%10): loan_rate, gold_rice_exchange_rate, arms_buy_price_rate, gold_men_hire_rate (+1 more) — the contiguous word array $6E0B..$6E13. (was 'view_render_five_stats'.)
NesPrgRom:459A:effect_view_defending_province:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Thin wrapper: effect_view_a(battle_defending_province) -- the View-others path, runs the View screen on the currently-targeted defending province.
NesPrgRom:45B4:draw_fief_view_label:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Draws the fief's View-window label: if fief_is_daimyo_capital[arg1] ($6DA2), redraw_window(msg_home "Home") + msg_fief_bab0; else redraw the province-state label from the $FEE9 table indexed by get_province_ai_state(arg1). (was 'view_window_redraw_by_6da2_flag'.)
NesPrgRom:491D:develop_loyalty:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Develop-loyalty command: guard amount<1; gain = math32_3arg(amount, 6-const_two, sqrt_int((fief->loyalty + fief->output)/2 + amount)) (min 1), capped at headroom (header-loyalty); fief->loyalty += gain<<1. Returns gain. Same Grow shape as effect_grow; const_two = skill (higher = less gain).
NesPrgRom:496F:develop_wealth:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Develop-wealth command: guard amount<1; gain = math32_3arg(amount, 6-const_two, sqrt_int((fief->wealth + fief->town)/2 + amount)) (min 1), capped at headroom (header-wealth); fief->wealth += gain<<1. Returns gain. (Grow shape; const_two = skill.)
NesPrgRom:49C1:develop_morale:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Develop-morale command: guard amount<1; gain = math32_3arg(amount, 6-const_two, sqrt_int((fief->morale + fief->men)/2 + amount)) (min 1), capped at headroom (header-morale); fief->morale += gain (NOT gain<<1 — morale grows HALF as fast as loyalty/wealth, a deliberate quirk). Returns gain.
NesPrgRom:4BC1:compute_bribe_effect_value:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns word_sub_saturating(arg1, pct_op(min_word(arg2, *arg1)+1, rng_mod(25)+30) + 1) — arg1 minus a random 30-54% of min(arg2, *arg1), floored at 0. The post-bribe remaining value. Sole caller effect_bribe ($8D4D).
NesPrgRom:4BF4:apply_hire_unit_stats:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Blends arg2 newly-hired men into army record arg1: morale/skill/arms each = scaled_force_transfer(old, recruit_base, arg2, men, header) — recruit bases are random (morale rng+40, skill rng+60, arms rng+50), weighted toward the new troops; then men += arg2. Diluting average. 2 callers (player + AI hire paths).
NesPrgRom:4C68:random_daimyo_stat_increment:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] For the player's province only (get_province_ai_state==0) and a 1-in-10 roll: pick a random daimyo stat (record +1..+5 = HEALTH/DRIVE/LUCK/CHARISMA/IQ) and +2, capped at 200 (0xC8). Per-turn slow stat growth. Returns 255.
NesPrgRom:4D02:bribe_success_check:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Bribe contest: briber score = province[arg1] loyalty ($700D=+12) + daimyo CHARISMA (+4); target score = same for arg2 + rng_mod(10)*const_two(skill). Returns 1 (bribe succeeds) iff briber > target AND a coin-flip (rng_mod(2)) passes; else 0. Sole caller effect_bribe.
NesPrgRom:4DFD:resolve_siege_assault_outcome:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Non-tactical (auto-resolve) siege/assault: reads attacker (selected_province) vs defender (battle_defending_province) morale/skill/arms triples at record $7013 (+18/+20/+22), plus the war-state men/rice from $6F7F (attacker) / $6F85 (defender), and computes the outcome code (returned). The off-map auto-resolution of a war.
NesPrgRom:5009:ai_attack_announce_prompt:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Announces an AI attack: message_display(attacker daimyo name = daimyo_name_table[selected_province_owner()]), draw_message(msg_from_fief_2d_has, selected_province_idx+1), draw_message(msg_invaded_s_in_fief_2d, daimyo_name_table[fief_owner(defender)], defender+1), confirm_prompt — '<X> from fief N has invaded <Y> in fief M'.
NesPrgRom:5046:ai_commit_attack_deduct_resources:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI attack commit: sets war_side_state_flag ($6F65; random bit7 if a resting capital, else 0); computes attack_budget = min(rice*2, men, gold) from the province record ($7001 +6/+16/+0); bails (returns 0) if budget < 5, else proceeds to commit the attack.
NesPrgRom:5181:decrement_byte_at:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Thin wrapper: deduct_byte_at(arg1, 1) — subtracts 1 from the byte at address arg1. (was 'ca12_with_const1_wrapper'; $CA12 = deduct_byte_at, const arg = 1.)
NesPrgRom:518D:ninja_mission_resolve_vs_defender:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Resolves a ninja/spy mission against the defender (only if defender is player-AI-state 0): contests the attacking daimyo's stats (selected_province_daimyo +4/+5 = CHARISMA/IQ) vs the defender daimyo's, with skill-scaled noise (rng_mod(const_two*10) on each side); the winner determines mission success. arg1 = mission type.
NesPrgRom:5301:war_prep_clamp_depleted_field_notify:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] If the field *arg3 is depleted (<=0): zero it, and if province arg2 is active (get_province_ai_state), message_display(arg1) + confirm_prompt. Returns *arg3. arg1=message ptr, arg2=province idx, arg3=field ptr. Callers effect_war_combat_prep_a/b/c pass province*26 + $7001/$7007/$7011 = the gold/rice/men fields.
NesPrgRom:5382:fief_men_if_provisioned:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns the fief's men (province record $7001+16) ONLY if it has rice (record +6 != 0); else 0. An unprovisioned army counts as 0 effective men. (record arg1*26+$7001.)
NesPrgRom:539D:fief_men_ratio_pct:[DIRECTION PINNED 2026-06-03 probe-ai-war-target.py] ratio = 100*men(argSlot1)/(men(argSlot1)+men(argSlot2)) where argSlot1 = FP+0x0B. ⚠️ The decompiled C DISPLAYS args reverse-pushed: in source `fief_men_ratio_pct(X,Y)` the SECOND-displayed arg Y is the NUMERATOR (Y's share of the X+Y men pool). Read every caller's >50/<50 comparison with that flip — it flips the apparent winner (pick_weakest_men_fief loop, find_fief_by_owner_men_minority). Oracle: (200,50)->80, (50,200)->20 reading the first slot. [CONFIRMED/HIGH] Verified at bytecode/call-index altitude. sub $939D (body $93A2): PUSH local13 -> CALL $9382, PUSH local12 -> CALL $9382, then CALL $D6DE (math32_2arg) over both results, RETURN at $93B2. The inner helper $9382 computes province = $7001 + arg*26 (province_tabl…
NesPrgRom:53B3:pick_weakest_men_fief:[NAME CORRECTED 2026-06-03, probe-ai-war-target.py] RETURNS THE FEWEST-MEN (WEAKEST) FIEF, not the most — the prior name 'pick_fief_with_most_men' was BACKWARDS. The decompiler's reverse-push display inverted the >50 test on read. ORACLE: a synthetic $6F4F list {men 200,50,120} returns the men=50 fief in BOTH orderings (list ptr arg @ FP+0x0B). So the AI's DEFAULT war target = the weakest adjacent enemy (fewest provisioned men). [AMENDED/MED] $93B3 walks an $FF-terminated fief-id list (caller $949A passes $6F4F at $94D0/$94D3; combat/war context — siblings call fief_owner_weakness/compact_relation_list/dd3a). Loop @ $93BE-$93D8: local 11 = running selected fief (init to list[0] @ $93B8-BA); for each list …
NesPrgRom:53DD:ai_relations_and_low_drive_skip_gate:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI gate, returns 1 iff (a relations-vs-rng_mod(100) check on candidate_fief — province relation if it passes, else owner relation) AND the acting daimyo's DRIVE (record +2) < 50. Low-drive + favorable-relations = skip/defer the action against this fief.
NesPrgRom:5423:pick_ai_attack_target_fief:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI attack-target picker: scans fief_list; for each AI-state target NOT skipped by ai_relations_and_low_drive_skip_gate whose fief_men_ratio_pct vs the candidate > 50, keeps it. Returns the chosen target fief.
NesPrgRom:545D:find_fief_by_owner_men_minority:[MED CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Scans list arg1 for the first fief owned by daimyo arg2 with fief_men_ratio_pct(fief, selected_province_idx) >= 50; returns it (else breaks). NOTE the test is ratio>=50 (comparable-or-stronger), so the name men_minority reads backwards vs the code -- confirm intent.
NesPrgRom:549A:ai_try_war_attack:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI war-attack attempt: bails if the attacker fief is weak or has no men/rice; else compact_relation_list, filter_province_list_by_owner, pick_weakest_men_fief as the target; if a valid target, commits the attack. The AI offensive decision.
NesPrgRom:55C9:ai_develop_grow_if_men_exceeds_gold:[UNPARKED via call-graph reconcile 2026-05-31, MED] Shared epilogue of ai_develop_town_handler ($B3AA) + ai_develop_dam_and_grow ($B42B). Body ($95CE): rng_mod(2) coin-flip increments a daimyo counter (selected_province_daimyo_record+4); then if men(+16) > gold(+0), calls apply_two_grows_const1_override ($8379) to apply extra grows, returns 14 else 0. Live $7001 map (+16=men, +0=gold). Was REFUTED helper_95C9 until callers were named.
NesPrgRom:560C:ai_reinforce_province_arms_and_econ_10pct:[MED CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI province reinforcement: bumps the daimyo's DRIVE (record +2) by rng_mod(const_two+1); then if the province has men (>8), seeds/distributes the unit-type arms allocation (province_unit_type_pct $76A9: base 50 + 5 per type + random +5 boosts) and applies the econ adjustment. (Deeper econ branch only partially decoded.)
NesPrgRom:57C1:fief_list_parallel_lookup:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Scans the 0xFF-terminated fief list at $6F4F for key arg1; on match returns the parallel word array's entry at the same index (*(word*)arg2, advancing arg2 += 2 per step). A parallel-array lookup keyed by fief. (was 'candidate_list_6f4f_lookup'.)
NesPrgRom:57EA:relations_roll_vs_owner:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10, bytecode-verified] Returns relations_matrix_get(p0, p1, order) > rng_mod(100) — a relations CHECK: does the pairwise relation beat a random 0-99 roll. arg2!=0 -> owner-vs-owner (selected_province_owner, fief_owner(arg1), 1); else province-vs-province (selected_province_idx, arg1, arg2). WARNING 4-c VALUE-WRONG: it renders the RHS as phi_980d_0 (a party index) instead of the rng_mod(100) roll — the early-computed roll was dropped (value-render bug); bytecode @ $97EF authoritative.
NesPrgRom:6255:hire_stat_drain_rng:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns (rng_mod(max_word(pct_op(arg1, sqrt_int(arg2)), 1)) + 1) * 5 — a randomized stat cost/drain in multiples of 5, with the RNG range = max(pct_op(arg1, sqrt(arg2)), 1). Body $A25A-$A273 (sqrt_int/pct_op/max_word/rng_mod host calls).
NesPrgRom:6274:report_fief_stat_decline:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] draw_message(msg_fief_d_s_s_has_declined_by_d, battle_defending_province+1, stat_name, arg2) — 'Fief N's <stat> has declined by <arg2>'. stat_name = msg_town_value when arg1==7, else the $F8AE stat-name table at arg1<<1.
NesPrgRom:629B:effect_ninja_failed:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10, bytecode-verified] The ninja/spy FAILURE effect: decrement_byte_at(daimyo CHARISMA +4) by 1 (reputation hit), redraw_window(msg_your_ninja_failed), standard_delay, then province gold ($7001+0) -= math32_muladddiv(hire_gold_rate, arg2) (the gold cost is still paid). REFUTES old name 'effect_hire_pay_gold' — the body is the ninja-failed path ('your ninja failed' + charisma loss), not a hire payment.
NesPrgRom:6553:effect_hire_men:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Hire-men effect: max = ratio_times10_capped(gold, gold_men_hire_rate, header-men); 'how many', number_input; gold -= math32_muladddiv(gold_men_hire_rate, n), apply_hire_unit_stats(fief, n) (blends recruit quality), cap arms, cycle_economy_rate(4), clamp men. (was 'effect_hire_variant_pay'.) [legacy: bytecode-confirmed at $A558a hire/recruit effect. $A558-A563: local9 = *(arg+24) - *(arg+16) (recruitable headroom; C names these arg1->header - arg1->men). $A565-A56B: validate via ratio_times10_capped($6E11 cost const, *…
NesPrgRom:68D3:give_transfer_apply:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Give effect: deducts the given amount from the fief's gold (arg2==1) or rice (+6); number_input(1, available); then develops the recipient — develop_loyalty + develop_wealth if arg3==1, else develop_morale. Giving resources raises the target fief's stats.
NesPrgRom:691E:give_eligibility_flags:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Builds a 2-bit givable-resource flag: bit1 set if arg2>0, bit0 set if arg1>0; returns the OR (0..3). For the Give command — arg1/arg2 are the two amounts available to give.
NesPrgRom:694D:give_rice_gold_eligibility:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Give-eligibility (gold/rice variant): returns give_eligibility_flags(fief gold *arg1, fief->rice) — the 2-bit flag of whether gold / rice can be given.
NesPrgRom:6B22:render_arms_edit_screen:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Renders the arms-allocation edit screen: for each of the 5 unit types, loads the province's allotment from province_unit_type_pct ($76A9 + selected_province_idx*5) into the arg2 word buffer, caps at 9999, draws it as "%3d" with the unit-type label (cursor col 5/14, rows 20-24).
NesPrgRom:6BBD:commit_arms_record_from_buffer:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Compares the edited arms buffer (arg1, 5 words) against the province's current allotment (province_unit_type_pct $76A9 + selected_province_idx*5); sets a dirty flag if any differ; if dirty and arg2==0, commits the buffer back. The arms-edit-screen save path.
NesPrgRom:6DF6:fief_select_input_loop:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] On-map fief selection: loads the fief's cell list from SRAM ($9E3C table, 34 bytes) into a buffer, then runs a cursor-input loop scanning the (x,y) cell entries (0xFF-terminated) to let the player pick a fief on the strategic map. arg1 = anchor fief.
NesPrgRom:72B2:ai_seed_fief_tax_rate:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Seeds fief arg1's tax rate to a random 35-64: swap_word(&arg1, battle_defending_province) installs arg1 as the active fief, fief_tax_rate ($6D2D)[that fief] = rng_mod(30)+35, then swap_word back. Net: fief_tax_rate[arg1] = rng+35. (was 'ai_seed_fief_collection_rate_6d2d'.)
NesPrgRom:72EF:ai_calc_men_surplus_over_gold_and_rice:[UNPARKED via call-graph reconcile 2026-05-31, HIGH] Computes two >=0-clamped surpluses into caller-supplied output pointers: *out1 = max(0, men(+16) - gold(+0)), *out2 = max(0, men(+16) - rice(+6)) ($B2F4-$B329). Called by ai_province_gold_to_rice_convert/ai_develop_town_handler/ai_develop_dam_and_grow/ai_state2_recruit_arm_train — drives AI spend decisions. Live $7001 map. Was REFUTED helper_B2EF.
NesPrgRom:732B:rng_threshold_10_29:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns rng_mod(20) + 10 = a uniform random 10..29 inclusive.
NesPrgRom:7338:ai_province_gold_to_rice_convert:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI gold<->rice conversion: 3/4 chance; rng_threshold_10_29 vs gold_rice_exchange_rate decides direction -- if low, sell half the rice surplus (effect_sell_rice_for_gold); if high, buy rice with the gold surplus (ratio_times10_capped, gold -= cost, rice += gain), cycle_economy_rate(2). Balances the AI economy by the market rate.
NesPrgRom:73AA:ai_develop_town_handler:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI town-development turn: ai_calc_men_surplus_over_gold_and_rice, ai_seed_fief_tax_rate, ai_province_gold_to_rice_convert; then if town (+4) < cap (+24) and a 2/3 roll, develops the town by an effect_send-derived gain (capped by year and gold surplus), debiting gold.
NesPrgRom:742B:ai_develop_dam_and_grow:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI develop driver: ai_calc_men_surplus_over_gold_and_rice -> gold/rice budgets; ai_seed_fief_tax_rate; if loyalty (+12) > output (+8), spends the gold budget on dams (effect_dam + add_effect_gain_clamped on the +10 dams field) and grows output. The AI economy-development turn.
NesPrgRom:74D5:ai_state2_recruit_arm_train:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI state-2 military turn: ai_try_war_attack first; else compute men/gold/rice surpluses and, scaled by game year and a skill-gated rng (rng_mod(10) < const_two+3), recruit men (gold_men_hire_rate), buy arms, and/or train -- the AI military buildup. Caller of scale_div10_capcheck.
NesPrgRom:764B:ai_econ_command_dispatch:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI economy command dispatch: ensures the fief has some rice; seeds capital men if empty; then on a 1/10 roll runs the military turn (ai_state2_recruit_arm_train), else economic development. The AI per-fief command chooser.
NesPrgRom:76B4:command_menu_select_loop:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] The lord-command menu selection loop: cursor at (21,7); polls until A (confirm -> selected command index) or B (cancel -> 17); fief_menu_info_mode_flag offsets the menu page (0 or 12). Returns the chosen command.
NesPrgRom:779B:issue_province_command:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Issues the command turn for a fief: if its owner is resting (rest counter $6D67[owner]>0) and it is the capital, just show the view and decrement the rest counter (+ bump a daimyo stat); else effect_view_c then proceed to the command menu. Per-fief turn entry.
NesPrgRom:7875:ai_econ_action_state0:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI economic action (ai-state 0): ai_econ_command_dispatch, random_daimyo_stat_increment, and on a 1/4 roll bumps the arms field ($7001+22). One AI fief's economy turn.
NesPrgRom:789B:ai_per_fief_command_driver:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] ai_per_fief_command_driver -- THE bank-1 root (depth 7, the AI turn loop). For each acting fief (ai_per_fief_loop_index): sets ui_input_mode, resets+rolls ai_turn_flags (trade flag = rng_mod(100) < 55-const_two*5 difficulty-scaled; weakness abort flag), checks game-over (count_6da2_set / is_ai_count_ge_8), and dispatches that fief's command (issue_province_command / ai econ-or-military). The main per-fief turn driver.
NesPrgRom:7B36:cycle_economy_rate_fmt:[ROM-STR] "%2d.%1d": cycle_economy_rate prints a value in tenths (v / 10 . v % 10)
NesPrgRom:7B49:msg_has_retreated:[ROM-STR] " has\nretreated" (resolve_siege_assault_outcome)
NesPrgRom:7B58:msg_has_fled:[ROM-STR] " has fled" (resolve_siege_assault_outcome)
NesPrgRom:7E59:effect_assign_fmt_3d_1:[ROM-STR] "%3d" (effect_assign, 1st of 4)
NesPrgRom:7E5D:effect_assign_fmt_3d_2:[ROM-STR] "%3d" (effect_assign, 2nd of 4)
NesPrgRom:7E61:effect_assign_fmt_3d_3:[ROM-STR] "%3d" (effect_assign, 3rd of 4)
NesPrgRom:7E65:effect_assign_fmt_3d_4:[ROM-STR] "%3d" (effect_assign, 4th of 4)
NesPrgRom:4000:bank1_entry:[HIGH 2026-10-28] Bank 1 entry point: 3 bytes, JMP $B89B (ai_per_fief_command_driver), the target call_bank_wrap(1) reaches. Read from the ROM bytes; labelled like bank0_entry.
NesPrgRom:8004:map_tile_gfx_8004:[GFX-TILES 2026-06-10] Strategic-map tile-upload source (ppu_upload_block_wrap, map_render_driver).
NesPrgRom:9C25:daimyo_banner_chr:[ROM-DATA; RECLASSIFIED 2026-06-12] DAIMYO BANNER (家紋/crest) CHR — NOT map terrain tiles. 3 tiles (48 B) per daimyo, stride 49 (the preceding byte $9C24+idx*49 = the banner's attribute/palette byte). upload_map_cell_tiles($882A) blits the owning daimyo's banner to PT1 $1510 (per side) for the battlefield unit display; drawn next to the O/X leader marker (tile 178 daimyo-led / 179 general-led) + the men-count digits in each unit cell's lower half. Index = fief_to_mapid(owner) ($DC66): 17-fief -> province_to_mapid_table[daimyo], 50-fief -> daimyo index directly. Decoded + rendered to a labeled chart per scenario by tools/render-daimyo-banners.py (the crests are shared across scenarios; only the index arithmetic differs). Was the misleading 'map_cell_tile_source'.
NesPrgRom:A604:digit_gfx_a604:[GFX-TILES 2026-06-10] Number-digit tile source (ppu_upload_block_wrap, unpack_base5_digits_upload).
NesPrgRom:A9C4:digit_gfx_a9c4:[GFX-TILES 2026-06-10] Number-digit tile source (unpack_base5_digits_upload).
NesPrgRom:AD84:digit_gfx_ad84:[GFX-TILES 2026-06-10] Number-digit tile source (unpack_base5_digits_upload).
NesPrgRom:AEAC:digit_sram_aeac:[SRAM-ADDR 2026-06-10] SRAM work region for unpack_base5_digits_upload.
NesPrgRom:B0BA:strategic_map_fief_x:[HIGH CONFIRMED] 50-byte table: strategic-map X coordinate per fief (indexed by fief_to_mapid). Read by select_quadrant_damage_by_direction to compute attack bearing dx = X[att]-X[def]. X spans 3..77 (W->E). VERIFIED 2026-06-01: adjacency neighbors (bank4 $8004) are spatially nearest, mean dist-rank 2.8 / median 2.
NesPrgRom:B0EC:strategic_map_fief_y:[HIGH CONFIRMED] 50-byte table: strategic-map Y coordinate per fief (indexed by fief_to_mapid). Read by select_quadrant_damage_by_direction; dy = Y[att]-Y[def]; |dx|<|dy| picks vertical axis else horizontal, sign picks the entry edge. Y spans 3..31 (N->S). Ends at $B11E. VERIFIED 2026-06-01 vs adjacency.
NesPrgRom:B11E:terrain_attr_table:[ROM-DATA 2026-06-10; type map confirmed 2026-06-17] 6 terrain-attribute records, 16 bytes each = a 4x4 metatile tile-block per terrain type, indexed by terrain type 0..5 (lookup_terrain_attr_record $83C6: cell&$FE bit->type; 32->0,16->1,8->2,128->3,4->4,64/none->5). Types: 0=castle(tiles 63-72), 1=forest(A2-B1), 2=town(73-81), 3=mountain(92-A1), 4=clear(82-91), 5=river/sea(57-66). Types 0/1/2 carry the +270/+60/+30% combat bonus (ai_terrain_strength_term $9BB4 / terrain_strength_mult_table $B9C2); 3/4/5 give 0. Immediately preceded by strategic_map_fief_y ($B0EC, ends at $B11E). first bytes: 63 64 67 68 65 66 69 6a 6b 6c 6f 70. (was 'lookup_terrain_attr_reco_data_b11e'.)
NesPrgRom:B144:fief_tile_block_tiles:[ROM-DATA 2026-06-10] Tile IDs for the fief graphic block (build_blit_fief_tile_block); 36-byte 6x6 cell.
NesPrgRom:B196:combat_message_table:[ROM-DATA HIGH 2026-06-10] Word-ptr table of >=10 combat announcement strings (bank 2), read by announce_combat_side_daimyo_and_status, draw_combat_message ($936A), redraw_combat_side_window. Verified entries: [0] blank, [1] '..men have deserted to our..', [2] 'Some of our men have des..', [3] 'You can`t move there!', [4] 'we seem to have the upper..', [5] 'Enemy unit %d has been..', [6] 'they`ve counter-attacked', [7] 'Unit %d has been wiped out', [8] 'we have taken an enemy a..', [9] 'Which unit shall we go a..'. (was 'jumptab_b196'.)
NesPrgRom:B4F0:combat_command_menu_str_ptrs:[ROM-DATA 2026-06-10] Word-ptrs to combat-command menu items: Move/Attack/Bribe/Flee/Pass/View (combat_command_dispatch_loop_per_unit).
NesPrgRom:B51E:str_keypad_yn_prompt:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] '8 9 ( 0  (Y/N)?','8932170 (%d-%d)' direction keypad
NesPrgRom:B540:map_scroll_marker_tiles:[ROM-DATA 2026-06-10] Scroll-arrow + section marker tiles for the tactical map (map_render_driver).
NesPrgRom:B542:map_scroll_marker_tiles_a:[ROM-DATA 2026-06-10] +offset alias of map_scroll_marker_tiles ($B540).
NesPrgRom:B544:map_scroll_marker_tiles_b:[ROM-DATA 2026-06-10] +offset alias of map_scroll_marker_tiles ($B540).
NesPrgRom:B547:map_scroll_marker_tiles_c:[ROM-DATA 2026-06-10] +offset alias of map_scroll_marker_tiles ($B540).
NesPrgRom:B54A:map_water_cell_tile:[ROM-DATA 2026-06-10] The default (water/border) tactical map cell tile data, 0x01 fill (map_populate fallback).
NesPrgRom:B55A:combat_map_palette:[HIGH CONFIRMED] 16-byte NES palette (4 sub-palettes) for the tactical battle screen; loaded by render_combat_map_screen via the 16-iter palette_write_wrap loop. Followed at $B56A by msg_day_2d. bytes: 3e 16 38 30 3e 1a 2a 3c 3e 1c 38 30 3e 01 3c 30
NesPrgRom:B5B1:battle_strength_stat_weights:[CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] 8 per-stat weights for ai_sum_battle_strength's attacker-vs-defender tally = [HEALTH 5, DRIVE 10, LUCK 10, CHARISMA 5, IQ 20] (daimyo record +1..+5) then [morale 10, skill 25, arms 15] (province +18/+20/+22). For each stat the side that wins it adds the weight to its battle-strength score; skill (25) is the biggest term, IQ (20) the top daimyo stat. Drives the AI engage/avoid decision, NOT per-attack damage (the charisma capture contest). bytes (decimal): 05 10 10 05 20 10 25 15, then 0xFE terminator. (CORRECTED 2026-06-10: prior note had only 7 weights, missing arms=15.)
NesPrgRom:B5B9:unit_presence_clear_masks:[ROM-DATA 2026-06-10] 5 AND-masks to clear unit-presence bit n in war_side_state_flag: [0xFE,0xFD,0xFB,0xF7,0xEF] = ~(1<<n) for slots 0..4. Read by remove_unit ($8F97). (Bytes after the 5 masks belong to adjacent data.)
NesPrgRom:B626:combat_msg_blank_str:[ROM-STR 2026-06-10] Single $00 = blank string at $B626 (the byte immediately before msg_unit_d_s $B627 'unit %d\n%s'); message_display of it homes/clears the combat message line. Read by draw_combat_message ($936A). (was 'draw_combat_ui_string_data_b626' — not a table, just the leading NUL.)
NesPrgRom:B632:jumptab_b632:[ROM-DATA] pointer/dispatch table; read by announce_battle_outcome_retreat_or_won via imm-word ptr; bytes: 68 b6 9b b6 ba b6 fc b6 2e b7 5c b7
NesPrgRom:B640:battle_conclusion_msgs_loser:[CONFIRMED 2026-06-02] 6 LE string pointers indexed by (outcome_code-1) in announce_battle_outcome_retreat_or_won — the LOSER's-view battle-end messages: [1]$B7B1 'this is truly unfortunate...', [2]$B7CE 'someday we will avenge this outrage!', [3]$B7F3 'your men are exhausted!'(timeout), [4]$B80B 'supply reports... out of rice'(rice<=0), [5]$B848 'the command unit has been destroyed!'(commander), [6]$B87B 'not a single soldier remains'(annihilation).
NesPrgRom:B650:battle_conclusion_msgs_observer:[CONFIRMED 2026-06-02] 4 LE string pointers — the third-person/observer battle-end messages: [1]$B8D1 '<lord> is out of rice and must surrender', [2]$B8F4 "<lord>'s command unit has been wiped out", [3]$B929 "<lord>'s men have been completely destroyed", [4]$B94F '<lord> has no soldiers / He has lost'. Pairs with battle_conclusion_msgs_loser by outcome code.
