NesPrgRom:AFE1:battle_init_driver:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Battle-init driver (bank-2 entry, $8000 = JMP here) and ROOT of the bank-2 call tree (depth 13): ui_input_mode=3, sram_save_checksum = rng_mod(4)+53, repaint_screen, audio (call_bank10_entry(2)), map_populate (ROM->staging), render_combat_map_screen (staging->PPU), battle_init_defender, draw_combat_fief_day_header, latch the map section; then dispatch_battle_resolution(result). Run headless via probe-map-emit.py / render-rom-to-map.py.
NesPrgRom:8903:map_populate:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Tactical-map POPULATOR: per cell, is_cell_clear_of_bits(col,row,2) ? lookup_terrain_attr_record : default attr ($B54A=water/border); expands the per-fief cell data from ROM into the SRAM staging buffer at $7BFD (11 cols x 88 stride, 5 rows of metatiles). Inputs: battle_defending_province ($6F63) + scenario_fief_count ($6D9D); source = tactical_map_cell_pool ($A57E, bank 4) via province_to_mapid_table ($F70E). Reads cells one byte at a time through syscall_memcpy_banked ($10). Verified cell-exact on Mino/Tanba/Ezo + the whole 50-fief atlas. Returns clean with only memcpy syscalls.
NesPrgRom:885E:map_render_driver:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Renders the tactical battle map for the current tactical_battle_phase: (1) blits the 5 visible columns (screen X = i*4+10, i=0..4) from the $7BFD staging buffer at source offset (phase*3 + i)*88 — the phase*3 scroll matches is_cell_valid_for_phase/calc_tactical_cell_coords; (2) uploads the map background (fief_to_mapid(battle_defending_province)*144 + phase*48 + $8004) to PPU $23C8; (3) draws phase-conditional scroll markers at screen cols 11 (left arrow if phase>0, else label) and 27 (right arrow if phase!=2, else label). Staging->PPU, NOT the populator (map_populate $8903).
NesPrgRom:8086:compose_upload_daimyo_portrait:[HIGH VISUAL 2026-06-01] DAIMYO COMPOSITE-PORTRAIT composer. Reads the packed base-5 face code *($6EB1 + 2*daimyo_idx[$6F5B]), splits it into base-5 feature digits (repeated /5,%5), then uploads each feature's variant tile block from BANK 8 to CHR-RAM via ppu_upload_block ($CF7C, bank arg=8): feature0 $A604+d*192->CHR$17F0, f1 $A9C4+d*96->$18B0, f2 $ABA4+d*96->$1910, f3 $AD84+d*192->$1970 (the 4 portrait_feature*_tiles); then 4 $CBBD sram-wrap writes ($AE34/$AE70/$AE8E/$AEAC = the face attribute/layout record). Assembles a 6x6 (48x48px) face. VISUALLY VERIFIED via tools/render-portrait.py (faces render as recognizable daimyo). (was unpack_base5_digits_upload_blocks.)
NesPrgRom:822A:prompt_yes_no:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Modal Yes/No prompt: redraws the (Y/N) window (msg_y_n_b526), polls wait_button_edge until A(0x40) or B(0x80). A -> echoes 'Y' (char 89) and returns 1; B -> echoes 'N' (char 78) and returns 0. Frame-timer bracketed (read_frame_timer 1/0).
NesPrgRom:8270:set_tactical_cursor_pos:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Sets the tactical-map cursor origin: tactical_cursor_cell_7bf5 ($7BF5, col/X) = arg1, tactical_cursor_row_7bf7 ($7BF7, row/Y) = arg2; returns arg2. draw_tactical_cursor_region ($840B) consumes the pair to draw/erase the 4x4 selection cursor; callers push a unit's $6FD0/$6FDA coords. (was 'set_combat_state_pair_7bf5_7bf7'.)
NesPrgRom:827E:side_resource_ptr:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Address of a combat SIDE's resource pool: arg1*6 + $6F7D, arg1 = combat side (0/1). 3 word fields: +0 gold, +2 rice, +4 men. Field labels from msg_gold_4d_rice_4d_men_4d rosetta @ $08C4F; daily-ration check men/15<=rice @ $0838E; men cap 9999 @ $09EFA; gold spend @ $09E84. (was 'unit_record_ptr', '+4 = hp/damage' — REFUTED: per-side gold/rice/men, not a per-unit record.)
NesPrgRom:828B:unit_col_ptr:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] &byte = a unit's tactical-map COLUMN (X): arg1*5 + arg2 + $6FD0, arg1=side (0/1), arg2=slot (0..4, 5 slots/side). Coordinate pair with unit_row_ptr ($6FDA): unit-present-at-(col,row) scan @ $8FC7/$A079, off-map sentinel 200 written @ $8FBE. (was generic 'unit_field_ptr_6fd0 arg1=row/arg2=column'.)
NesPrgRom:829A:unit_row_ptr:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] &byte = a unit's tactical-map ROW (Y): arg1*5 + arg2 + $6FDA, arg1=side, arg2=slot; sibling X-column at $6FD0 ($828B, +10 bytes). draw_terrain_feature_if_valid(col,row) @ $09082; off-map sentinel 200 @ $8FBD. (was 'unit_field_ptr_6fda'.)
NesPrgRom:82C9:unit_strength_ptr:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] &word = a unit's STRENGTH (troop count): $6FBC + arg1*10 + arg2*2, arg1=side (5 words/side), arg2=slot. Capped to 9999 via min_word @ $08A57; read as base_strength @ $09C97; casualty subtract / reinforce add attrition @ $09F63/$09F83. (was generic 'unit_word_field_ptr_6fbc word-field table'.)
NesPrgRom:82DB:is_cell_clear_of_bits:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns 1 if cell (col,row) is CLEAR of mask arg3: off-map (col>10||row>4) -> 1, else (read_map_cell($DC88) & arg3) ? 0 : 1. So 1 = passable / no masked bits, 0 = a masked terrain/edge bit IS set. REFUTES the old 'returns whether bits are set, 0 on out-of-bounds' note — polarity was backwards on BOTH counts. (was 'test_map_cell_bits'.)
NesPrgRom:82FF:is_no_province_selected:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns selected_province_idx ($6F5F) == 50; 50 = one-past-last sentinel (valid fiefs 0-49) = the "no/invalid province selected" guard. ~15 combat/UI sites branch-skip when true.
NesPrgRom:838F:get_battle_side_province:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Maps a battle side to its province index: side 0 = attacker = selected_province_idx ($6F5F), side!=0 = defender = battle_defending_province ($6F63). 25 callers — the side->province resolver. Confirms cur_combat_side polarity 0=attacker/1=defender.
NesPrgRom:83A2:calc_tactical_cell_coords:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] In-place (col,row)->screen-coord transform via two output ptrs: *row = (*row+1)*4 + (*col&1)*2 (Y, odd-col stagger); *col = (*col - tactical_battle_phase*3)*4 + 10 (X, window scrolls 3 cells/phase). The phase*3 scroll matches is_cell_valid_for_phase's per-phase cell window (cross-confirm). NOTE: bank-1 also has a $83A2 (province_window_redraw_ba6f) — a legit same-CPU-addr/different-bank pair, NOT a mis-key.
NesPrgRom:83C6:lookup_terrain_attr_record:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Reads map cell (col,row) terrain byte (read_map_cell $DC88) & 0xFE, maps the terrain bit to a type index via fall-through switch: 32->0, 16->1, 8->2, 128->3, 4->4, 64/none->5; returns &terrain_attr_table[type] = ($B11E + type*16). 6 terrain types, 16-byte records.
NesPrgRom:8488:read_dpad_dir_code:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Polls the controller (poll_input) and maps d-pad bit combos to a 48-based DIRECTION CODE (52/54/56/...) consumed by step_coord_from_dir_code ((code-48)>>1)-1; 0/other = no direction. (was 'read_button_press' — it specifically returns the hex-grid dir code.)
NesPrgRom:84F7:step_coord_by_direction:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Moves the tactical position (*arg1=col, *arg2=row) one cell by direction arg3 (switch 0..3: dir0 row+1, dir1 col-1, dir2 col+1, dir3 row-1; returns 0 if arg3>=4), then validates the result via is_tile_in_bounds ($8F11) — out-of-range returns 0.
NesPrgRom:8792:prompt_province_selection:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Modal cursor-pick prompt: draws the range window (msg_d_d_b536 "%d %d", arg1/arg2 = min/max), runs select_province_by_cursor(arg1,arg2), clears the lower-left rect unless the result is 0 or 1; returns the picked index (0=cancel, 1=special/no-confirm). Reused in combat to pick a target unit slot (caller $A9FB, list-size 5).
NesPrgRom:882A:upload_map_cell_tiles:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Uploads one map cell's tile block: syscall16_sram_wrap(5, src=arg1*49+$9C24, dst=arg2*9+$6FE4, 1) then ppu_upload_block_wrap(5, src=arg1*49+$9C25, dst=arg2*48+$1510, 3). arg1 = source tile-block index (stride 49), arg2 = destination map-cell index (stride 9 SRAM / 48 PPU @ $1510). CORRECTS the prior note, which had the syscall arg order reversed and src/dst swapped.
NesPrgRom:8B39:draw_combat_day_header:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] At cursor (2,5): draw_current_year(), spacing, draw_current_season(), then draw_message(msg_day_2d "Day %2d", arg1) — arg1 = battle day number. The year/season/day header line for the combat screen.
NesPrgRom:8E40:ai_score_strength_term_40pct:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Strength adjustment term: returns strength_base + pct_op(pct_op(strength_base,40), battle_side_strength_mod[side_idx*2 + $7BEA]) — i.e. base + 40%-of-base scaled by the per-side modifier. side_idx 0=attacker, 1=defender (caller $8F10 compares attacker vs defender adjusted men; also an addend in the $9CDC engagement-strength sum).
NesPrgRom:8E5C:ai_sum_battle_strength:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] WRITER of battle_side_strength_mod ($7BEA attacker / $7BEC defender): zeroes both, then for 8 stats compares attacker vs defender; the side that WINS (>) each stat adds its battle_strength_stat_weights entry to its accumulator. loop1 5x = daimyo-record bytes +1..+5 (HEALTH/DRIVE/LUCK/CHARISMA/IQ, attacker=selected_province_daimyo_record, defender=fief_to_daimyo_record_addr($6F63)); loop2 3x (i=5,6,7) = province-record words at idx*26+$7013 +18/+20/+22 (morale/skill/arms). Feeds ai_score_strength_term_40pct ($8E40). (Prior note said 'loop2 7x' + 2 province stats — actually 3 iterations incl. arms.)
NesPrgRom:8F11:is_tile_in_bounds:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Tactical-grid bounds predicate: 1 iff col(arg1)<=10 AND row(arg2)<=4 — the combat tile map is 11 wide (cols 0-10) x 5 tall (rows 0-4).
NesPrgRom:8F28:validate_dir_code_and_dispatch:[MED CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Validates a hex-grid direction code arg3 and dispatches: REJECTS exactly {52,53,54} (returns 0); valid codes {49,50,51,55,56,57} remap to dir 0..5 via (arg3-49) then -3 when the original >=55, then tail-call coord-stepper $8003(arg1,arg2,dir). REFUTES the prior note ('returns 0 if code>=55' — backwards: >=55 dispatches; the gap 52-54 is rejected). The C's '(arg3-49)>=6' is a value-reuse artifact for 'original code >=55'. NOTE: bank-2 $8003 (coord stepper) still unground.
NesPrgRom:813C:build_blit_fief_tile_block:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Renders active_province_idx_copy's fief tile block (gated on daimyo_record(fief)+6 == 0): loads 4 palette entries ($B51E), pulls a tile descriptor (fief_to_mapid*4 + $BBD0) from SRAM, ppu_upload_block_wrap, then builds a 36-byte (6x6) tile buffer from fief_to_mapid*36 + $B144 (each cell +36 tile-base) and blits at (dst_col, dst_row).
NesPrgRom:82A9:cur_unit_col_ptr:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Current unit's MAP-COLUMN (X) address: unit_col_ptr(cur_combat_side $7BE8, cur_combat_unit_slot $7BE4). (Old comment mislabeled $7BE8 'current-field index' and $7BE4 'current-unit index' — both REFUTED: $7BE8=side, $7BE4=slot.)
NesPrgRom:82B9:cur_unit_row_ptr:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Current unit's MAP-ROW (Y) address: unit_row_ptr(cur_combat_side $7BE8, cur_combat_unit_slot $7BE4); mirror of $82A9 (column). (Old comment's $7BE4/$7BE8 'unit/field index' labels REFUTED.)
NesPrgRom:836A:side_has_rice_for_day:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Daily-ration check: returns ceil(men/15) <= rice for side arg1, reading side_resource_ptr +4=men and +2=rice. True = enough rice to feed the army one day; caller applies STARVATION casualties on the false branch. REFUTES old name+note ('unit_damage_within_strength', +4=damage/+2=strength) — built on the refuted unit_record_ptr reading; these are the per-side rice/men pool.
NesPrgRom:840B:draw_tactical_cursor_region:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Draws (arg1==1) or erases (else) the tactical selection cursor as a 4x4 block of 16 sprites: bails if !is_cell_valid_for_phase(cursor_cell). Draw path seeds col/row from $7BF5/$7BF7, calc_tactical_cell_coords, then 16x syscall_set_sprite at (col<<3, (row<<3)-1) advancing col with row-wrap at (col+1)&3==2. Erase path parks all 16 sprites at (248,248). Callers blink it around input polling.
NesPrgRom:8544:step_coord_from_dir_code:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] If dir code arg3 != 48 ('0' sentinel = no move), decode to a direction index via ((code-48)>>1)-1 then step (*arg1,*arg2) one cell via step_coord_by_direction ($84F7); else return 0.
NesPrgRom:87B7:draw_tactical_terrain_feature:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Per-cell terrain renderer: ONLY when the cell is CLEAR of bit 2 (!is_cell_clear_of_bits(arg1,arg2,2) is false) -> calc_tactical_cell_coords, lookup_terrain_attr_record, ppu_copy_rect_wrap the tile at attr+8, then switch on attr[0] (terrain-type marker) for feature variants. CORRECTS prior note: it draws when bit 2 is CLEAR, not set (bit 2 = water/border = skip).
NesPrgRom:8977:render_combat_map_screen:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Full combat-map setup: palette_swap(1), 16x palette_write_wrap from combat_map_palette, PPU tile block upload; uploads the ATTACKER cell (upload_map_cell_tiles(mapid,0); mapid = fief_to_mapid(selected_province_owner()), or sram_save_checksum when is_no_province_selected) and the DEFENDER cell (upload_map_cell_tiles(fief_to_mapid(fief_owner(battle_defending_province)),1)); sets tactical_battle_phase=0, map_render_driver(), palette_swap(0).
NesPrgRom:8B8A:draw_side_resource_field:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10, bytecode-verified] Combat resource readout: gated on combat_unit_window_mode_flag ($7BFB)==2; saves cursor ($7FCD/$7FCF), set_cursor(6, (side?9:15)+arg2), draws side_resource_ptr(arg1) field arg2 as "%4d" (msg $B574), restores cursor. arg1=side, arg2=stat: switch 0=+0 gold / 1=+2 rice / 2=+4 men. FIXED 2026-06-11 (deref-consumer value_merge_phis): cases now read +0/+2/+4 correctly; ORACLE-CERTIFIED vs ROM (gold/rice/men). (was 'draw_unit_stat_field' — it's per-SIDE resources, not unit stats; no unit_record_ptr involved.)
NesPrgRom:8BEA:combat_unit_window_refresh:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Skips if combat_unit_window_mode_flag==2; else clear_rect_left_upper, then for each side (local11 1->0) draws the lord NAME (daimyo_name_table $77A8) + draw_message(msg_gold_4d_rice_4d_men_4d, side_resource_ptr gold/rice/men), and sets the mode flag=2. WARNING DREAM value bug: the attacker name source (selected_province_owner $D77E @ $8C17) is dropped in 4-c — both rows render fief_owner(battle_defending_province); bytecode arms reconverge at the shared *9+$77A8 tail (same family as $8B8A).
NesPrgRom:8C61:draw_unit_roster_columns:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Renders side arg1's battle-roster column (ui_window_col=(arg1+1)*12): seeds side_resource_ptr (local9), province military record (local10 = get_battle_side_province*26+$7013) and daimyo record (local11), then a do-loop over the rows dispatching on ui_cursor_row to advance a pointer +2 and emit a %4d/---- column string ($B591-$B5A2) per stat, ending at the draw call $E76F (20,24).
NesPrgRom:8D39:draw_combat_fief_day_header:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] set_cursor(2,3), redraw_window_row(battle_defending_province), draw_message(msg_fief_2d "Fief %2d", battle_defending_province+1), then draw_combat_day_header(1) for the year/season/Day line. The defending-fief + date banner.
NesPrgRom:8EF5:ai_attacker_outstrengths_defender:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] The AI engage/avoid gate: ai_sum_battle_strength() (fills battle_side_strength_mod), then returns ai_score_strength_term_40pct(war_attacker_men, 0) > ai_score_strength_term_40pct(war_defender_men, 1) — true when the attacker's stat-adjusted men exceed the defender's. (war_attacker_men=$6F81, war_defender_men=$6F87.)
NesPrgRom:8F55:end_war_relocate_capital:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Conquest finalization: clears bit 7 (war/siege state) of war_side_state_flag[cur_combat_side] (&127), then RELOCATES the daimyo capital — fief_is_daimyo_capital[from_fief]=0, fief_is_daimyo_capital[to_fief]=1. Returns 1. REFUTES old name+note ('clear_unit_combat_flags / zeros $6DA2 for both' — to_fief is SET to 1, not zeroed; this is a capital move). (was 'clear_unit_combat_flags'.)
NesPrgRom:8F79:is_unit_present:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10, bytecode-verified] Returns bit arg2 of byte[$6F65 + arg1] (war_side_state_flag), guarded arg2<5. arg1 = combat side (0/1), arg2 = unit slot (0..4) -> tests whether that side's unit slot is present. Bytecode @ $8F84: LOADL 12, +$6F65, BYTE_DEREF, >>local13, &1 — it DOES index $6F65 (disproves the $6F65 note's 'indexes $6DA2' claim). Implies $6F65[side] is a PACKED byte: bits 0-4 = unit-slot presence, bit 7 = war/siege state. (was 'test_unit_type_present_flag'; 'type' is really the slot index.)
NesPrgRom:8F97:remove_unit:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Removes unit (arg1=side, arg2=slot): clears its presence bit in war_side_state_flag[side] via AND-mask unit_presence_clear_masks[slot] (= ~(1<<slot)), then off-maps it (unit_row/unit_col = 200, the off-map sentinel). (was 'clear_unit_status_flag_set_field_200'.)
NesPrgRom:8FC0:side_has_unit_at_cell:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Scans side arg1's 5 unit slots; returns 1 if any unit is at (col=arg2, row=arg3) — unit_col[slot]==arg2 AND unit_row[slot]==arg3 — else 0. (was 'find_unit_slot_by_fields'; returns a bool, not a slot index.)
NesPrgRom:900A:wrap_index_0_2_to_zero:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Wraps a 0..2 index: if arg > 2 (unsigned) resets it to 0, else leaves it; returns the index. Wrap-to-zero, not saturating clamp.
NesPrgRom:9019:is_map_cell_blocked:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns 1 if cell (arg1,arg2) has any blocking bit of mask 0xC2 (bits 7,6,1) set, else 0 — = !is_cell_clear_of_bits(arg1,arg2,0xC2). (was 'test_map_cell_blocked_c2'; dropped the mask-value suffix.)
NesPrgRom:9030:battleside_not_state5_or_resting:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns (get_province_ai_state(get_battle_side_province(side)) != 5) || rest_turns_remaining[fief_owner(fief)] — TRUE when the side's province is NOT in ai_state 5, OR its owner is resting; FALSE only when state==5 AND not resting. REFUTES old name+note ('true iff state5 AND not resting') — that is the exact negation. (ai_state 5 = available/selectable marker.)
NesPrgRom:90BB:build_daimyo_province_list:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Builds the list of fiefs owned by fief's daimyo: target_owner=fief_owner(fief); scans the 0xFF-terminated province list at $6F4F, skipping province_state_is_FF entries, appending fiefs whose fief_owner==target to a local buffer, 0xFF-terminates, then syscall16_sram_wrap(2, &buf, deduped_owner_list, 8) copies buf->deduped_owner_list. (Prior note had the syscall arg order reversed + src/dst swapped: source is $6F4F, dest is deduped_owner_list.)
NesPrgRom:9675:set_combat_arena_rect_by_approach:[ORACLE-CONFIRMED 2026-06-02, renamed from select_quadrant_damage_by_direction] Sets the tactical-arena bounding rect ($6FF6/$6FF8/$6FFA/$6FFC = x_min/y_min/x_max/y_max) to the ATTACKER's entry strip, from the compass bearing between the two fiefs' STRATEGIC-map coords (strategic_map_fief_x $B0BA / _y $B0EC, indexed by fief_to_mapid; |dx| vs |dy| via abs16 picks axis, sign picks edge). Default full grid (0,0,10,4). Returns the entry-edge code {1=N,2=S,3=W,4=E} (0 on the no-op path: defender side or no province) -- consumed by ai_place_combat_units_random_or_smart for deployment, NOT damage. The old 'damage formula' reading was a pre-decompiler misnomer. Proof: tools/probe-combat-arena.py.
NesPrgRom:9C69:ai_strength_term_gated_table_word:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI strength term: if wrap_index_0_2_to_zero(idx) > wrap_index_0_2_to_zero(gate_idx) returns unit_strength_ptr(unit, idx) word, else 0; one conditional addend in the engagement strength-sum chain.
NesPrgRom:830B:consume_daily_battle_rice:[CORRECTED 2026-06-02, was apply_unit_damage_over_30 — it's NOT damage] The daily RICE/SUPPLY drain. Per side: rice(unit_record+2) -= live_men(unit_record+4)/30 (+%30 carried remainder), clamped >=0; redraws the stat field. An army of `men` eats `men/30` rice/day => ~`men` rice over a full ~30-day battle; rice 0 -> 'you have no rice!' terminator = the rice-exhaustion/doughnut-fief mechanic + the real '31-day limit'. The per-side battle record $6F7D+6*side = {+0 gold, +2 rice, +4 men} ($8BEA Gold/Rice/Men display). Cross-dump proof: tools/probe-combat-bleed.py (rice drains men-proportionally while men & $6FBC slots hold). Decoupled from kills (apply_pct_reduction_to_unit_strength) and capture (resolve_attack_apply_casualties).
NesPrgRom:8561:wait_button_press_debounced:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Blinking-cursor debounced input wait: set_tactical_cursor_pos(arg1,arg2), blinks draw_tactical_cursor_region, polls read_dpad_dir_code in a 100-iter loop until a direction registers, then returns it.
NesPrgRom:8D5D:draw_combat_roster_window:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Builds the combat roster window: palette_swap + window-chrome fills/renders (ppu_fill_rect/ppu_render_rect), resets ui_input_sel_latch_7fdf=255 and combat_unit_window_mode_flag=0, prints each side's lord name (daimyo_name_table $77A8, or select_uprising_message when is_no_province_selected), then draws_unit_roster_columns(0) and (1).
NesPrgRom:8FEC:is_any_unit_at_tile:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns 1 if EITHER side has a unit at tile (col=arg1, row=arg2) — loops sides 0..1 calling side_has_unit_at_cell, early-returns on first match, else 0. (was 'find_unit_at_tile'; returns a bool, not a unit.)
NesPrgRom:910C:prompt_hit_any_key_return_button:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] set_cursor(2,24), redraw_window(msg_hit_any_key), blocks on wait_button_edge, clear_rect_left_lower, reset_prompt_selection; returns the captured button-edge code (caller tests ==2 to cancel).
NesPrgRom:91A1:prompt_select_province_from_list:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] select_province_by_cursor(1, scenario_fief_count) -> 1-based pick; converts to 0-based, scans the 0xFF-terminated province list at $6F4F (built by build_daimyo_province_list $90BB) for membership; returns the matched 0-based index, or 255 if cancelled / not in list.
NesPrgRom:91D5:distribute_men_into_unit_strengths:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Battle setup: for each side, splits the army's total MEN (side_resource +4) across the 5 unit_strength columns ($6FBC + side*10) proportionally to that province's unit-type composition percentages (province_unit_type_pct, $76A9 + prov*5) via pct_op; sets all 5 presence bits (war_side_state_flag[side] |= 31), runs a remainder pass for leftover men, and remove_unit's any zero-strength slot. REFUTES old name+note ('damage'): +4 is MEN, not damage (the unit_record_ptr hangover). (was 'distribute_damage_across_unit_types'.)
NesPrgRom:929C:clear_all_unit_positions:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Battle-init: off-maps every unit — sets unit_col and unit_row to 200 (the off-map sentinel) for both sides (0..1) x all 5 slots (0..4). (was 'reset_unit_field_grid_to_200'.)
NesPrgRom:936A:draw_combat_message:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Draws combat announcement string #arg1 from combat_message_table ($B196) for unit slot arg2: homes the message line (message_display of blank combat_msg_blank_str $B626), then draw_message(table[arg1], arg2+2) where arg2+2 fills the string's '%d' unit number. arg1 reaches >=8 (table has >=10 entries). Caller announce_combat_side_daimyo_and_status passes idx 5 ('Enemy unit %d has been..') vs 7 ('Unit %d has been wiped out') by side. (was 'draw_combat_ui_string_b196'.)
NesPrgRom:9387:draw_unit_type_label:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Draws "unit %d\n%s" (msg_unit_d_s $B627) for the current unit via draw_message: %d = cur_combat_unit_slot ($7BE4)+1, %s = unit-type name from unit_type_name_table ($F9AF) indexed by (wrap_index_0_2_to_zero(slot)+1)%3 -> 'Rifles'/'Infntry'/'Cavalry' (verified in ROM). Per-unit give-orders UI. (was 'draw_unit_label_b627'; the b627 suffix was the adjacent string, not this code.)
NesPrgRom:93AA:announce_battle_outcome_retreat_or_won:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Battle-end announce for province arg1: repaint_screen, loads the victory palette+graphic (msg_the_enemy_has_turned_tail_and, ppu block @ $83BC), then branches on get_province_ai_state(arg1) and whether arg1==battle_winner_province_sel to show '%s has retreated' vs 'hung on to the end and won' (arg2 capped at 7). (Bank-2 $93AA; a different bank's $93AA is ravage_defender_loyalty — same CPU addr, distinct banks.)
NesPrgRom:95BE:erase_cursor_advance_phase:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Erases the tactical cursor (draw_tactical_cursor_region(0)), then ADVANCES tactical_battle_phase based on arg1 (cursor column): from phase 0 -> (col>=8 ? 2 : 1); phase 1 -> (col>5 ? 2 : 0); etc. REFUTES old note ('thin wrapper, not phase-gated') — it transitions the phase, which the prior comment missed entirely. (was 'draw_tactical_cursor_region_arg0'.)
NesPrgRom:960E:is_cell_valid_for_phase:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Valid-cell gate for the current tactical_battle_phase ($6FFE): returns 1 iff cell index arg1 is in the phase's 5-cell window — phase0: 0-4, phase1: 3-7, phase2: 6-10 (window advances 3 cells/phase). Cross-confirmed by calc_tactical_cell_coords ($83A2) subtracting phase*3. REFUTES the old note ('phase1 arg1>=8, phase2 arg1>5 return 0') — it dropped the lower bound and flipped phase2's polarity.
NesPrgRom:9647:find_free_tactical_placement_cell:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Scans tactical cells (col local11 outer x row local10 0..4 inner); on the first cell with bit 32 SET (placeable: !is_cell_clear_of_bits(col,row,32)), writes col->*arg1, row->*arg2 and returns. CORRECTS prior note: it matches bit-32 SET (placeable), not clear; and *arg1=col / *arg2=row (prior had both backwards).
NesPrgRom:970A:is_coord_in_combat_rect:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns 1 iff (tile_x, tile_y) is inside the combat arena rect: combat_arena_x_min($6FF6) <= x <= combat_arena_x_max($6FFA) AND combat_arena_y_min($6FF8) <= y <= combat_arena_y_max($6FFC); else 0.
NesPrgRom:97F8:is_cur_unit_absent:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns is_unit_present(cur_combat_side, cur_combat_unit_slot) ? 0 : 1 — i.e. 1 when the current unit slot is ABSENT, 0 when present (the INVERSE of is_unit_present). Used as the loop-continuation guard to skip empty slots. (was 'test_cur_unit_slot_present' — returned the negation, so the name read backwards.)
NesPrgRom:9954:rng_search_combat_rect_for_unit_cell:[MED CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Randomized search over the combat rect (bounds $6FFA x $6FFC): two rng_mod(2) seeds bias the per-axis scan direction; switch on approach_dir zeroes one/both axis flips; inner loop tests cells via side_has_unit_at_cell, acting on the first hit. (Decompiled switch case values 65535+ are a DREAM signed/width artifact.)
NesPrgRom:9BB4:ai_terrain_strength_term:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI terrain bonus to combat strength: reads the unit's cell (read_map_cell at unit_col/unit_row) & 0xFE, maps terrain bit to a class via fall-through switch (32->0, 16->1, 8->2, else->3), then returns pct_op(unit_strength[side][slot], terrain_mult[$B9C2 + class*2]) * 3 — a terrain-typed strength contribution.
NesPrgRom:9C04:ai_province_stat_diff_term:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI strength term: over 3 province military stats (record $7013+side*26, +0/+2/+4 = morale/skill/arms), sums this side's POSITIVE advantage vs the enemy province (this.stat - enemy.stat, if >0) as pct_op(unit_strength[side][unit_field], diff/100); returns sum*3.
NesPrgRom:9DA8:reduce_defending_province_town_chaos:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] When a combatant stands on a bit-8 (town) cell — !(both units clear of bit 8) — shows msg_the_town_is_in_complete_chaos and reduces the defending province's town field ($7005 = battle_defending_province*26 + $7001+4): zeroes it if field <= arg1/2, else word_sub_saturating by a pct_op/math32-scaled amount; clear_rect_left_lower_alt. (bit 8 = town terrain.)
NesPrgRom:A01A:unit_type_count_gt3_and_equals_arg1:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Counts present unit slots on cur_combat_side (is_unit_present, slots 0..4); returns true iff count>3 (i.e. 4 or 5) AND (count-1)==arg1 — i.e. arg1 equals the highest occupied slot index when the side is near-full.
NesPrgRom:85A7:tactical_cursor_input_validate_redraw:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Per-frame tactical cursor input handler: polls input, validates the target cell for the phase (is_cell_valid_for_phase), and on phase-boundary input erases the cursor + advances the phase (erase_cursor_advance_phase), restoring the cursor with frame-timer waits. (Bank-2 $85A7; a different bank's $85A7 is effect_view_c.)
NesPrgRom:89DF:draw_unit_count_digits:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Renders a unit's troop count on the map: reads unit_col/unit_row (bail if off-map; erase cursor if !is_cell_valid_for_phase), calc_tactical_cell_coords, writes a war-state marker tile (test_6f65_bit7 ? 178 : 179) then the min_word(strength,9999) split to base-10 digits (+8 = digit-tile base, leading-zero suppression via local7) into the $6FE5 + side*9 buffer, then blits. arg1=side, arg2=slot.
NesPrgRom:8B25:draw_terrain_feature_if_valid:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Gates on is_cell_valid_for_phase(arg1); if valid, draws the tactical terrain feature via draw_tactical_terrain_feature(arg1,arg2). Thin guard wrapper.
NesPrgRom:912B:paged_flee_fief_list_display:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Displays the 0xFF-terminated fief list at $6F4F (built by build_daimyo_province_list) in 3 columns under a "Fief:" header (msg $B5F6/$B601), each as "%2d" (fief+1); page-breaks every 6 entries with prompt_hit_any_key_return_button (B-button ==2 cancels -> returns 0). Empty-list 'no fief to flee to' path gives the 'flee' framing. Returns the entry count.
NesPrgRom:92CA:battle_init_defender:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Defender battle init: battle_defender_status_flag_6f66 = fief_is_daimyo_capital[def]<<7; SNAPSHOTS the defending province's resources into war_defender_gold/rice/men from record def*26+$7001 at +0=gold / +6=rice($7007) / +16=men($7011), zero-clamping any field <=0 (rice-empty sets defender_depleted_flag=7); then distribute_men_into_unit_strengths ($91D5) + clear_all_unit_positions ($929C). Confirms the $7001 record offsets. (was 'battle_init_clear_defending_province_fields' — it loads war_defender_*, not just clears.)
NesPrgRom:94F6:announce_combat_side_daimyo_and_status:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Announces one combat side: branches on get_province_ai_state(get_battle_side_province(cur_combat_side)) and the opposing side (cur_combat_side^1); draws the daimyo name + a combat_message_table status string (index from arg1), then for the current unit uses is_unit_present to pick combat_message_table[5 vs 7] via draw_combat_message. message_display inside the side window.
NesPrgRom:9735:tile_blocked_for_placement:[MED CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Placement guard (only for cur_combat_side==0): returns 1 (blocked) if the cell is clear of bit 32 (not placeable) AND has bit 8 set, OR if (arg1,arg2) is one of the 6 hex-neighbors of find_free_tactical_placement_cell's result (steps each direction via tactical_hex_step and matches). CORRECTS prior note: it steps 6 DIRECTIONS from the free placement cell, NOT 'iterates 6 unit slots'. Sole caller commit_unit_dest_tile_if_valid ($9792). (was 'tile_blocked_by_existing_unit_in_placement'.)
NesPrgRom:9C88:ai_eval_battle_strength_total:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] THE per-unit battle-strength evaluator (sums every AI strength term): ai_sum_battle_strength() then base=unit_strength[side][unit_slot] + (test_6f65_bit7(side)?base:0 war bonus) + ai_terrain_strength_term + ai_province_stat_diff_term + ai_strength_term_gated_table_word + ai_score_strength_term_40pct + pct_op(base, byte[$7BEE+other_unit_slot]*20). Returns pct_op(base+total, mod) where mod = DIFFICULTY-scaled (115 - const_two*15) when the side is AI (=85 at default skill 2; 100/85/70/55/40 for skill 1..5), else 100. CORRECTS prior note ('30 or 100', 'pct_op(100,total)') — it's 115-skill*15 and the base scaled is base+total.
NesPrgRom:A148:find_flagged_present_unit_type:[MED CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Scans the 6-entry unit-type list at arg1 (byte each); returns the type code of the LAST entry that is valid (value<5) AND whose byte[$7BEE + value] > 0, else 255. ($7BEE = a per-unit-type byte that also scales a strength term *20% in $9CDC; its writer still to ground.)
NesPrgRom:A221:bfs_path_distance_to_target:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Tactical-grid BFS from the current unit (cur_unit_col/row) to target (arg1,arg2): returns 0 if already there; else inits an 11-wide dist_grid (blocked = 128 where read_map_cell & 194/0xC2 — the same blocking mask as is_map_cell_blocked), flood-fills via tactical_hex_step neighbor steps, and returns the path step-count when the target is reached.
NesPrgRom:A04E:is_unit_at_coords:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns 1 iff unit (side=arg3, slot=arg4) is_unit_present AND unit_col[arg3][arg4]==arg1(col) AND unit_row[arg3][arg4]==arg2(row); tests whether that specific present unit occupies tile (arg1,arg2). (Cf. side_has_unit_at_cell $8FC0 which scans all of a side's slots.)
NesPrgRom:AB8E:check_commander_alive_both_sides:[CONFIRMED 2026-06-02, was check_unit_type0_present_both_sides] Unit TYPE 0 IS THE COMMANDER. Tests presence on side0 then side1; returns 0 if both commanders alive, else OUTCOME CODE 5 (commander killed) after setting battle_winner_province_sel to the side that still has its commander. Called after every unit action in ai_run_all_units_combat_actions -> propagates up to dispatch_battle_resolution(5) = 'the command unit has been destroyed!'. Losing the type-0 unit ends the battle.
NesPrgRom:9B4A:validate_phase_unit_cells_draw_cursor:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Plays an audio cue (call_bank10_entry(wrap(cur_slot)+31)); reads enemy unit arg1's cell (cur_combat_side^1), advances the phase if its column isn't valid (erase_cursor_advance_phase), then blinks the tactical cursor between the current unit's tile and the enemy unit's tile (set_tactical_cursor_pos + draw_tactical_cursor_region 1/0). The attack-targeting visual.
NesPrgRom:AB37:redraw_combat_side_window:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] message_display(mem_B4F8); then ONLY for unit slot 0 (cur_combat_unit_slot==0) redraws combat_message_table[ test_6f65_bit7(cur_combat_side) ? 18 : 19 ] (war-state-dependent side header); always clear_rect_left_lower_alt. CORRECTS prior note: the slot-0 case selects the string (not 'clear if set'); the index 18/19 keys on the war bit-7, not a frame-local flag.
NesPrgRom:8623:poll_cursor_input_until_button:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] set_tactical_cursor_pos(arg1,arg2), then blinks draw_tactical_cursor_region(1) and polls tactical_cursor_input_validate_redraw up to 100 iterations per phase until input registers; returns the code callers switch on. (Prior note's 'effect_view_c' was the wrong-bank name for $85A7.)
NesPrgRom:8B58:draw_unit_counts_in_valid_cells:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Nested loop over both sides x 5 slots: if the unit's column (unit_col_ptr) is_cell_valid_for_phase, calls draw_unit_count_digits($89DF) to render its troop-count tiles. A per-unit DRAW/refresh pass. (was 'draw_valid_unit_field_cells'.)
NesPrgRom:9058:place_unit_at_tile_if_free:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Validates (is_tile_in_bounds && !is_any_unit_at_tile && !is_map_cell_blocked); if all pass, restores terrain at the old pos (draw_terrain_feature_if_valid), writes (arg1,arg2) into cur_unit_col/row, redraws the troop count (draw_unit_count_digits), returns 1; else 0. The AI-movement commit (cf. commit_unit_dest_tile_if_valid for the player path).
NesPrgRom:9792:commit_unit_dest_tile_if_valid:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Validates a destination tile via 4 guards — !is_any_unit_at_tile && !is_map_cell_blocked && !tile_blocked_for_placement && is_coord_in_combat_rect — and on success writes unit_col/unit_row[cur_combat_side][cur_combat_unit_slot] = (arg1,arg2) and returns 1; else returns 0. (Prior note said 'returns 0' — it returns 1 on commit.)
NesPrgRom:AD38:display_morale_falling_message:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Displays "<daimyo> <our/enemy> morale is falling": if get_province_ai_state(battle_defending_province) -> defender's name + msg_our; elif get_province_ai_state(selected_province_idx) -> attacker's name + msg_enemy; each then redraw_window(msg_morale_is_falling) + clear_rect_left_lower_alt. Else no-op.
NesPrgRom:AE2C:transfer_owned_fiefs_and_announce_succession:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Post-battle conquest resolution: if test_6f65_bit7 of the (winner==defender) side and battle_winner_province_sel != 50, announce_daimyo_death(winner) and increment_ai_player_count if AI; then (unless is_no_province_selected) builds the 0xFF-terminated $6F89 fief list (bound scenario_fief_count) of the conquered lord's fiefs, reassigns each, and prints the 'passed from Lord %s to Lord %s' succession line (daimyo_name_table $77A8).
NesPrgRom:AF3B:dispatch_battle_resolution:[CORRECTED 2026-06-02, was battle_setup_select_province_phase — it's the battle AFTERMATH dispatcher, not setup] Called by battle_init_driver with an OUTCOME CODE: 3=day-31 timeout('your men are exhausted!'), 4=rice<=0('out of rice'), 5=commander(type-0) killed('command unit destroyed'), 6=annihilation(5 escalated when war_side_state_flag[0]&31==0, no units left). Does arg1+=1 when that flag is clear (escalates 5->6), then announce_battle_outcome_retreat_or_won(code) for both provinces (indexes the loser table battle_conclusion_msgs_loser[(code-1)*2] + observer table $B650), transfer_owned_fiefs_and_announce_succession, apply_conquest_outcome ($E03C: spoils-merge both sides' gold/rice/men into the conquered fief, -10..19% output pillage, ownership transfer). arg1==5 is the retreat/special path. find_record_9e3c(30) restores post-battle UI.
NesPrgRom:8669:combat_command_menu_input_loop:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Cursor combat-command menu loop at (3,10): polls poll_cursor_input_until_button(arg1,arg2) until A (confirm, code 0) or B (cancel, code 4); returns the selected command index, which the caller uses to index the $B9F8 command-dispatch table.
NesPrgRom:86F9:select_menu_entry_by_cursor:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Cursor-driven menu picker at (2,21): polls poll_cursor_input_until_button(arg1,arg2) until A (confirm) or B (cancel, sets code 6), returns the selected entry. Used by the move-direction prompt ($90A0) over the keypad-style msg_d_d ($B52F). (was 'select_entry_from_b52f_table_by_cursor'; $B52F is a string prompt, not a lookup table.)
NesPrgRom:97D9:commit_unit_move_and_redraw_count:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] commit_unit_dest_tile_if_valid(arg1,arg2); if it succeeds, ADVANCES cur_combat_unit_slot (++) and draw_unit_count_digits for that slot. Returns the commit result. (Prior note missed the slot advance — used in the placement loop to step to the next unit.)
NesPrgRom:98FE:seek_enemy_adjacent_cell_and_commit_move:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Scans the 6 hex-neighbor cells of (arg1,arg2) via tactical_hex_step for one occupied by an enemy unit (side_has_unit_at_cell, cur_combat_side^1); on finding an enemy-adjacent cell, commits the move there. AI melee-approach.
NesPrgRom:9A18:player_interactive_unit_move_loop:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Player positioning phase: loops the 5 unit slots (skipping empty via is_cur_unit_absent), prompts 'please position unit %d' (+ the lord name for slot 0), then runs a D-pad cursor loop bounded by the combat rect, validating via is_coord_in_combat_rect/is_cell_valid_for_phase and committing on the confirm button via commit_unit_dest_tile_if_valid; ends clear_rect_left_lower.
NesPrgRom:9D03:apply_pct_reduction_to_unit_strength:[CONFIRMED 2026-06-02] The combat KILL applier: reduces a $6FBC unit-slot strength (and the side's men total unit_record+4 -- which is MEN, not a damage-accum) by pct_op(arg3, *slot)=floor(arg3*strength/100), cut clamped to the field; clears the unit on reaching 0. Caller tally_unit_type_then_check_strength_parity_50 ($9DFB) splits 100% of the damage between the two engaged units by relative strength: local11 = calc_battle_strength_pct_one_side ($9D75) = math32_2arg(A,B)=100A/(A+B); defender loses local11%, attacker loses (100-local11)%. The actual troop-killing math (kills are decoupled from the rice clock $830B and the capture contest $9E73). Reverse-push arg order on the pct call -> confirm exact A/B in var-walk.
NesPrgRom:9D75:calc_battle_strength_pct_one_side:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns math32_2arg(A, B) = floor(100*A/(A+B)) where A = ai_eval_battle_strength_total(cur_combat_side, cur_combat_unit_slot, unit_type) and B = the mirror for the other side; a 0-100 strength-share %, thresholded at 50 by callers to decide which side is stronger.
NesPrgRom:9E73:resolve_attack_apply_casualties:[EMULATOR-CONFIRMED 2026-06-02, probe-combat-casualty.py] The combat attack as a CAPTURE/DEFECTION CONTEST. Body arg1=target enemy unit-slot (0-4), arg2=men committed (reverse-push display). atk_score = rng(6-skill) + morale(atk_prov,+18) + charisma(atk_daimyo,+4); def_score = morale(def_prov,+18) + charisma(def_daimyo,+4) + 2*skill. If atk_score>def_score, captured = pct_op(math32_2arg(atk_score, atk_score-def_score), enemy_slot_strength) men move from the enemy's slot to the attacker's slot 0 (cap recipient<=9999); if 0 or contest lost, enemy province morale -= skill instead. Charisma is the decisive combat stat (can dominate morale). Subsequent draws are UI; stub them to run headless.
NesPrgRom:A07A:find_adjacent_unit_around_tile:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns 1 if unit (side=arg3, slot=arg4) occupies any of the 6 hex-neighbor cells of tile (arg1,arg2): for dir 0..5, reset to (arg1,arg2), single-step via tactical_hex_step, test is_unit_at_coords; early-return on match, else 0.
NesPrgRom:A0F3:build_reachable_enemy_target_list:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI adjacency targeting: for each of the 6 hex directions from (unit_x,unit_y), inits out_buf[dir]=0xFF, steps ONE cell via tactical_hex_step(&x,&y,dir), then scans the 5 enemy slots (cur_combat_side^1) with is_unit_at_coords; records the enemy unit index of one occupying that adjacent cell into out_buf[dir]. Builds the 6-entry reachable-target list (out_buf=arg3).
NesPrgRom:A3BD:ai_step_unit_toward_target:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI one-step pathfind-and-move: bfs_path_distance_to_target(unit_x,unit_y); if dist>0, reads cur_unit_col/row, steps one tile closer via tactical_hex_step, then commits with place_unit_at_tile_if_free; returns 1 on a successful step, else 0.
NesPrgRom:AAA7:combat_flee_to_fief_command:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Player FLEE combat command (cur_combat_unit_slot==0 path): prompt_yes_no, load_daimyo_relation_row(defender), build_daimyo_province_list(source_fief) -> paged_flee_fief_list_display -> prompt_select_province_from_list (dest != 255); confirms, then relocates to the chosen fief. Ties together $90BB/$912B/$91A1 — confirms the 'flee' framing of paged_flee_fief_list_display.
NesPrgRom:AB6A:prompt_hit_any_key_and_redraw_combat_screen:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] draw_combat_roster_window, 'Hit any key' prompt at row 26, wait_button_edge, reset_prompt_selection, then render_combat_map_screen + draw_unit_counts_in_valid_cells; returns 1. (Prior note said 'returns 0'.)
NesPrgRom:AD86:halve_defender_morale_for_breaching_attackers:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] For each ATTACKER unit (is_unit_present(side 0, slot 0..4)) standing ON a placeable cell (bit 32 set: !is_cell_clear_of_bits(unit_col,unit_row,32)), halves the DEFENDER's morale ($7013 + battle_defending_province*26, = the $7001 record's +18 morale field) and shows display_morale_falling_message. CORRECTS prior note: the loop is over ATTACKER (side-0) units, not the defending province's; the cell test is ON-bit-32 (placeable/breach), not 'NOT on a blocked cell'. (was 'halve_defender_province_stat_for_exposed_units'.)
NesPrgRom:90A0:prompt_unit_move_direction_at_tile:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Draws the move-direction menu (msg_up_up_rt_down_rt_down_down_lt) and runs select_menu_entry_by_cursor seeded at the current unit's tile (cur_unit_col/row), returning the chosen direction code (caller compares to $30).
NesPrgRom:9810:ai_place_unit_in_free_slot_resolve_coords:[MED CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI placement loop (for slot_idx 0..5, while cur_combat_unit_slot < max_slots(arg1)): skips absent units (is_cur_unit_absent -> ++slot), else steps from own unit-0 in direction slot_idx (tactical_hex_step) and commit_unit_move_and_redraw_count there. Spreads the side's units out across the placement zone.
NesPrgRom:9D9A:ai_battle_strength_ratio_below_50:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns calc_battle_strength_pct_one_side(unit_type) < 50 — true when this side holds less than half the combined battle strength (outmatched). Thin AI predicate.
NesPrgRom:9E20:resolve_attack_apply_mutual_casualties:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Core melee resolution vs enemy unit arg1: targeting blink (validate_phase_unit_cells_draw_cursor), increments the $7BEE[arg1] attack counter, computes pct = calc_battle_strength_pct_one_side(arg1) (own win-%), then APPLIES CASUALTIES to both sides — apply_pct_reduction_to_unit_strength(own, 100-pct) + apply_pct_reduction_to_unit_strength(enemy, pct) — and feeds the loss total to reduce_defending_province_town_chaos. Returns 0 if pct==50 (parity), 1 if pct>50 (own won), 2 if pct<50 (own lost). (Prior note missed the casualty application; was 'tally_unit_type_then_check_strength_parity_50'.)
NesPrgRom:A0AD:is_enemy_unit_adjacent:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Returns is_unit_present(cur_combat_side^1, arg1) && find_adjacent_unit_around_tile(cur_unit_col, cur_unit_row, enemy, arg1) — true when enemy unit slot arg1 is present AND in one of the 6 hex-neighbors of the current unit. CORRECTS prior note: it checks ADJACENCY (6 neighbors), not 'occupies the current unit's tile'. (was 'enemy_unit_type_present_at_unit_tile'.)
NesPrgRom:A194:ai_place_units_near_enemy_loop:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI placement driver: for each of the 6 hex directions from the current unit, steps via tactical_hex_step and build_reachable_enemy_target_list to find adjacent enemies, then places the unit on a free tile (place_unit_at_tile_if_free) near an enemy.
NesPrgRom:A4BC:find_strongest_unit_type_by_strength:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Scans the 6-entry list arg1[] (valid <5), ranks each by calc_battle_strength_pct_one_side (win-% vs enemy), tracks the argmax; returns 255 if the best %% is below the threshold arg2, else the winning unit-type byte. (Prior note missed the arg2 threshold + that the metric is the strength-RATIO.)
NesPrgRom:9865:ai_advance_units_when_attacker_stronger:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI advance: place the first unit on a free placement cell (find_free_tactical_placement_cell + commit_unit_move_and_redraw_count); if ai_attacker_outstrengths_defender, spread the rest (ai_place_unit_in_free_slot_resolve_coords(5)) and step each present unit (is_cur_unit_absent gate) one cell toward the enemy via tactical_hex_step + place.
NesPrgRom:A0DA:eval_and_announce_battle_strength_parity_if_enemy_present:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] If enemy unit arg1 is_enemy_unit_adjacent, resolves the attack (resolve_attack_apply_mutual_casualties $9E20 -> 0/1/2 outcome) and announces it via announce_combat_side_daimyo_and_status; else returns immediately. The attack-and-announce wrapper.
NesPrgRom:A4FC:min_own_strength_pct_vs_list:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Loops the 6-entry unit-type list arg1[] (valid <5), computes calc_battle_strength_pct_one_side for each, and keeps the MINIMUM (accumulator starts at 100, takes the smaller) — the own win-% in the WORST matchup. REFUTES old name+note ('keeps the max, peak strength pct') — it's a MIN, ceiling 100. (was 'max_enemy_unit_type_strength_pct'.)
NesPrgRom:A721:ai_rng_resolve_combat_apply_casualties:[MED CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI combat resolver, gated by rng_mod(const_two+1) (difficulty-scaled: skill+1, not a hardcoded 3); after province-selected / enemy-AI-state / slot-0 / strength guards, scans the 5 enemy slots for the strongest present unit (is_unit_present + unit_strength_ptr), then resolve_attack_apply_casualties ($9E73). (Deeper branch logic only partially decoded.)
NesPrgRom:A7E5:ai_own_double_lt_enemy_total:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Sums the strengths of present enemy units adjacent to own unit-0 (build_reachable_enemy_target_list + is_unit_present + unit_strength_ptr), and returns (unit_strength[cur][0] << 1) < enemy_total — TRUE when own doubled strength is OUTMATCHED by the adjacent enemy total. REFUTES old name+note ('>= enemy_total, own >= enemy/2') — the comparison is LESS-THAN, the opposite. (was 'ai_test_own_double_ge_enemy_total_strength'.)
NesPrgRom:A90E:player_move_unit_until_placed_loop:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Interactive move loop: prompt_unit_move_direction_at_tile, exit on dir-code 48 (cancel); else validate_dir_code_and_dispatch steps the coord, and if is_tile_in_bounds && place_unit_at_tile_if_free succeeds, returns; else re-prompts.
NesPrgRom:A96C:player_move_unit_with_occupancy_check_loop:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Interactive move loop with attack: prompt_unit_move_direction_at_tile (exit on 48), validate_dir_code_and_dispatch + is_tile_in_bounds; if the target tile is occupied by an enemy, resolve_attack_apply_mutual_casualties ($9E20) + announce_combat_side_daimyo_and_status; else move. The player melee path.
NesPrgRom:AC7F:combat_command_dispatch_loop_per_unit:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Per-unit combat command loop: iterates units (cur_combat_unit_slot 0..<5), gates each by is_unit_present, draws the command menu (combat_command_menu_str_ptrs), reads a command via combat_command_menu_input_loop, then dispatches through the $B9F8 jump table at (cmd<<1); command index 3 is the terminator and check_unit_type0_present_both_sides ($AB8E) tests continuation.
NesPrgRom:99D2:ai_place_combat_units_random_or_smart:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Battle-init AI unit placer: if cur_combat_side -> smart advance (ai_advance_units_when_attacker_stronger); else random (rng_search_combat_rect_for_unit_cell). Then for each present slot (is_cur_unit_absent gate), commits a random cell commit_unit_move_and_redraw_count(rng_mod(11), rng_mod(5)).
NesPrgRom:A1EF:ai_engage_present_enemy_if_favorable:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] If is_enemy_unit_adjacent(unit_idx): bails (return 0) only when the matchup is weak (ai_battle_strength_ratio_below_50) AND the side is still supplied (side_has_rice_for_day); otherwise engages via eval_and_announce_battle_strength_parity_if_enemy_present and returns 1. No adjacent enemy -> 0. (Prior note's 'always returns 0' is wrong.)
NesPrgRom:A3F8:ai_select_weak_reachable_enemy_target:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI target picker (slot>0): build_reachable_enemy_target_list from own unit-0, then drops (sets 0xFF) any entry that is NOT is_enemy_unit_adjacent, keeping only adjacent enemies; prefers a type where our strength ratio is favorable (enemy weak), and commits the choice.
NesPrgRom:A52F:ai_decide_unit_action_attack_or_advance:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] The per-unit AI tactical brain: threshold = (unit_type_count_gt3_and_equals_arg1 || side 0) ? 0 : 50; picks a target via find_flagged_present_unit_type, else find_strongest_unit_type_by_strength(list, threshold). If target<5 -> ATTACK (eval_and_announce...). Else if an ally is adjacent (find_adjacent_unit_around_tile) -> 1; else if min_own_strength_pct_vs_list > threshold -> ADVANCE (ai_place_units_near_enemy_loop). Integrates the whole batch-8..13 AI-strength stack.
NesPrgRom:A84D:ai_claim_province_when_strong_enough:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI auto-conquest: gated on slot 0 + war bit7 + a selected province, and on (NOT ai_own_double_lt_enemy_total AND side_has_rice_for_day) — i.e. strong enough and supplied. Then builds the lord's fief list, sets battle_winner_province_sel, end_war_relocate_capital, and SETS the conquered owner's province_ai_state = 5. REFUTES old note ('clears province_ai_state to 0', 'own*2>=enemy') — it SETS state 5 and the strength gate is NOT-outmatched. (was 'ai_clear_province_state_when_strong_enough'.)
NesPrgRom:A9FB:combat_command_select_target_resolve_attack:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Player ATTACK command (slot-0 path; AI/resume path branches on is_no_province_selected || ai_turn_planner_resume_flag): prompt_province_selection(1,5) picks the enemy target unit (1-based), gated by is_unit_present on the enemy side, then resolve_attack_apply_casualties ($9E73) + message_display. Reuses prompt_province_selection for unit targeting.
NesPrgRom:9B08:deploy_both_sides_units_loop:[ORACLE-CONFIRMED 2026-06-02, renamed from resolve_combat_damage_both_sides_loop] The setup-time UNIT DEPLOYMENT loop (run ONCE by battle_init_driver $AFE1, NOT per day): for each of the 2 sides, set_combat_arena_rect_by_approach ($9675) computes the entry-edge code, then AI sides place units via ai_place_combat_units_random_or_smart(code) and the player side via player_interactive_unit_move_loop. No damage here -- the old name was a misnomer inherited from the stale combat-damage memory.
NesPrgRom:A5A4:ai_advance_units_toward_reachable_enemies:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] If ai_select_weak_reachable_enemy_target hits, return it; else build_reachable_enemy_target_list from own unit-0 and, for each reachable enemy (<5), ai_step_unit_toward_target one cell closer; returns on the first successful step.
NesPrgRom:A625:ai_advance_units_into_free_adjacent_cells:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] If ai_select_weak_reachable_enemy_target hits, return it; else probe the 6 hex-neighbors of the current unit (is_tile_in_bounds / is_any_unit_at_tile / is_map_cell_blocked) for a free cell and advance the unit into it. The fallback when no reachable enemy to step toward.
NesPrgRom:A6C5:ai_choose_combat_action_by_battle_strength:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] AI action by strength: pct = min_own_strength_pct_vs_list(reachable enemies); if pct<20 OR own unit-0 strength<=1 -> ai_place_units_near_enemy_loop (desperate huddle). Else find_strongest_unit_type_by_strength(list, 70): if a target <5 -> attack (eval_and_announce...); else (player side / unit_type>5) fall through to ai_advance_units_into_free_adjacent_cells.
NesPrgRom:A8CF:ai_select_unit_combat_action:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Per-unit AI action selector: if ai_claim_province_when_strong_enough(fief) -> return 1; else ai_rng_resolve_combat_apply_casualties, then dispatch by state — slot 0 -> ai_choose_combat_action_by_battle_strength; else (attacker side AND ai_attacker_outstrengths_defender AND not unit_type_count_gt3) -> ai_advance_units_toward_reachable_enemies; else ai_advance_units_into_free_adjacent_cells.
NesPrgRom:ABB7:ai_run_all_units_combat_actions:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] One side's combat turn: loops the 5 unit slots (is_unit_present gate), refreshes the unit window, and per present unit invokes ai_select_unit_combat_action; returns the resolved/continue flag via check_unit_type0_present_both_sides ($AB8E).
NesPrgRom:ADD1:run_both_sides_combat_turn:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] One combat day (called by the resolution path): halve_defender_morale_for_breaching_attackers, then for each side (cur_combat_side 0,1) clears the 5 per-type counters ($7BEE+0..4), skips sides that are battleside_not_state5_or_resting, and runs the per-side AI/player handler ai_run_all_units_combat_actions; early-exits when it signals combat resolved.
NesPrgRom:B591:roster_fmt_4d_1:[ROM-STR] "%4d" (draw_unit_roster_columns, 1st column)
NesPrgRom:B595:roster_dashes_1:[ROM-STR] "----" (draw_unit_roster_columns; the tables lane read it as binary)
NesPrgRom:B59A:roster_fmt_4d_2:[ROM-STR] "%4d" (draw_unit_roster_columns, 2nd column)
NesPrgRom:B59E:roster_fmt_4d_3:[ROM-STR] "%4d" (draw_unit_roster_columns, 3rd column)
NesPrgRom:B5A2:roster_dashes_2:[ROM-STR] "----" (draw_unit_roster_columns; the tables lane read it as binary)
NesPrgRom:8003:tactical_hex_step:[HIGH CONFIRMED] NATIVE 6502 (bank 2, $8003-$8085), called from bytecode via CALL_abs_imm1 {native}. tactical_hex_step(&x, &y, dir): one step on the 11x5 offset-column hex grid of the tactical map (x 0..10, y 0..4). dir 1 = y+1, 4 = y-1; 0/2/3/5 = x-1/x+1/x-1/x+1, then y moves or not by the parity of the new x (down-left, down-right, up-left, up-right). Returns 1 if the step stays on the map, 0 at an edge; a diagonal can move x and then fail on y, leaving x changed. Caller validate_dir_code_and_dispatch maps keypad '1','2','3','7','8','9' to dir 0-5.
NesPrgRom:8000:bank2_entry:[HIGH 2026-10-28] Bank 2 entry point: 3 bytes, JMP $AFE1 (battle_init_driver), the target call_bank_wrap(2) reaches. Read from the ROM bytes; labelled like bank0_entry.
NesPrgRom:28003:play_audio_by_id:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Bank-10 audio entry (body of call_bank10_entry). Gated on audio_wait_gate==1. Dispatches on sound_request_id ($7FE5): >64 = no-op; <27 = song (load 3 voices from the $8617 table at id*3, audio_control(1..3,1)); 27-63 = single SFX voice (load 1 from $8617[id], channel = byte&4). The sound/music trigger bytecode requests via call_bank10_entry.
NesPrgRom:28617:play_audio_by_id_stream_ptrs:[ROM-DATA] word pointer table read by play_audio_by_id ($8090, $80D9, $8110, ...): the audio streams in bank 10
NesPrgRom:28000:bank10_entry:[HIGH 2026-10-28] Bank 10 entry point: 3 bytes, JMP $8003 (play_audio_by_id), the target call_bank_wrap(10) reaches. Read from the ROM bytes; labelled like bank0_entry.
NesPrgRom:38003:busy_wait_delay:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Busy-wait: arg1 outer iterations x ~50 inner (nested decrement loops). The cutscene engine's timing-delay primitive. Renamed 2026-10-28 (was cutscene_delay) to the family's reviewed name (emu-harness vocabulary.toml; match family: identical code in 3 titles): generic code that sits in the cutscene bank.
NesPrgRom:3801D:draw_sprite_grid:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] Renders a rectangular block of OAM sprites: reads tile/attr data from SRAM (syscall16_sram_wrap), then loops rows x cols calling syscall_set_sprite stepping 8px per col/row from base (arg2,arg3), advancing the OAM index; ends with wait_for_nmi. The cutscene engine's multi-sprite blit primitive.
NesPrgRom:380AD:run_cutscene:[HIGH CONFIRMED 2026-06-10] The AI-turn cutscene SCRIPT INTERPRETER. Reads a 5-byte descriptor at cutscene_id*5 + cutscene_table ($AF80), loads its palette (32 entries) + CHR (ppu_upload_block), then runs a command stream via a big switch: set/move position, draw_sprite_grid, cutscene_delay, loop (counter at fp-39), clear-all-sprites, play audio via call_bank10_entry, and end. Driven by trigger_cutscene ($E80C).
NesPrgRom:3AF80:cutscene_table:[MED 2026-06-10] Bank-14 cutscene descriptor table: 5 bytes/entry indexed by cutscene_id ($7FCB). Per entry: SRAM source bank + data pointers (palette/CHR/script). Read by run_cutscene ($80AD).
NesPrgRom:38000:bank14_entry:[HIGH 2026-10-28] Bank 14 entry point: 3 bytes, JMP $80AD (run_cutscene), the target call_bank_wrap(14) reaches. Read from the ROM bytes; labelled like bank0_entry.
NesPrgRom:1257E:tactical_map_cell_pool:Per-fief tactical-map cell data, ~33+ maps of 55 bytes each. The live per-cell metatile source map_populate ($8903) reads one byte at a time, indexed as $A57E + province_to_mapid_table[province]*55. NOT a directly-renderable flat table (that older interpretation, in render-atlas.py, was the disproven dead-end) — correct path is to RUN $8903, not read this flat. Session 2026-05-30.
NesPrgRom:22604:portrait_feature0_head_tiles:[HIGH VISUAL] Portrait feature 0 (head/hair/forehead): 5 variants x 12 tiles (192-byte stride $C0), 2bpp. block = $A604 + digit*192 -> CHR $17F0. Top 2 rows of the 6x6 face.
NesPrgRom:229C4:portrait_feature1_eyes_tiles:[HIGH VISUAL] Portrait feature 1 (eyes): 5 variants x 6 tiles (96-byte stride), 2bpp. block = $A9C4 + digit*96 -> CHR $18B0. Row 3 of the face (visibly distinct eyes per variant).
NesPrgRom:22BA4:portrait_feature2_nose_tiles:[HIGH VISUAL] Portrait feature 2 (nose/mid-face): 5 variants x 6 tiles (96-byte stride), 2bpp. block = $ABA4 + digit*96 -> CHR $1910. Row 4 of the face.
NesPrgRom:22D84:portrait_feature3_mouth_tiles:[HIGH VISUAL] Portrait feature 3 (mouth/chin/collar): 5 variants x 12 tiles (192-byte stride $C0), 2bpp. block = $AD84 + digit*192 -> CHR $1970. Bottom 2 rows of the face.
